    thinking: "**Analyzing Firebase Context**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the specific Firebase details provided. I\'m taking inventory of the project name, database location, enabled authentication method, and storage configuration. These details are helping me establish a solid foundation for understanding the environment. I need to make sure I understand the scope of the project based on this information, and any implicit details the user may have in mind.\n\n\n**Reviewing Firebase Access**\n\nI\'ve just recognized a critical server access pattern: firebase-admin is initialized using applicationDefault() and the project ID sourced from environment variables, avoiding any service account JSON files. Crucially, I\'m documenting the server-side environment variables: GEMINI_API_KEY, FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID (cnc-copilot-abc26), STORAGE_BUCKET, and ADMIN_EMAILS (biju0716@gmail.com). I also need to make a .env.example file. This is great, as I can start checking the important steps in the skill instructions. I\'m focusing on the first instruction to call `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"firebase_setup\"` to initiate the user interaction.\n\n\n**Defining Firebase Provisioning**\n\nI\'m now completely clear on the subsequent steps. Once the user accepts the terms, I must call `rpc_action` to provision the database. The `service_name` will be \"fax\", the `method_name` \"ProvisionFirebase\", and arguments are: `platform`: \"web\", `project_id`: \"cnc-copilot-abc26\", `firestore_region`: \"asia-south1\", and `database_id`: \"(default)\". Importantly, I need to compare `set_up_firebase` and `show_aistudio_ui` now to make sure I don\'t take any unexpected routes. I remember `set_up_firebase` is critical to call when the user has not accepted terms yet!\n\n\n**Clarifying UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction flow. My focus is on the crucial immediate stop after calling `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"firebase_setup\"`. I must wait for the user\'s response, especially confirmation or decline. I need to make sure I don\'t initiate additional actions prematurely. I\'m clarifying whether `show_aistudio_ui` and `set_up_firebase` can be called under specific conditions. I will be checking parameters.\n\n\n**Examining Skill Interactions**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `show_aistudio_ui` arguments, noting `ui_type: \"firebase_setup\"` and `arguments: {}`. I\'ve confirmed that `set_up_firebase` is a tool, but I must follow the instructions. I must wait for user response after calling `show_aistudio_ui`. I\'m also reviewing `metadata.json` for app name and description, currently a placeholder, with the real app name as \"CNC Copilot\". I\'ll integrate the new tagline into the description: \"AI explains. Physics decides. High-precision CNC shopfloor copilot with physics-based cutting calculations, G-code verification.\" I\'ll need to check the html file as well.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
