  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Deployment Success**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the Firestore rules deployed without a hitch! Now, I\'m shifting my focus to the requirements for Milestone 1. I\'m taking a close look at the project structure, design system, navigation, Firebase Auth sign-in implementation, and the components for the landing page, dashboard, and server setup with token middleware. I\'m keen on getting this milestone locked down.\n\n\n**Defining Milestone 1 Scope**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into Milestone 1 specifications. I\'m carefully reviewing the requirements for the server entry point (Node.js, Express, TypeScript) and the configuration file setup. I\'m also ensuring a good understanding of environment variables and their usage, focusing on Firebase admin access and security considerations, especially regarding the GEMINI_API_KEY. I\'m setting up the groundwork for the API health check and the rate limiter.\n\n\n**Implementing API Security Measures**\n\nI\'m currently working to establish the API security framework. I\'ll pass the Firebase ID token in the \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" format for every /api call. I will utilize Express middleware for verification, attaching relevant user data. GET /api/health will remain public. I\'m focusing on the rate limiting: each AI endpoint call will increment Firestore usage counts. Once a daily limit is reached, an HTTP 429 error and an informative message will be displayed to the user. Admins will bypass the limit.\nI\'m establishing the logging format for AI requests now. I plan to log route information, hashed user ID, controller, language, called tools, citation count, latency, model, token counts, but never any sensitive data. For Gemini calls, I\'m setting a 25-second timeout, with a retry mechanism for specific error codes, and a user-friendly error message. Lastly, I\'m defining the structure of the users/{uid} document in Firestore.\n\n\n**Defining User Document Schema**\n\nI\'m solidifying the structure of the `users/{uid}` document in Firestore. I am setting up the initial fields: `createdAt` (server-created on sign-in) and `role` (assigned as \"admin\" if the email is in the `ADMIN_EMAILS` list, otherwise \"user\"). Importantly, I am making sure the client cannot write the `role` field. I am confident in this approach.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Specifying Design System Details**\nI am now finalizing the design system specifications. I\'m focusing on the dark industrial theme, including the background color, noise overlay, and color palette. I\'ve chosen Inter and JetBrains Mono for fonts, covering UI text and technical values respectively. I\'m setting up panel styles with rounded corners, background, border, hover effects, and transitions. Accessibility is also key. I am making sure WCAG AA contrast, aria-labels for icon buttons, visible focus rings, and minimum touch targets for gloved hands. I\'m ensuring a responsive design, stacking multi-column screens vertically on small screens.\n\n\n**Mapping UI Componentry**\n\nI\'m currently mapping out the UI components across both desktop and mobile views. I\'ve designed the top bar for desktop, incorporating the \"CNC Copilot\" logo, spindle icon, navigation links, language selector, and avatar menu. I also have the mobile layout for navigation which will use a bottom tab bar. I am planning for consistent loading skeletons, error states, and empty states. I\'m prioritizing the structure and features for the \"/\" route, ensuring both signed-in and signed-out experiences are user-friendly and informative.\n\n\n**Designing Operator Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the operator dashboard layout for signed-in users. I\'m incorporating a dynamic greeting with time-based good morning/afternoon/evening and a live date display with shift information. I\'m adding a resume banner for recent chats and quick action cards for key tasks like diagnosis, calculations, G-code verification, and Crash Lab. I\'m also visualizing recent activity with resume links.\n\n\n**Structuring Server-Side Logic**\n\nI am now focusing on the server architecture. I\'m verifying how Express integrates with Vite during development and production. I\'ve updated the `package.json` scripts to run the server with TypeScript. I\'m also planning out the `/server` directory, defining `/server/config.ts` and `/server/firebase.ts` for initialization.\n\n\n**Defining Server-Side Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the server components. I\'ve defined `/server/authMiddleware.ts` to verify tokens and fetch user data, plus `/server/rateLimiter.ts` for daily checks. I\'m finalizing `/server/logger.ts` for hashed user IDs and `routes/` for health and user endpoints. I\'m also preparing for the Express and Vite integration and the Gemini API model selection.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_896758"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\ndotenv.config();\\n\\nexport const MODEL_FLASH = \'gemini-2.5-flash\';\\nexport const MODEL_PRO = \'gemini-2.5-pro\';\\nexport const MODEL_TTS = \'gemini-2.5-flash\';\\n\\nexport const FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID = process.env.FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID || \'cnc-copilot-abc26\';\\nexport const STORAGE_BUCKET = process.env.STORAGE_BUCKET || `${FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID}.firebasestorage.app`;\\nexport const ADMIN_EMAILS = (process.env.ADMIN_EMAILS || \'biju0716@gmail.com\')\\n  .split(\',\')\\n  .map(e => e.trim().toLowerCase())\\n  .filter(Boolean);\\n\\nexport const GEMINI_API_KEY = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY || \'\';\\nexport const PORT = parseInt(process.env.PORT || \'3000\', 10);\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create /server/config.ts with model and environment constants\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/server/config.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating /server/config.ts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create server config\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
