  planner_response {
    response: "### Identified Issues & Fixes Applied\n\n1. **`auth/popup-closed-by-user` Uncaught Exception**:\n   - **Root Cause**: When a user closed or dismissed the Google OAuth popup window before authenticating, Firebase threw `auth/popup-closed-by-user`, which was uncaught and bubbled up as an application error.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `src/context/AuthContext.tsx` to handle `auth/popup-closed-by-user` and `auth/cancelled-popup-request` gracefully as standard user cancellations without logging or raising an unhandled exception.\n\n2. **`7 PERMISSION_DENIED: Missing or insufficient permissions` on Firestore**:\n   - **Root Cause**: \n     1. The server was connecting to the default Firestore database instead of the provisioned database ID (`ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598`).\n     2. In `firestore.rules`, `users/{uid}` had `allow create: if false`, which prevented client-side profile creation on first sign-in while the server environment lacked cross-project IAM write permissions.\n     3. `/server/authMiddleware.ts` and `/server/routes/user.ts` threw errors when server-side Firestore operations failed.\n   - **Fixes**:\n     1. Updated `server/firebase.ts` to explicitly pass the database ID `ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598` to `getFirestore()`.\n     2. Updated `firestore.rules` so the authenticated owner can create their initial `users/{uid}` document (`allow create: if isOwner(uid) && (!(\'role\' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.role == \'user\')`), while strictly blocking any client mutation of the `role` field on update. Deployed the updated rules to Firebase.\n     3. Updated `server/authMiddleware.ts` to deterministically determine the user\'s role (`admin` or `user`) from the verified token email against `ADMIN_EMAILS`, making the middleware completely resilient and eliminating PERMISSION_DENIED warnings.\n     4. Added an in-memory fallback to `server/rateLimiter.ts` to guarantee seamless 100 requests/day tracking even during transient Firestore access hiccups."
    modified_response: "### Identified Issues & Fixes Applied\n\n1. **`auth/popup-closed-by-user` Uncaught Exception**:\n   - **Root Cause**: When a user closed or dismissed the Google OAuth popup window before authenticating, Firebase threw `auth/popup-closed-by-user`, which was uncaught and bubbled up as an application error.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `src/context/AuthContext.tsx` to handle `auth/popup-closed-by-user` and `auth/cancelled-popup-request` gracefully as standard user cancellations without logging or raising an unhandled exception.\n\n2. **`7 PERMISSION_DENIED: Missing or insufficient permissions` on Firestore**:\n   - **Root Cause**: \n     1. The server was connecting to the default Firestore database instead of the provisioned database ID (`ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598`).\n     2. In `firestore.rules`, `users/{uid}` had `allow create: if false`, which prevented client-side profile creation on first sign-in while the server environment lacked cross-project IAM write permissions.\n     3. `/server/authMiddleware.ts` and `/server/routes/user.ts` threw errors when server-side Firestore operations failed.\n   - **Fixes**:\n     1. Updated `server/firebase.ts` to explicitly pass the database ID `ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598` to `getFirestore()`.\n     2. Updated `firestore.rules` so the authenticated owner can create their initial `users/{uid}` document (`allow create: if isOwner(uid) && (!(\'role\' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.role == \'user\')`), while strictly blocking any client mutation of the `role` field on update. Deployed the updated rules to Firebase.\n     3. Updated `server/authMiddleware.ts` to deterministically determine the user\'s role (`admin` or `user`) from the verified token email against `ADMIN_EMAILS`, making the middleware completely resilient and eliminating PERMISSION_DENIED warnings.\n     4. Added an in-memory fallback to `server/rateLimiter.ts` to guarantee seamless 100 requests/day tracking even during transient Firestore access hiccups."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\376\001\n\373\001\001i\024}\023\031\036\354\222r\217hi\255\225\302z\373\250\346y\035z&<R\246\322e\343\305\331\321e\027\216/C\255\002<k\034\330\006R\264\375\237\354\212\021\357\236\236\343\256o\020[/b@\341(j\275\277f\000\\G\352Q\206}\363\351W\2120(g\3204\n\021\220\210\f\3428\314\377P\232ht\f\264\f\343\265\210\216Ic\f\016\370\243\v6a_h\243#o\241-\345\200j\215\253p\023}\345\304\n\370\336\315\025\343~\352\002`A\264 v\235k\307\024f<C:\241 \247\016\233\374\036K\220s\332%;Y{\203\342\000]DJf<\265\300e\235f\v\334&I\022qR\371]\242\274\023&\t\225\257\240\206\b\2734\031.\3666\'\334\215\270\354=\240\223zK#\224\330O\224K\376\357\2140VV\341_\025\326\265\203:\r\n\263\016*\247\'\321\030\275\204+\377\320-\247"
