    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Documents**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the design documentation. Specifically, I am thoroughly examining the provided `DESIGN.md` and `operator_dashboard/code.html` to establish the definitive visual design. My objective is to meticulously replicate the layout grid, section order, and card structure from the HTML source in the signed-in Operator Dashboard.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual details. I\'ve noted the colored top borders for the quick-action cards and the shift to Material Symbols Outlined icons. I\'m focusing on the M3 color tokens defined in the Tailwind configuration for the visual design. Furthermore, I\'ll be implementing 12px card sizing, 8px controls, and 4px square badges. JetBrains Mono is the choice for numbers and labels, with a glow effect for active elements. I am migrating all color tokens into tailwind.config. I am replacing lucide icons.\n\nI am also formulating the data rules. An alert banner will appear for recent chats with alarm codes. A greeting block will display a user\'s name, the time, shift, and preferred controller. Four stat chips will appear, as well.\n\n\n**Updating Data Visualizations**\n\nI am now focusing on data representation within the dashboard. I plan to incorporate \"Questions today,\" \"Calculations today,\" and \"Programs verified today\" alongside Crash Lab data. I\'ve decided to maintain the style of the quick action cards as found in the HTML. I\'ll replace the existing telemetry chart with a \"Copilot Activity, last 7 days\" chart showcasing daily activity from users. I\'m also planning to replace the existing \"Chamber Enclosure CAM\" section with a dynamically updated screen snapshot, extracted alarm information, and appropriate empty state messaging. I will include recent activity and shop logs, along with pinned manuals, and shop standards.\n\n\n**Defining UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on the final UI components. The top navigation bar is my next target, mirroring the HTML design, but excluding the shop status and including the controller selector and language selector. The footer will be updated with the \"CNC Copilot\" branding and app version information. I will verify that the Material Symbols Outlined font is linked in `index.html`. Furthermore, I am implementing Tailwind and checking for the correct setup.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Variables**\n\nI\'m now integrating the exact color values extracted from `operator_dashboard/code.html` into `src/index.css` using `@theme`. I\'ll be defining classes like `bg-surface` for direct use within the application. These precise values will ensure visual consistency across the dashboard.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1639900"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/index.html\",\"toolAction\":\"Checking index.html\",\"toolSummary\":\"View index.html for fonts and Material Symbols\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
