  planner_response {
    response: "### Milestone 2 Complete: Deterministic Cutting Engine, 3D Tool Contact Simulation, Cutting Calculator, and Copilot Explain API\n\nThe Cutting Calculator screen has been built to match the attached Stitch HTML design (`cutting-calculator/code.html`) and `DESIGN.md`. All calculations are derived from Kienzle specific cutting force formulas with physical limits verification.\n\n---\n\n### Files Created or Modified:\n- `src/engine/materials.ts` \342\200\224 Comprehensive database of 7 machining materials (Aluminium 6061, Medium Carbon Steel 1045, Alloy Steel 4140, Stainless Steel 304, Titanium Ti-6Al-4V, Grey Cast Iron, and Brass) with ISO groups, hardness, yield strength, Kienzle $k_{c1.1}$ specific forces, chip exponents $m_c$, and recommended $V_c$ / $f_z$ bands for Solid Carbide and HSS.\n- `src/engine/cutting.ts` \342\200\224 Pure TypeScript physics engine implementing:\n  - Spindle speed $n = \\frac{1000 \\cdot V_c}{\\pi \\cdot D}$\n  - Milling table feed $v_f = f_z \\cdot z \\cdot n$ and MRR $Q = \\frac{a_p \\cdot a_e \\cdot v_f}{1000}$\n  - Average chip thickness $h_m = f_z \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{a_e}{D}}$ and Kienzle force $k_c = k_{c1} \\cdot h^{-m_c}$\n  - Cutting power $P_c$ with efficiency $\\eta = 0.8$, spindle torque $M_c = \\frac{P_c \\cdot 30000}{\\pi \\cdot n}$, and 3-tier power load zones (green $< 70\\%$, amber $70-90\\%$, red $> 90\\%$)\n  - Turning/Boring surface roughness $R_a = \\frac{f_n^2}{8 \\cdot r} \\cdot 1000$, cycle time, and $> 4\\times D$ boring overhang chatter warnings\n  - Drilling thrust force $F_f$, cycle time, and $> 5\\times D$ peck drilling warnings\n  - Tapping tap drill formulas and Fanuc rigid tapping G-code blocks (`M29 S{n}` / `G84 Z-{L} R2.0 F{vf}`)\n  - Input validation returning typed error/warning arrays\n- `src/components/calculator/Calculator3DView.tsx` \342\200\224 Interactive 3D simulation with cylinder cutter spinning at speed proportional to RPM, clamped workpiece block, machine bed grid, XYZ triad readouts, and playback/speed controls.\n- `src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx` \342\200\224 Calculator interface matching `cutting-calculator/code.html`:\n  - Process selector bar (Milling, Turning, Drilling, Tapping, Boring)\n  - Segmented Metric ($mm/min$) / Imperial ($IPM$) unit switcher\n  - Material selector with reference values disclaimer\n  - Carbide vs HSS grade switcher\n  - 48px touch-target steppers for tool diameter $D_c$ and flutes $z$\n  - Surface speed slider with green recommended sweet-spot range guide and inline warnings\n  - Feed slider with finishing, slotting, and roughing band indicators\n  - Machine limits configuration (Max RPM, Spindle Motor kW)\n  - 4 core metric cards in JetBrains Mono 32px bold: Spindle Speed, Feed Rate, MRR, and Spindle Torque\n  - Cutting power consumption card with horizontal 3-zone load gauge\n  - Slide-out Copilot Process Engineer AI drawer\n- `server/routes/explain.ts` \342\200\224 `POST /api/explain` endpoint using `MODEL_FLASH` to explain cutting parameters in under 120 words in the operator\'s preferred language, flagging high power loads ($> 80\\%$), out-of-band speeds, deep holes, or long overhangs. Writes an activity row to `users/{uid}/activity` and tracks transactional rate limits.\n- `server.ts` \342\200\224 Mounted `/api/explain` endpoint with authentication middleware.\n- `src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Integrated `CuttingCalculator` into the main application router.\n\n---\n\n### 3-Step Manual Test for the Preview:\n\n1. **Verify Default Milling Physics & 3D Viewport**:\n   - In the top navigation, click **Cutting Calculator**.\n   - With the default parameters (**Aluminium 6061-T6**, **\303\23010.0mm 4-Flute Carbide**, $V_c = 160\\text{ m/min}$, $f_z = 0.080\\text{ mm/tooth}$, $a_p = 15.0\\text{ mm}$, $a_e = 4.0\\text{ mm}$):\n     - Confirm **Spindle Speed**: `5,093 RPM`\n     - Confirm **Feed Rate**: `1,630 mm/min`\n     - Confirm **MRR**: `97.8 cm\302\263/min`\n     - Confirm **Cutting Power Consumption**: `3.0 kW / 15.0 kW Max` (20% Spindle Load, green zone)\n     - Observe the 3D tool contact viewport spinning the end mill cutter smoothly above the workpiece.\n\n2. **Verify Process Switching & Physics Warnings**:\n   - Switch to **Tapping**:\n     - Observe the **Thread Pitch** stepper and the automatically generated **Fanuc Rigid Tapping Block (G84)** with `M29 S5093` and tap drill calculation `\303\2308.5 mm`.\n   - Switch to **Turning** and drag feed to $0.35\\text{ mm/rev}$:\n     - Observe the calculated **Surface Finish ($R_a$)** and cycle time updates.\n   - Select **Titanium Ti-6Al-4V** and increase $V_c$ above $70\\text{ m/min}$:\n     - Notice the orange warning box instantly appears: *\"Surface speed exceeds recommended CARBIDE limit (70 m/min) for Titanium Ti-6Al-4V...\"*\n   - Toggle **Imperial (IPM)** to test real-time unit conversion across all readouts.\n\n3. **Verify \"Ask Copilot Why\" AI Process Explanation**:\n   - Click the bottom button **\"Ask CNC Copilot to verify this setup for tool chatter & deflection\"**.\n   - The industrial side drawer will slide open and call `/api/explain`.\n   - Confirm Gemini generates a concise explanation (under 120 words) analyzing the cutting load, thermal stability, and toolpath safety.\n   - Return to the **Dashboard** and verify that a new activity entry has been logged under **Recent Activity & Shop Logs** with a \"Resume\" link back to the calculator."
    modified_response: "### Milestone 2 Complete: Deterministic Cutting Engine, 3D Tool Contact Simulation, Cutting Calculator, and Copilot Explain API\n\nThe Cutting Calculator screen has been built to match the attached Stitch HTML design (`cutting-calculator/code.html`) and `DESIGN.md`. All calculations are derived from Kienzle specific cutting force formulas with physical limits verification.\n\n---\n\n### Files Created or Modified:\n- `src/engine/materials.ts` \342\200\224 Comprehensive database of 7 machining materials (Aluminium 6061, Medium Carbon Steel 1045, Alloy Steel 4140, Stainless Steel 304, Titanium Ti-6Al-4V, Grey Cast Iron, and Brass) with ISO groups, hardness, yield strength, Kienzle $k_{c1.1}$ specific forces, chip exponents $m_c$, and recommended $V_c$ / $f_z$ bands for Solid Carbide and HSS.\n- `src/engine/cutting.ts` \342\200\224 Pure TypeScript physics engine implementing:\n  - Spindle speed $n = \\frac{1000 \\cdot V_c}{\\pi \\cdot D}$\n  - Milling table feed $v_f = f_z \\cdot z \\cdot n$ and MRR $Q = \\frac{a_p \\cdot a_e \\cdot v_f}{1000}$\n  - Average chip thickness $h_m = f_z \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{a_e}{D}}$ and Kienzle force $k_c = k_{c1} \\cdot h^{-m_c}$\n  - Cutting power $P_c$ with efficiency $\\eta = 0.8$, spindle torque $M_c = \\frac{P_c \\cdot 30000}{\\pi \\cdot n}$, and 3-tier power load zones (green $< 70\\%$, amber $70-90\\%$, red $> 90\\%$)\n  - Turning/Boring surface roughness $R_a = \\frac{f_n^2}{8 \\cdot r} \\cdot 1000$, cycle time, and $> 4\\times D$ boring overhang chatter warnings\n  - Drilling thrust force $F_f$, cycle time, and $> 5\\times D$ peck drilling warnings\n  - Tapping tap drill formulas and Fanuc rigid tapping G-code blocks (`M29 S{n}` / `G84 Z-{L} R2.0 F{vf}`)\n  - Input validation returning typed error/warning arrays\n- `src/components/calculator/Calculator3DView.tsx` \342\200\224 Interactive 3D simulation with cylinder cutter spinning at speed proportional to RPM, clamped workpiece block, machine bed grid, XYZ triad readouts, and playback/speed controls.\n- `src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx` \342\200\224 Calculator interface matching `cutting-calculator/code.html`:\n  - Process selector bar (Milling, Turning, Drilling, Tapping, Boring)\n  - Segmented Metric ($mm/min$) / Imperial ($IPM$) unit switcher\n  - Material selector with reference values disclaimer\n  - Carbide vs HSS grade switcher\n  - 48px touch-target steppers for tool diameter $D_c$ and flutes $z$\n  - Surface speed slider with green recommended sweet-spot range guide and inline warnings\n  - Feed slider with finishing, slotting, and roughing band indicators\n  - Machine limits configuration (Max RPM, Spindle Motor kW)\n  - 4 core metric cards in JetBrains Mono 32px bold: Spindle Speed, Feed Rate, MRR, and Spindle Torque\n  - Cutting power consumption card with horizontal 3-zone load gauge\n  - Slide-out Copilot Process Engineer AI drawer\n- `server/routes/explain.ts` \342\200\224 `POST /api/explain` endpoint using `MODEL_FLASH` to explain cutting parameters in under 120 words in the operator\'s preferred language, flagging high power loads ($> 80\\%$), out-of-band speeds, deep holes, or long overhangs. Writes an activity row to `users/{uid}/activity` and tracks transactional rate limits.\n- `server.ts` \342\200\224 Mounted `/api/explain` endpoint with authentication middleware.\n- `src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Integrated `CuttingCalculator` into the main application router.\n\n---\n\n### 3-Step Manual Test for the Preview:\n\n1. **Verify Default Milling Physics & 3D Viewport**:\n   - In the top navigation, click **Cutting Calculator**.\n   - With the default parameters (**Aluminium 6061-T6**, **\303\23010.0mm 4-Flute Carbide**, $V_c = 160\\text{ m/min}$, $f_z = 0.080\\text{ mm/tooth}$, $a_p = 15.0\\text{ mm}$, $a_e = 4.0\\text{ mm}$):\n     - Confirm **Spindle Speed**: `5,093 RPM`\n     - Confirm **Feed Rate**: `1,630 mm/min`\n     - Confirm **MRR**: `97.8 cm\302\263/min`\n     - Confirm **Cutting Power Consumption**: `3.0 kW / 15.0 kW Max` (20% Spindle Load, green zone)\n     - Observe the 3D tool contact viewport spinning the end mill cutter smoothly above the workpiece.\n\n2. **Verify Process Switching & Physics Warnings**:\n   - Switch to **Tapping**:\n     - Observe the **Thread Pitch** stepper and the automatically generated **Fanuc Rigid Tapping Block (G84)** with `M29 S5093` and tap drill calculation `\303\2308.5 mm`.\n   - Switch to **Turning** and drag feed to $0.35\\text{ mm/rev}$:\n     - Observe the calculated **Surface Finish ($R_a$)** and cycle time updates.\n   - Select **Titanium Ti-6Al-4V** and increase $V_c$ above $70\\text{ m/min}$:\n     - Notice the orange warning box instantly appears: *\"Surface speed exceeds recommended CARBIDE limit (70 m/min) for Titanium Ti-6Al-4V...\"*\n   - Toggle **Imperial (IPM)** to test real-time unit conversion across all readouts.\n\n3. **Verify \"Ask Copilot Why\" AI Process Explanation**:\n   - Click the bottom button **\"Ask CNC Copilot to verify this setup for tool chatter & deflection\"**.\n   - The industrial side drawer will slide open and call `/api/explain`.\n   - Confirm Gemini generates a concise explanation (under 120 words) analyzing the cutting load, thermal stability, and toolpath safety.\n   - Return to the **Dashboard** and verify that a new activity entry has been logged under **Recent Activity & Shop Logs** with a \"Resume\" link back to the calculator."
