  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Shopfloor Agent HTML**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `shopfloor-agent/code.html` file provided. My primary objective is to thoroughly analyze the HTML structure. I\'m carefully reviewing the layout, components, and general organization of the code to understand its design. I intend to extract design pattern features of this code.\n\n\n**Defining Agent Routes**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifications for the `/agent` route, along with the `POST /api/agent` endpoint, as part of Milestone 3. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the structure of the left sidebar, messaging components, controller chips, and their data sources (Firestore). My goal is to extract design pattern features of this code and replace placeholders with real data and empty states, as directed in the specifications.\n\n\n**Detailing Response Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the components within the agent\'s response section. I\'m taking notes on how they\'re structured and designed. I\'m seeing the markdown rendering, citation chips, the \"Play answer\" button, and feedback buttons. Additionally, the collapsible \"How I got this\" panel, the citation chip interaction, and the composer features, are all under consideration.\n\n\n**Defining Agent API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now detailing the requirements for the `/api/agent` POST endpoint and related parameters. I need to handle image and audio uploads (up to 2048px and 5MB). The plan is to create a well-defined `POST /api/agent` structure, including considerations for an empty state with suggestion cards. I need to make the system instructions clear, including specifics around data sourcing, safety, and language handling, focusing on the controller variable.\n\n\n**Formulating Function Calls**\n\nI\'m now detailing the `POST /api/agent` structure, concentrating on Step 1: `MODEL_FLASH` function declarations. This includes `calculate_cutting`, `get_material`, and `verify_gcode` calls. I\'m focusing on incorporating image and audio handling. My aim is to define how the model will process these inputs, including inline audio transcription and image-based alarm identification.\n\n\n**Defining Feedback Loop**\n\nI\'m now detailing the requirements for the feedback loop, focusing on the `/api/feedback` endpoint. I\'m noting the data structure for `POST /api/feedback`, including `chatId`, `messageId`, `rating`, and optional `comment`. This feedback will write to `feedback/{id}`. I am also inspecting the `shopfloor-agent/code.html` file, observing the UI elements, including the sidebar and chat components, such as the `New Session` button, search input, chat session items, the main chat column header, operator and copilot messages.\n\n\n**Designing Response Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the diagnostic card within the agent\'s response section. I\'m taking notes on how it is to be structured and designed, including the fault confidence metric and operational checklist. Additionally, I\'m noting the verified citation chips, the \"How I got this\" collapsible panel, the thumbs up/down feedback buttons, and the audio speaker button. I\'m also planning the new sticky composer, including the text area, upload buttons, and send button. I\'m also planning the execution, beginning with the G-code verification helper file.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_866215"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface GCodeFinding {\\n  severity: \'CRITICAL\' | \'WARNING\' | \'INFO\';\\n  line: number;\\n  code: string;\\n  message: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GCodeSegment {\\n  type: \'rapid\' | \'feed\' | \'arc\';\\n  from: { x: number; y: number; z: number };\\n  to: { x: number; y: number; z: number };\\n  center?: { x: number; y: number; z: number };\\n  line: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GCodeParseResult {\\n  segments: GCodeSegment[];\\n  findings: GCodeFinding[];\\n  blockCount: number;\\n  criticalCount: number;\\n  warningCount: number;\\n  infoCount: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport function parseAndVerifyGCode(program: string, _controller: string = \'fanuc\'): GCodeParseResult {\\n  const lines = program.split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const findings: GCodeFinding[] = [];\\n  const segments: GCodeSegment[] = [];\\n\\n  let currentPos = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 50 };\\n  let activeTool: number | null = null;\\n  let activeH: number | null = null;\\n  let spindleOn = false;\\n  let hasG90orG91 = false;\\n  let hasPlane = false;\\n  let hasFeed = false;\\n  let hasWcs = false;\\n  let currentFeed = 0;\\n  let currentSpindle = 0;\\n  let isAbsolute = true;\\n  let activeMotion: \'G00\' | \'G01\' | \'G02\' | \'G03\' = \'G00\';\\n  let firstMotionSeen = false;\\n  let lastNonEmptyLine = 1;\\n  let endsWithM30orM02 = false;\\n\\n  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\\n    const lineNum = i + 1;\\n    let raw = lines[i].trim();\\n    if (!raw) continue;\\n    lastNonEmptyLine = lineNum;\\n\\n    // Check for comments in ( )\\n    const pitchMatch = raw.match(/\\\\(M(\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?)[xX](\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?)\\\\)/i);\\n    let tapPitch: number | null = null;\\n    if (pitchMatch) {\\n      tapPitch = parseFloat(pitchMatch[2]);\\n    }\\n\\n    // Strip comments in ( ) and after ;\\n    const stripped = raw.replace(/\\\\([^)]*\\\\)/g, \'\').replace(/;.*$/, \'\').trim();\\n    if (!stripped) continue;\\n\\n    // Tokenize\\n    const tokens = stripped.toUpperCase().match(/[A-Z]-?\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?/g) || [];\\n\\n    let lineHasMotion = false;\\n    let newX = currentPos.x;\\n    let newY = currentPos.y;\\n    let newZ = currentPos.z;\\n    let movedX = false;\\n    let movedY = false;\\n    let movedZ = false;\\n    let arcR: number | null = null;\\n    let arcI: number | null = null;\\n    let arcJ: number | null = null;\\n    let isTapCycle = false;\\n\\n    for (const tok of tokens) {\\n      const letter = tok[0];\\n      const val = parseFloat(tok.slice(1));\\n\\n      if (letter === \'G\') {\\n        if (val === 0) { activeMotion = \'G00\'; lineHasMotion = true; }\\n        else if (val === 1) { activeMotion = \'G01\'; lineHasMotion = true; }\\n        else if (val === 2) { activeMotion = \'G02\'; lineHasMotion = true; }\\n        else if (val === 3) { activeMotion = \'G03\'; lineHasMotion = true; }\\n        else if (val === 90) { isAbsolute = true; hasG90orG91 = true; }\\n        else if (val === 91) { isAbsolute = false; hasG90orG91 = true; }\\n        else if (val === 17 || val === 18 || val === 19) { hasPlane = true; }\\n        else if (val >= 54 && val <= 59) { hasWcs = true; }\\n        else if (val === 43) { /* Handled with H */ }\\n        else if (val === 49) { activeH = null; }\\n        else if (val === 84) { isTapCycle = true; }\\n      } else if (letter === \'M\') {\\n        if (val === 3 || val === 4) spindleOn = true;\\n        else if (val === 5) spindleOn = false;\\n        else if (val === 30 || val === 2) endsWithM30orM02 = true;\\n      } else if (letter === \'T\') {\\n        activeTool = Math.round(val);\\n      } else if (letter === \'H\') {\\n        activeH = Math.round(val);\\n      } else if (letter === \'S\') {\\n        currentSpindle = val;\\n      } else if (letter === \'F\') {\\n        currentFeed = val;\\n        hasFeed = true;\\n      } else if (letter === \'X\') {\\n        newX = isAbsolute ? val : currentPos.x + val;\\n        movedX = true;\\n      } else if (letter === \'Y\') {\\n        newY = isAbsolute ? val : currentPos.y + val;\\n        movedY = true;\\n      } else if (letter === \'Z\') {\\n        newZ = isAbsolute ? val : currentPos.z + val;\\n        movedZ = true;\\n      } else if (letter === \'R\') {\\n        arcR = val;\\n      } else if (letter === \'I\') {\\n        arcI = val;\\n      } else if (letter === \'J\') {\\n        arcJ = val;\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Motion validations\\n    if (movedX || movedY || movedZ || lineHasMotion) {\\n      if (!firstMotionSeen) {\\n        if (!hasG90orG91) {\\n          findings.push({\\n            severity: \'WARNING\',\\n            line: lineNum,\\n            code: \'NO_ABS_INC\',\\n            message: \'No G90/G91 modal positioning state declared before the first motion block.\',\\n          });\\n        }\\n        firstMotionSeen = true;\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check Arc Center\\n      if ((activeMotion === \'G02\' || activeMotion === \'G03\') && arcR === null && arcI === null && arcJ === null) {\\n        findings.push({\\n          severity: \'CRITICAL\',\\n          line: lineNum,\\n          code: \'ARC_NO_CENTER\',\\n          message: `${activeMotion} circular interpolation without defined R radius or I/J arc center vector.`,\\n        });\\n      }\\n\\n      if ((activeMotion === \'G02\' || activeMotion === \'G03\') && !hasPlane) {\\n        findings.push({\\n          severity: \'WARNING\',\\n          line: lineNum,\\n          code: \'NO_PLANE\',\\n          message: \'No G17/G18/G19 work plane declared before the first circular arc move.\',\\n        });\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check Spindle Off while feeding\\n      if ((activeMotion === \'G01\' || activeMotion === \'G02\' || activeMotion === \'G03\') && !spindleOn) {\\n        findings.push({\\n          severity: \'CRITICAL\',\\n          line: lineNum,\\n          code: \'SPINDLE_OFF_FEED\',\\n          message: `${activeMotion} cutting feed commanded while spindle rotation is OFF (M05 or unstarted). Immediate tool breakage risk.`,\\n        });\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check Missing Feed Rate\\n      if (activeMotion === \'G01\' && (!hasFeed || currentFeed <= 0)) {\\n        findings.push({\\n          severity: \'WARNING\',\\n          line: lineNum,\\n          code: \'NO_FEED\',\\n          message: \'G01 linear motion block executed before any F feed rate was established.\',\\n        });\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check Rapid Plunge into Z < 0 while moving X or Y\\n      if (activeMotion === \'G00\' && newZ < 0 && (movedX || movedY)) {\\n        findings.push({\\n          severity: \'CRITICAL\',\\n          line: lineNum,\\n          code: \'RAPID_PLUNGE\',\\n          message: `G00 rapid traverse plunged into negative Z (${newZ.toFixed(1)}mm) while simultaneously moving X/Y. High kinematic collision risk with workpiece.`,\\n        });\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check first Z move after T.. M06 without G43 H matching\\n      if (movedZ && activeTool !== null) {\\n        if (activeH === null || activeH !== activeTool) {\\n          findings.push({\\n            severity: \'CRITICAL\',\\n            line: lineNum,\\n            code: \'NO_G43\',\\n            message: `Z motion commanded after tool change (T0${activeTool}) without an active G43 H0${activeTool} tool length compensation offset.`,\\n          });\\n          activeTool = null; // Report once per tool change\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      // Record 3D kinematic segment\\n      segments.push({\\n        type: activeMotion === \'G00\' ? \'rapid\' : (activeMotion === \'G02\' || activeMotion === \'G03\') ? \'arc\' : \'feed\',\\n        from: { ...currentPos },\\n        to: { x: newX, y: newY, z: newZ },\\n        center: arcI !== null && arcJ !== null ? { x: currentPos.x + arcI, y: currentPos.y + arcJ, z: currentPos.z } : undefined,\\n        line: lineNum,\\n      });\\n\\n      currentPos = { x: newX, y: newY, z: newZ };\\n    }\\n\\n    // Check Rigid Tapping Feed vs Speed x Pitch\\n    if (isTapCycle && tapPitch && currentSpindle > 0) {\\n      const expectedFeed = Math.round(currentSpindle * tapPitch);\\n      if (Math.abs(currentFeed - expectedFeed) > 5) {\\n        findings.push({\\n          severity: \'WARNING\',\\n          line: lineNum,\\n          code: \'TAP_FEED\',\\n          message: `G84 rigid tapping feed rate (F${currentFeed}) does not match Spindle (S${currentSpindle}) x Pitch (${tapPitch}mm) = F${expectedFeed}. Risk of stripped threads or tap fracture.`,\\n        });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Final program checks\\n  if (!endsWithM30orM02) {\\n    findings.push({\\n      severity: \'WARNING\',\\n      line: lastNonEmptyLine,\\n      code: \'NO_END\',\\n      message: \'G-code program does not terminate with an M30 (program end & rewind) or M02 block.\',\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!hasWcs) {\\n    findings.push({\\n      severity: \'INFO\',\\n      line: 1,\\n      code: \'NO_WCS\',\\n      message: \'No explicit Work Coordinate System (G54 - G59) declared; program relies on current controller active datum.\',\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  const criticalCount = findings.filter(f => f.severity === \'CRITICAL\').length;\\n  const warningCount = findings.filter(f => f.severity === \'WARNING\').length;\\n  const infoCount = findings.filter(f => f.severity === \'INFO\').length;\\n\\n  return {\\n    segments,\\n    findings,\\n    blockCount: lines.length,\\n    criticalCount,\\n    warningCount,\\n    infoCount,\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create src/engine/gcode.ts for deterministic G-code verification and modal tracking\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/engine/gcode.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating gcode.ts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create G-code parsing engine\"}"
