  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":1,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:49:06Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nAct as a Principal Full-Stack Architect, CNC domain expert and Senior UI/UX engineer. Build a complete, working full-stack web app called \\\"CNC Copilot\\\", tagline \\\"AI explains. Physics decides.\\\", using the attached Stitch design. Follow every rule below exactly. Use only real data from Firestore or real API calls. Never hard-code sample records, fake alarms, fake scores or placeholder statistics in the UI; when there is no data, show a designed empty state.\\n\\n# 1. STACK AND ARCHITECTURE\\n- Fronte\\n<truncated 22982 bytes>\\nrrent local time is: 2026-10-15T23:49:06-07:00.\\n\\nThe user has uploaded 6 image(s):\\n- Image 1.png\\n- Image 3.png\\n- Image 5.png\\n- Image 7.png\\n- Image 9.jpeg\\n- Image 13.png\\nYou can embed these images in an artifact if you need the USER to review them.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nUser Email: biju0716@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"Image 1.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 2.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"Image 3.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 4.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"Image 5.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 6.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"Image 7.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 8.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\",\"uri\":\"Image 9.jpeg\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 11.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 12.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"Image 13.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"Image 14.html\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"uri\":\"Image 15.markdown\"}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":2,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:49:15Z\",\"input_tokens\":130002,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":838,\"thinking\":\"**Defining the Project Scope**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m carefully dissecting this request. \\\"CNC Copilot\\\" with that tagline is the focus. I\'m noting the required roles: architect, CNC expert, and UI/UX engineer. It\'s a broad scope, so I need to establish the core responsibilities for each role to prevent mission creep. I will prioritize essential functions.\\n\\n\\n**Outlining Milestones Rigorously**\\n\\nI\'ve established the foundation, and now I\'m breaking down the development into concrete, testable milestones as dictated. Each \\n<truncated 171 bytes>\\ntion, Firebase auth, landing page, dashboard, and the /api/health endpoint.\\n\\n\\n**Prioritizing Milestone Progress**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on Milestone 7. This involves integrating /api/tts functionality and defining crucial Firestore and Storage rules. Furthermore, I\'m working to implement error handling and empty state management, alongside ensuring responsiveness down to a 375px mobile viewport. I\'m focusing on starting from Milestone 1 for the app\'s structure and design. I will prepare for my Skill Check.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read Firebase skill\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":4,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:49:25Z\",\"input_tokens\":14062,\"cache_read_tokens\":130244,\"output_tokens\":76,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing workspace files\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List root directory\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":6,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:49:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":2289,\"cache_read_tokens\":142243,\"output_tokens\":1587,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Firebase Context**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the specific Firebase details provided. I\'m taking inventory of the project name, database location, enabled authentication method, and storage configuration. These details are helping me establish a solid foundation for understanding the environment. I need to make sure I understand the scope of the project based on this information, and any implicit details the user may have in mind.\\n\\n\\n**Reviewing Firebase Access**\\n\\nI\'ve just recognized a crit\\n<truncated 1827 bytes>\\n}`. I\'ve confirmed that `set_up_firebase` is a tool, but I must follow the instructions. I must wait for user response after calling `show_aistudio_ui`. I\'m also reviewing `metadata.json` for app name and description, currently a placeholder, with the real app name as \\\"CNC Copilot\\\". I\'ll integrate the new tagline into the description: \\\"AI explains. Physics decides. High-precision CNC shopfloor copilot with physics-based cutting calculations, G-code verification.\\\" I\'ll need to check the html file as well.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Set application name and description in metadata.json\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"6\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json with CNC Copilot details\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CNC Copilot\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"AI explains. Physics decides. High-precision CNC shopfloor copilot with physics-based cutting calculations, G-code kinematic verification, crash simulation, and manual grounding.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"requestFramePe\\n<truncated 118 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"requestFramePermissions\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"majorCapabilities\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\\\\\\\"]\\\\n}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":8,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:49:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":3975,\"cache_read_tokens\":143144,\"output_tokens\":845,\"thinking\":\"**Updating HTML Sync**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating `/index.html` to synchronize the page\'s title, meta description, and Open Graph metadata. I\'m also integrating Google Fonts for \\\"Inter\\\" and \\\"JetBrains Mono,\\\" per the design system\'s font specifications. \\\"Inter\\\" is for UI text, and \\\"JetBrains Mono\\\" is for all numbers.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Sync index.html title, meta tags, and fonts with CNC Copilot brand\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"18\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update index.html with CNC Copilot title, description, and Google fonts\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\\\n<html lang=\\\\\\\"en\\\\\\\" class=\\\\\\\"dark\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <head>\\\\n    <meta charset=\\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <title>CNC Copilot | AI explains. Physics decides.</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\n<truncated 1236 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\\\n<html lang=\\\\\\\"en\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <head>\\\\n    <meta charset=\\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"An applic\\n<truncated 464 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update index.html with CNC Copilot metadata and fonts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":10,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:49:53Z\",\"input_tokens\":3660,\"cache_read_tokens\":145115,\"output_tokens\":136,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.env.example\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading .env.example\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read current .env.example\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":12,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:50:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":2534,\"cache_read_tokens\":146700,\"output_tokens\":191,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"# Server environment variables\\\\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nFIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nSTORAGE_BUCKET=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nADMIN_EMAILS=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nAPP_URL=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update .env.example with required variables and empty values\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/.env.example\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing .env.example\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update .env.example\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":14,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:50:08Z\",\"input_tokens\":2375,\"cache_read_tokens\":147160,\"output_tokens\":155,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"show_aistudio_ui\",\"args\":{\"arguments\":\"{}\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Requesting Firebase setup UI\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Show Firebase setup UI\\\"\",\"ui_type\":\"\\\"firebase_setup\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":16,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T06:50:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":2317,\"cache_read_tokens\":147462,\"output_tokens\":71,\"content\":\"Please complete the Firebase setup confirmation in the panel to proceed with provisioning the Firestore database and Authentication for CNC Copilot.\"}\n{\"step_index\":17,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:13:22Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nFirebase terms accepted, continue setting up database.\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: true\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-16T00:13:22-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nUser Email: biju0716@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":18,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:13:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":150076,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":380,\"thinking\":\"**Confirming UI Actions**\\n\\nI\'ve got confirmation on the UI interaction! Now I\'m checking the skill instructions. They state that, if Firebase setup is declined, I should avoid any Firebase RPCs or implementation. Otherwise, I should call `rpc_action` with `service_name`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"rpc_action\",\"args\":{\"arguments\":\"{}\",\"method_name\":\"\\\"GetFirebaseTos\\\"\",\"service_name\":\"\\\"fax\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Verifying Firebase terms\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Verify Firebase terms accepted\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:13:36Z\",\"input_tokens\":2543,\"cache_read_tokens\":148064,\"output_tokens\":185,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"rpc_action\",\"args\":{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"database_id\\\":\\\"(default)\\\",\\\"firestore_region\\\":\\\"asia-south1\\\",\\\"platform\\\":\\\"web\\\",\\\"project_id\\\":\\\"cnc-copilot-abc26\\\"}\",\"method_name\":\"\\\"ProvisionFirebase\\\"\",\"service_name\":\"\\\"fax\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Provisioning Firebase database\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Provision Firebase with project ID and region\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":22,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:14:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":2668,\"cache_read_tokens\":148531,\"output_tokens\":99,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking generated config\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check root files for firebase config\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":24,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:14:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":2336,\"cache_read_tokens\":149125,\"output_tokens\":75,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/firebase-applet-config.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking firebase config\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View firebase-applet-config.json\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":26,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:14:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":2635,\"cache_read_tokens\":149386,\"output_tokens\":75,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking dependencies\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View package.json\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":28,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:14:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":2839,\"cache_read_tokens\":149945,\"output_tokens\":357,\"thinking\":\"**Identifying Dependencies**\\n\\nI\'ve made progress on outlining the necessary dependencies. I\'ve pinpointed `firebase` for the client-side Auth and Firestore interaction. Furthermore, `firebase-admin` is needed for server-side operations, initialized with `applicationDefault()`. To handle the Markdown rendering, I\'ll use `react-markdown`. Lastly, `@react-three/fiber` is required.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"install_applet_package\",\"args\":{\"PackageNames\":\"[\\\"firebase\\\",\\\"firebase-admin\\\",\\\"react-markdown\\\",\\\"three\\\",\\\"@react-three/fiber\\\",\\\"@react-three/drei\\\",\\\"multer\\\"]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Installing packages\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Install Firebase, 3D, and Markdown packages\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":30,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:15:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":2536,\"cache_read_tokens\":150792,\"output_tokens\":76,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"install_applet_package\",\"args\":{\"IsDevDependency\":\"true\",\"PackageNames\":\"[\\\"@types/three\\\",\\\"@types/multer\\\"]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Installing dev dependencies\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Install types for Three and Multer\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":32,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:15:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":2237,\"cache_read_tokens\":151255,\"output_tokens\":478,\"thinking\":\"**Examining the Script**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `package.json` file. I\'ve noted the dev script\'s instruction to use `server.ts` with Express for backend functionality, leveraging `vite.middlewares` in development. It\'s crucial that Express is never mounted within Vite itself, per the prescribed configuration guidelines.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing package.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check package.json scripts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":34,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:16:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":3409,\"cache_read_tokens\":151483,\"output_tokens\":1924,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Blueprint & Rules**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `firebase-blueprint.json` file and the Firestore rules to understand the system\'s structure. I\'m focusing on the `users/{uid}` document, specifically extracting the required fields: `displayName`, `email`, `photoURL`, and the preference fields, `preferredLanguage` and `preferredController`, noting the language options and the possible controller choice. This will inform my next steps.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'ve been mapping out the data structures in detail now. Specifically, the schema for chats, messages, user activity, academy progress, usage, knowledge base documents, and feedback is being defined. It\'s a comprehensive view of how each element integrates into the system. I\'m focusing on attributes, roles, and how data is created and updated.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"entities\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"User\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User Profile\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User profile with preferences and assigned role\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"properties\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"displayName\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\" }\\n<truncated 4751 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create firebase-blueprint.json intermediate representation\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Write firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":36,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:16:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":4125,\"cache_read_tokens\":152976,\"output_tokens\":672,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Firestore Rules**\\n\\nI\'m currently crafting the `firestore.rules` file to implement the specified access controls. I\'ve focused on ensuring users can only manage their own data under `users/{own uid}`, excluding the `role` field. Furthermore, I\'m setting up public read access for `kb_docs`, while restricting any client-side modifications. Finally, I\'ve restricted access to usage, feedback and config.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"rules_version = \'2\';\\\\n\\\\nservice cloud.firestore {\\\\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\\\\n    // Default-deny catch-all\\\\n    match /{document=**} {\\\\n      allow read, write: if false;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    function isSignedIn() {\\\\n      return request.auth !=\\n<truncated 1501 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Write secure firestore.rules according to specifications\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Write firestore.rules\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":38,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:16:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":2864,\"cache_read_tokens\":155109,\"output_tokens\":53,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"deploy_firebase\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Deploying firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Deploy Firestore security rules\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":40,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:16:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":2207,\"cache_read_tokens\":155896,\"output_tokens\":2518,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Deployment Success**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report that the Firestore rules deployed without a hitch! Now, I\'m shifting my focus to the requirements for Milestone 1. I\'m taking a close look at the project structure, design system, navigation, Firebase Auth sign-in implementation, and the components for the landing page, dashboard, and server setup with token middleware. I\'m keen on getting this milestone locked down.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Milestone 1 Scope**\\n\\nI\'m now diving deep into Milestone 1 specifications.\\n<truncated 3684 bytes>\\nanning out the `/server` directory, defining `/server/config.ts` and `/server/firebase.ts` for initialization.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Server-Side Components**\\n\\nI\'m now detailing the server components. I\'ve defined `/server/authMiddleware.ts` to verify tokens and fetch user data, plus `/server/rateLimiter.ts` for daily checks. I\'m finalizing `/server/logger.ts` for hashed user IDs and `routes/` for health and user endpoints. I\'m also preparing for the Express and Vite integration and the Gemini API model selection.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\\\ndotenv.config();\\\\n\\\\nexport const MODEL_FLASH = \'gemini-2.5-flash\';\\\\nexport const MODEL_PRO = \'gemini-2.5-pro\';\\\\nexport const MODEL_TTS = \'gemini-2.5-flash\';\\\\n\\\\nexport const FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID = process.env.FIREBASE_PROJECT_I\\n<truncated 418 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create /server/config.ts with model and environment constants\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server/config.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating /server/config.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create server config\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":42,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:17:19Z\",\"input_tokens\":2676,\"cache_read_tokens\":159083,\"output_tokens\":633,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Firebase Access**\\n\\nI\'m now building out `/server/firebase.ts` to manage Firebase access, focusing on initializing `firebase-admin` using `applicationDefault()` and the `projectId` from environment variables. I\'m making sure to avoid service account JSON files as instructed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import admin from \'firebase-admin\';\\\\nimport { applicationDefault } from \'firebase-admin/app\';\\\\nimport { FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID, STORAGE_BUCKET } from \'./config.js\';\\\\n\\\\nlet initialized = false;\\\\n\\\\ntry {\\\\n  if (!admin.apps.length) {\\\\n    admin.initializeApp({\\\\\\n<truncated 870 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create /server/firebase.ts for firebase-admin initialization\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server/firebase.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating /server/firebase.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create server Firebase admin module\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":44,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:17:30Z\",\"input_tokens\":2844,\"cache_read_tokens\":159721,\"output_tokens\":483,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Logging Strategy**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on implementing the logging requirements for each AI request. I\'m building `/server/logger.ts` now. Each request will output a JSON line to stdout, including details like the route, a UID hash, the controller used, language, called tools, citation count, latency, the model used, token counts for both input and output, and also ensuring sensitive information is never logged.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import crypto from \'crypto\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface AIRequestLog {\\\\n  route: string;\\\\n  uid?: string;\\\\n  controller?: string;\\\\n  language?: string;\\\\n  toolNames?: string[];\\\\n  citationCount?: number;\\\\n  latencyMs: number;\\\\n  model: string;\\\\n  promptTokens?: \\n<truncated 855 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create /server/logger.ts for structured JSON logging\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server/logger.ts\