plain`, `/api/gcode-review`, `/api/instructor`, `/api/tts`, and `/api/kb/test` routes. I\'m aiming for a robust and efficient solution.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { Request, Response, NextFunction } from \'express\';\\\\nimport { adminDb } from \'./firebase.js\';\\\\n\\\\nexport async function rateLimitAI(req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction): Promise<void> {\\\\n  const user = req.user;\\\\n  if (!user) {\\\\n    res.\\n<truncated 1138 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create /server/rateLimiter.ts for 100 requests/day per user Firestore transaction\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server/rateLimiter.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating /server/rateLimiter.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create rate limiter\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":50,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T07:17:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":2845,\"cache_read_tokens\":162644,\"output_tokens\":874,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Gemini Client Behavior**\\n\\nI\'m now implementing the Gemini client module. I\'ve set the call timeout to 25 seconds. I\'ve also incorporated a retry mechanism for rate limiting (429) or service unavailable (503) errors, employing a 2-second backoff with a single retry. The plan is to provide user-friendly error messages in the appropriate language upon ultimate failure.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { GoogleGenAI } from \'@google/genai\';\\\\nimport { GEMINI_API_KEY } from \'./config.js\';\\\\n\\\\nlet aiInstance: GoogleGenAI | null = null;\\\\n\\\\nexport function getGemini(): GoogleGenAI {\\\\n  if (!aiInstance) {\\\\n    aiInstance = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: GEMIN\\n<truncated 2461 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create /server/geminiClient.ts with 25s timeout and 2s retry logic\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"