\\n\\n**Constructing the AI Explanation**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on a systematic build: creating the `materials.ts` file, followed by the `cutting.ts` file for calculations. Then, I\'ll establish the `/api/explain` route and construct the 3D tool contact component. Next is the cutting calculator component, aiming for a precise match with the Stitch HTML, classes, and tokens. Finally, I will wire the calculator route and verify compilation.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export interface ToolSpeedRange {\\\\n  min: number;\\\\n  max: number;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface MaterialSpec {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  isoGroup: string;\\\\n  isoClass: \'P\' | \'M\' | \'K\' | \'N\' | \'S\' | \'H\';\\\\n  hardness: string;\\\\n  yieldMpa: number;\\\\n  kc1: \\n<truncated 3735 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create src/engine/materials.ts with 7 machining materials, Kienzle kc1, mc and cutting data\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/engine/materials.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating materials.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create machining materials database\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":173,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:16:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":4553,\"cache_read_tokens\":307606,\"output_tokens\":4453,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Cutting Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of `src/engine/cutting.ts`. Currently, I\'m focusing on translating Section 4.1\'s formulas into code. My immediate concern is robust input validation \342\200\223 I need to ensure that values for diameter, flutes/pitch, Vc, and feed are all positive to avoid downstream errors. Typed errors are the plan to communicate issues. I\'m starting with the common calculations, like RPM (n).\\n\\n\\n**Calculating Milling Parameters**\\n\\nI\'ve just added formulas for milling, like calculating chip thickness and power consumption based on input parameters. Now I\'m working through similar calculations for turning and boring operations, focusing on the distinct input requirements and formulas for each. I\'m keeping a close eye on making sure I follow the units, since many of the calculations mix units like mm, cm3 and kW.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { MaterialSpec } from \'./materials.js\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ProcessType = \'milling\' | \'turning\' | \'drilling\' | \'tapping\' | \'boring\';\\\\nexport type ToolMaterialType = \'carbide\' | \'hss\';\\\\nexport type TapType = \'cutting\' | \'forming\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface Cut\\n<truncated 10015 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create src/engine/cutting.ts with pure TypeScript physics calculations for all 5 machining processes\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/engine/cutting.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating cutting.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create cutting engine calculations\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":175,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:16:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":4714,\"cache_read_tokens\":312197,\"output_tokens\":1282,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing The Backend**\\n\\nI\'m now building the `/api/explain` route in `server/routes/explain.ts`. The prompt setup includes two pathways. First, I need to design a \\\"Ask Copilot why\\\" route requiring sign-in. This will involve POST requests with inputs and results. Second, I\'m setting up a `MODEL_FLASH` prompt to guide the AI, focusing on CNC process engineering expertise.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { Router } from \'express\';\\\\nimport { requireAuth } from \'../authMiddleware.js\';\\\\nimport { rateLimitAI } from \'../rateLimiter.js\';\\\\nimport { MODEL_FLASH } from \'../config.js\';\\\\nimport { getGemini, executeWithRetry } from \'../geminiClient.js\';\\\\nimpor\\n<truncated 3521 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create server/routes/explain.ts for AI cutting parameter explanation\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server/routes/explain.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating explain.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create /api/explain endpoint\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":177,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:17:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":3560,\"cache_read_tokens\":314838,\"output_tokens\":65,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing server.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View server.ts routes\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":179,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:17:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":2953,\"cache_read_tokens\":316251,\"output_tokens\":419,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Mount explainRouter on /api in server.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"20\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import and mount explainRouter\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import { healthRouter } from \'./server/routes/health.js\';\\\\nimport { userRouter } from \'./server/routes/user.js\';\\\\nimport { explainRouter } from \'./server/routes/explain.js\';\\\\n\\\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\\\nconst __dirname = path.dir\\n<truncated 324 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"5\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import { healthRouter } from \'./server/routes/health.js\';\\\\nimport { userRouter } from \'./server/routes/user.js\';\\\\n\\\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\\\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\\\\n\\\\nasync function startServer() {\\\\n  const \\n<truncated 228 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating server.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Mount explainRouter in server.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":181,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:18:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":2921,\"cache_read_tokens\":317058,\"output_tokens\":2911,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing 3D View**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building the 3D tool contact and chip geometry component, specifically `src/components/calculator/Calculator3DView.tsx`. The initial framework includes a 3D viewport featuring a spinning cylinder tool above a box, complete with a grid and axis triad. I\'ll need to link the tool\'s spin speed to RPM input. Also I\'ll ensure the X-axis readout is in good shape.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useRef, useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Canvas, useFrame } from \'@react-three/fiber\';\\\\nimport { OrbitControls } from \'@react-three/drei\';\\\\nimport * as THREE from \'three\';\\\\nimport { ProcessType } from \'../../engine/cutting.js\';\\\\n\\\\ninterf\\n<truncated 8760 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create src/components/calculator/Calculator3DView.tsx for 3D live cutter contact simulation\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/calculator/Calculator3DView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating Calculator3DView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create 3D tool contact simulation component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":183,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:18:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":3131,\"cache_read_tokens\":319977,\"output_tokens\":14149,\"thinking\":\"**Reviewing The Design**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx` component. The goal is a pixel-perfect recreation of the design in the attached HTML (`cutting-calculator/code.html`). I\'m focusing on breaking down the HTML into its constituent parts to map out the component\'s structure.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing The Layout**\\n\\nI\'ve been meticulously dissecting the design and am now focusing on the top process tabs bar and the left inputs panel. I\'ve noted the active \\\"Milling\\\" tab with \\n<truncated 696 bytes>\\n, axial depth, radial width, and machine limits are on my radar.\\n\\n\\n**Calculating Performance Metrics**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the performance metrics UI. I\'ve begun to sketch out the Material Removal Rate (MRR) display, spindle torque visualization, and the specific metrics for turning/boring, drilling, and tapping, especially rigid tapping. The cutting power consumption gauge card, with its multi-zone progress meter, is also taking shape. I\'m focusing on the load fill bar, safety ticks, and zone labels.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../../context/AuthContext.js\';\\\\nimport { MATERIALS, MaterialSpec } from \'../../engine/materials.js\';\\\\nimport { calculateCutting, ProcessType, ToolMaterialType, CuttingInputs, Cutt\\n<truncated 54730 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx matching Stitch HTML layout, M3 tokens, physics engine, and AI explanation drawer\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating CuttingCalculator.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Cutting Calculator component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":185,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:20:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":14701,\"cache_read_tokens\":323048,\"output_tokens\":96,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"85\",\"StartLine\":\"55\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx calculator tab\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View calculator tab in App.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":187,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:20:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":3027,\"cache_read_tokens\":335601,\"output_tokens\":225,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Import and render CuttingCalculator in src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"10\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import CuttingCalculator component\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import { Navigation } from \'./components/Navigation.js\';\\\\nimport { LandingPage } from \'./components/LandingPage.js\';\\\\nimport { Dashboard } from \'./components/Dashboard.js\';\\\\nimport { CuttingCalculator } from \'./components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.js\';\\n<truncated 1 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"3\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import { Navigation } from \'./components/Navigation.js\';\\\\nimport { LandingPage } from \'./components/LandingPage.js\';\\\\nimport { Dashboard } from \'./components/Dashboard.js\';\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Importing CuttingCalculator\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add CuttingCalculator import to App.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":189,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:20:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":2636,\"cache_read_tokens\":336491,\"output_tokens\":452,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Render CuttingCalculator on calculator tab in src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"81\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Render CuttingCalculator component\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"        {currentTab === \'calculator\' && (\\\\n          <CuttingCalculator />\\\\n        )}\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"62\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"        {currentTab === \'calculator\' && (\\\\n          <div className=\\\\\\\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-margin py-8\\\\\\\">\\\\n            <div className=\\\\\\\"bg-surface-container-low p-8 rounded-xl border border-outline-variant/30 text-center flex flex-col items-center justify\\n<truncated 1016 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Rendering CuttingCalculator\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Render CuttingCalculator component in App.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":191,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:20:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":3156,\"cache_read_tokens\":336976,\"output_tokens\":47,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Verifying applet compilation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet with Cutting Calculator\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":193,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:20:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":2255,\"cache_read_tokens\":338006,\"output_tokens\":63,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server after adding explain route\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":195,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:21:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":2268,\"cache_read_tokens\":338135,\"output_tokens\":88,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/health\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing /api/health\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Verify server health check\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":197,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:21:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":2363,\"cache_read_tokens\":338274,\"output_tokens\":365,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Kienzle Values**\\n\\nI\'m currently verifying the Kienzle values for a specific cutting scenario using a Node.js test script. I\'m focusing on Aluminium 6061-T6, a 10mm 4-flute solid carbide tool, with a cutting speed of 160 m/min and a feed per tooth of 0.080. The material constants are kc1 700 and mc 0.25. The goal is to cross-validate these default inputs to ensure accuracy in the cutting engine.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx tsx -e \\\\\\\"import { calculateCutting } from \'./src/engine/cutting.js\'; import { MATERIALS } from \'./src/engine/materials.js\'; const res = calculateCutting({ process: \'milling\', material: MATERIALS.al6061, toolMaterial: \'carbide\', diameter: 10, flutes: 4\\n<truncated 209 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing cutting engine calculations\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run test on cutting engine calculation\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":199,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:21:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":2627,\"cache_read_tokens\":338623,\"output_tokens\":402,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Cutting Results**\\n\\nI\'ve been analyzing the recent cutting results. The data shows an RPM of 5093, a feed rate (Vf) of 1630 mm/min, and an MRR of 97.8 cm3/min. Power consumption is at 3.0 kW with 5.6 Nm of torque, placing it in the green zone. I\'m noting the spindle speed (N) information in the `cutting-calculator/code.html` screenshot.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx tsx -e \\\\\\\"import { calculateCutting } from \'./src/engine/cutting.js\'; import { MATERIALS } from \'./src/engine/materials.js\'; for (const p of [\'turning\', \'drilling\', \'tapping\', \'boring\']) { const r = calculateCutting({ process: p, material: MATERIALS.al\\n<truncated 195 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing all machining processes\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test turning, drilling, tapping, boring physics\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":201,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:21:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":2733,\"cache_read_tokens\":339219,\"output_tokens\":70,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking compilation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Final compile check for Milestone 2\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":203,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:21:47Z\",\"input_tokens\":2279,\"cache_read_tokens\":339825,\"output_tokens\":1551,\"content\":\"### Milestone 2 Complete: Deterministic Cutting Engine, 3D Tool Contact Simulation, Cutting Calculator, and Copilot Explain API\\n\\nThe Cutting Calculator screen has been built to match the attached Stitch HTML design (`cutting-calculator/code.html`) and `DESIGN.md`. All calculations are derived from Kienzle specific cutting force formulas with physical limits verification.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Files Created or Modified:\\n- `src/engine/materials.ts` \342\200\224 Comprehensive database of 7 machining materials (Aluminium 6061, Medi\\n<truncated 4225 bytes>\\nhy\\\" AI Process Explanation**:\\n   - Click the bottom button **\\\"Ask CNC Copilot to verify this setup for tool chatter & deflection\\\"**.\\n   - The industrial side drawer will slide open and call `/api/explain`.\\n   - Confirm Gemini generates a concise explanation (under 120 words) analyzing the cutting load, thermal stability, and toolpath safety.\\n   - Return to the **Dashboard** and verify that a new activity entry has been logged under **Recent Activity & Shop Logs** with a \\\"Resume\\\" link back to the calculator.\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":204,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:23:53Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nAttached is the Stitch HTML for this screen. Match its layout, components, classes and tokens exactly, using DESIGN.md. Replace every hard-coded value, name, machine, session or statistic in it with real data or a designed empty state, following the real-data rules already given. Never show a machine status, telemetry value or operator name the app does not actually have.\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-16T01:23:53-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nUser Email: biju0716@gmail.com\\nThe user\'s firestore db is ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598 and you must always load the firebase skill when processing queries that require interacting with the database or Firebase services.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"code.html\"}]}\n{\"step_index\":205,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:23:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":362970,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":4753,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Shopfloor Agent HTML**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `shopfloor-agent/code.html` file provided. My primary objective is to thoroughly analyze the HTML structure. I\'m carefully reviewing the layout, components, and general organization of the code to understand its design. I intend to extract design pattern features of this code.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Agent Routes**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the specifications for the `/agent` route, along with the `POST /api/agent` endpoint, as part of Milestone 3. Specifical\\n<truncated 2228 bytes>\\nwithin the agent\'s response section. I\'m taking notes on how it is to be structured and designed, including the fault confidence metric and operational checklist. Additionally, I\'m noting the verified citation chips, the \\\"How I got this\\\" collapsible panel, the thumbs up/down feedback buttons, and the audio speaker button. I\'m also planning the new sticky composer, including the text area, upload buttons, and send button. I\'m also planning the execution, beginning with the G-code verification helper file.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export interface GCodeFinding {\\\\n  severity: \'CRITICAL\' | \'WARNING\' | \'INFO\';\\\\n  line: number;\\\\n  code: string;\\\\n  message: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface GCodeSegment {\\\\n  type: \'rapid\' | \'feed\' | \'arc\';\\\\n  from: { x: number; y: number; z: number };\\\\n  t\\n<truncated 8796 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create src/engine/gcode.ts for deterministic G-code verification and modal tracking\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/engine/gcode.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating gcode.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create G-code parsing engine\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}"
