    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "Act as a Principal Full-Stack Architect, CNC domain expert and Senior UI/UX engineer. Build a complete, working full-stack web app called \"CNC Copilot\", tagline \"AI explains. Physics decides.\", using the attached Stitch design. Follow every rule below exactly. Use only real data from Firestore or real API calls. Never hard-code sample records, fake alarms, fake scores or placeholder statistics in the UI; when there is no data, show a designed empty state.\n\n# 1. STACK AND ARCHITECTURE\n- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS. Icons: lucide-react. Markdown: react-markdown.\n- 3D: @react-three/fiber + @react-three/drei. Simple primitives only (lines, boxes, cylinders). No physics libraries, no particle chip generation.\n- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript in /server. The same service serves the built frontend and the /api routes (one Cloud Run service).\n- Firebase project: cnc-copilot-abc26. Firestore database \"(default)\" in asia-south1. Firebase Authentication with Google sign-in. Cloud Storage default bucket.\n- Server Firebase access: firebase-admin initialized with applicationDefault() credentials and projectId from env. Never use or create a service-account JSON key file.\n- AI: Google Gemini API through the @google/genai SDK, server side only.\n- Create /server/config.ts with constants: MODEL_FLASH, MODEL_PRO, MODEL_TTS set to the newest Gemini Flash, Gemini Pro and Gemini TTS model IDs available in this environment. Every Gemini call imports from this file.\n- Environment variables (server only): GEMINI_API_KEY, FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=cnc-copilot-abc26, STORAGE_BUCKET, ADMIN_EMAILS=biju0716@gmail.com. Create .env.example with these names and empty values.\n- SECURITY: GEMINI_API_KEY never reaches the browser. The client sends the Firebase ID token as \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" on every /api call. Express middleware verifies it with firebase-admin and attaches uid, email and role. Only GET /api/health is public.\n- Rate limit: every AI endpoint (/api/agent, /api/explain, /api/gcode-review, /api/instructor, /api/tts, /api/kb/test) increments usage/{uid}_{yyyymmdd}.requests in a Firestore transaction. Above 100 per day return HTTP 429 with {error:\"daily_limit\"} and the UI shows \"Daily limit reached. Resets at midnight.\" Admins are exempt.\n- Logging: each AI request logs one JSON line to stdout: route, uidHash (sha256 first 12 chars), controller, language, tool names called, citation count, latencyMs, model, promptTokens, outputTokens. Never log message text, images or audio.\n- Gemini calls: 25 second timeout, one retry on 429 or 503 with 2 second backoff, friendly error in the user\'s language on final failure.\n\n# 2. DESIGN SYSTEM (strict)\n- Dark industrial. Background #0B0F14 with a subtle CSS noise overlay (inline SVG data URI, opacity 0.04).\n- Colors: primary #FF7A1A (safety orange), secondary #22D3EE (coolant cyan), success #22C55E, warning #F59E0B, danger #EF4444, text #E6EDF3, muted #8B98A5, border #1F2A37.\n- Fonts: Inter for UI text, JetBrains Mono for all numbers, G-code, coordinates and technical values (Google Fonts).\n- Panels: rounded-xl (12px), bg-white/5 backdrop-blur-md border border-[#1F2A37]. Hover: border-[#FF7A1A]/30 shadow-lg shadow-orange-500/5 transition-all duration-200.\n- Accessibility: WCAG AA contrast, every icon button has an aria-label, visible focus ring in #22D3EE, minimum touch target 48x48 px for gloved hands.\n- Responsive: below 768 px every multi-column screen stacks vertically. No side-by-side grids on small screens.\n- Navigation (signed in): desktop top bar with logo \"CNC Copilot\" + spindle icon, links Home, Agent, Calculator, G-code, Academy, (Knowledge Base only for admins), language selector (English, Hindi, Malayalam, Tamil) and avatar menu (sign out). Mobile: bottom tab bar with 5 tabs: Home, Agent, Calc, G-code, Academy.\n- Every screen has loading skeletons, an error state with \"Retry\", and an empty state.\n\n# 3. FIRESTORE DATA MODEL\n- users/{uid}: displayName, email, photoURL, preferredLanguage (\"en\"|\"hi\"|\"ml\"|\"ta\"), preferredController (\"fanuc\"|\"mitsubishi\"|\"generic\"), role (\"user\"|\"admin\"), createdAt. Created by the server on first sign-in. role = \"admin\" if the email is in ADMIN_EMAILS, otherwise \"user\". The client can never write role.\n- users/{uid}/chats/{chatId}: title (first 60 chars of the first question), controller, createdAt, updatedAt.\n- users/{uid}/chats/{chatId}/messages/{msgId}: role (\"user\"|\"model\"), text, imageUrl, citations [{document, page, snippet}], toolCalls [{name, args, result}], createdAt.\n- users/{uid}/activity/{id}: type (\"chat\"|\"calc\"|\"gcode\"|\"academy\"), title, summary, link, createdAt. Written by the server after each successful action. Dashboard reads the latest 5.\n- users/{uid}/academy/progress: xp, level, streakDays, lastActiveDate, badges [], missions {missionId: {status, attempts, crashes, hintsUsed, bestXp, completedAt}}.\n- usage/{uid}_{yyyymmdd}: requests. Server only.\n- kb_docs/{docId}: name, controller, docType (\"Manual\"|\"Shop Notes\"|\"Parameter List\"), pages, status (\"Indexing\"|\"Ready\"|\"Failed\"), fileSearchDocumentName, storagePath, uploadedBy, createdAt.\n- feedback/{id}: uid, chatId, messageId, rating (1|-1), comment, createdAt. Server only.\n- config/app: fileSearchStoreName. Server only.\nFirestore rules: a user reads and writes only users/{own uid} and its subcollections, except the role field, which only the server sets. kb_docs readable by any signed-in user, no client writes. usage, feedback and config: no client access. Storage rules: no direct client reads or writes; all uploads and downloads go through the server.\n\n# 4. DETERMINISTIC ENGINES (pure TypeScript, no AI, no external dependencies)\n\n## 4.1 Cutting engine: src/engine/cutting.ts and src/engine/materials.ts\nMetric internally; the UI converts to inch when the units toggle is set. Validate inputs: diameter, flutes, Vc, feed > 0; return typed errors.\n- Common: n (rpm) = (1000 x Vc) / (pi x D). Torque Mc (Nm) = (Pc x 30000) / (pi x n). kc (N/mm2) = kc1 x h^(-mc), h = chip thickness (mm).\n- Milling (inputs D, z, Vc, fz, ap, ae, machineMaxKw, eta default 0.8): vf = fz x z x n. Q (cm3/min) = (ap x ae x vf) / 1000. hm = fz x sqrt(ae / D) if ae/D <= 0.5, else hm = fz. Pc (kW) = (ap x ae x vf x kc) / (60 x 10^6 x eta). Power % = Pc / machineMaxKw x 100: green < 70, amber 70 to 90, red > 90.\n- Turning and Boring (D, Vc, fn, ap, kr default 95 deg, nose radius r default 0.8, cut length L, eta 0.8): vf = fn x n. Q = Vc x ap x fn. h = fn x sin(kr). Pc = (Vc x ap x fn x kc) / (60 x 10^3 x eta). Ra (micrometre) = (fn^2 / (8 x r)) x 1000. Cycle time (min) = L / vf. Boring: if overhang / barDiameter > 4 warn \"Above 4xD use a damped bar or reduce Vc and ap\".\n- Drilling (D, Vc, fn, pointAngle default 140, depth L, eta 0.8): vf = fn x n. Q = (Vc x D x fn) / 4. h = (fn / 2) x sin(pointAngle / 2). Pc = (fn x Vc x D x kc) / (240 x 10^3 x eta). Thrust Ff (N) ~ 0.5 x kc x (D / 2) x fn x sin(pointAngle / 2). Cycle time = L / vf. If L / D > 5 warn \"Use peck drilling (G83) or a through-coolant drill\".\n- Tapping (nominal D, pitch P, Vc, tapType cutting|forming, depth L): n from Vc and D. vf = P x n. Tap drill: cutting = D - P, forming = D - 0.5 x P. Show the Fanuc rigid tapping block: \"M29 S{n}\" then \"G84 Z-{L} R2.0 F{vf}\".\nMaterials (label in UI: \"Reference values. Confirm with your tool supplier.\"):\nAluminium 6061: kc1 700, mc 0.25, Vc carbide 300-600, Vc HSS 80-120, fz 0.05-0.20\nSteel 1045: kc1 1700, mc 0.25, Vc carbide 180-250, Vc HSS 25-35, fz 0.05-0.15\nAlloy steel 4140: kc1 1950, mc 0.25, Vc carbide 150-220, Vc HSS 18-28, fz 0.05-0.12\nStainless 304: kc1 2000, mc 0.21, Vc carbide 120-180, Vc HSS 12-20, fz 0.04-0.10\nTitanium Ti-6Al-4V: kc1 1400, mc 0.23, Vc carbide 40-70, Vc HSS 6-10, fz 0.03-0.08\nGrey cast iron: kc1 1100, mc 0.28, Vc carbide 150-250, Vc HSS 20-30, fz 0.08-0.20\nBrass: kc1 700, mc 0.25, Vc carbide 200-400, Vc HSS 60-90, fz 0.05-0.20\n\n## 4.2 G-code engine: src/engine/gcode.ts\nTokenize lines, strip comments in ( ) and after ;. Track modal state: G00/G01/G02/G03, G90/G91, G17/G18/G19, G20/G21, G54-G59, F, S, T, H, spindle state (M03/M04 on, M05 off), active tool length offset (G43 H / G49). Output segments {type: \"rapid\"|\"feed\"|\"arc\", from {x,y,z}, to {x,y,z}, center?, line}. Arcs from R or I/J/K, interpolated at 24 points per 90 degrees. G91 moves accumulate.\nRule checks, each returns {severity, line, code, message}:\n- CRITICAL SPINDLE_OFF_FEED: G01/G02/G03 while spindle is off.\n- CRITICAL NO_G43: first Z move after \"T.. M06\" without an active G43 H matching the tool number.\n- CRITICAL RAPID_PLUNGE: G00 that ends with Z below 0 while also moving X or Y.\n- CRITICAL ARC_NO_CENTER: G02/G03 without R or I/J/K.\n- WARNING NO_ABS_INC: no G90/G91 before the first motion.\n- WARNING NO_PLANE: no G17/G18/G19 before the first arc.\n- WARNING NO_FEED: G01 before any F word.\n- WARNING TAP_FEED: G84 where F != S x pitch, pitch read from a comment like (M8x1.25) when present.\n- WARNING NO_END: program does not end with M30 or M02.\n- INFO NO_WCS: no G54-G59.\n\n## 4.3 Crash engine: src/engine/crash.ts (for the Academy)\nFixed scene in mm, work zero at top-left corner of the stock: table top Z = -60; vise box X -10..90, Y -15..65, Z -60..-10; stock box X 0..80, Y 0..50, Z -10..0. Tool length 100 mm. Replay segments from 4.2 and return the FIRST event:\n- RAPID_INTO_STOCK: a rapid segment that passes through the stock or vise volume (sample each segment every 0.5 mm).\n- NO_TOOL_OFFSET: Z motion after a tool change without G43 H; simulate by shifting the tool tip down 100 mm, so the tool drives into the vise or table.\n- SPINDLE_OFF_CUT: a feed move inside the stock while the spindle is off.\n- TAP_FEED_MISMATCH: G84 with F != S x pitch.\nIf more than one rule matches the same segment, report NO_TOOL_OFFSET first, then RAPID_INTO_STOCK, then the others.\nReturn {type, line, position {x,y,z}, damage {part, repairCostINR, downtimeDays}}:\nRAPID_INTO_STOCK: \"spindle bearings and end mill\", 180000, 4\nNO_TOOL_OFFSET: \"spindle, vise and table\", 340000, 6\nSPINDLE_OFF_CUT: \"end mill and workpiece\", 15000, 1\nTAP_FEED_MISMATCH: \"tap broken in part, part scrapped\", 8000, 1\nUI label under the damage card: \"Illustrative training cost. Real costs vary by machine.\"\n\n# 5. SCREENS\n\n## Route \"/\" \nSigned out: Landing page, short and factual.\n- Hero: \"Your machine stopped. Copilot knows why.\" Sub: \"Snap the alarm screen, ask in your language, get the fix from your own controller manual, with the page number.\" Buttons: \"Sign in with Google\" (orange), \"See how it works\" (scrolls). Right: simple 3D scene, end mill above an aluminium block with an orange toolpath line, slow auto-rotate.\n- \"Fix today\'s machine\": 3 cards (Shopfloor Agent, Cutting Calculator, G-code Verifier).\n- \"Build tomorrow\'s operator\": Academy band, headline \"Crash the machine here. Never on the shop floor.\" Mission cards, line \"Phase 2: VR operator training\".\n- \"How it works\": Ask (voice, photo, text) > Retrieve (your manuals) > Compute (physics engine) > Answer (your language, with citation).\n- \"Built on Google\": text grid Gemini, File Search, AI Studio, Antigravity, Cloud Run, Firebase.\n- Footer: \"Built for Google Cloud AI Builder Cup 2026\", GitHub link placeholder href=\"#\".\nSigned in: Operator Dashboard.\n- Header: \"Good morning / afternoon / evening, {firstName}\" from local time. Caption: live date like \"Friday, 16 Oct 2026\" and computed shift: Shift 1 06:00-14:00, Shift 2 14:00-22:00, Shift 3 22:00-06:00.\n- Resume banner (amber, only if the latest activity is a chat less than 24 h old): \"Last diagnosis: {title}. Continue\" linking to that chat. Icon lucide AlertTriangle, no emoji.\n- Quick actions: 4 large glass cards, min-h 140px, arrow-up-right icon bottom right: Diagnose Alarm (Camera, orange, opens /agent with camera ready), Calculate Feeds (Calculator, cyan), Verify G-code (Code, green), Crash Lab (GraduationCap, amber, shows current level and XP).\n- Recent activity: latest 5 from users/{uid}/activity with relative time and a \"Resume\" pill. Empty state: \"No activity yet. Start with a quick action above.\"\n- Manuals: cards from kb_docs where status = \"Ready\" (icon, name, controller, pages). Horizontal scroll on mobile, grid on desktop. Empty state: \"No manuals uploaded yet.\"\n\n## Route \"/agent\": Shopfloor Agent\n- Desktop: left sidebar w-80 + main chat. Mobile: full-width chat, sidebar in a drawer opened by a Menu icon.\n- Sidebar: \"New chat\" (orange), search box filtering chat titles, chat list from Firestore, controller chips Fanuc / Mitsubishi / Generic (saved to preferredController).\n- Messages: user bubbles right (bg-[#FF7A1A]/10), model bubbles left (bg-white/5) with markdown, citation chips (bg-[#22D3EE]/10 text-[#22D3EE] text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded), \"Play answer\" speaker button, thumbs up/down (writes feedback via POST /api/feedback), and a collapsible \"How I got this\" panel listing tool calls with args and results in JetBrains Mono.\n- Clicking a citation chip opens a right-side panel showing document name, page number and the cited snippet text returned by File Search.\n- Composer: textarea min-h 56px; Camera button (opens device camera via <input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" capture=\"environment\">), Mic button (hold to talk, pulsing ring while recording, max 60 s), Paperclip (image upload), Send (48x48 orange circle). Images resized on the client to max 2048 px, max 5 MB.\n- Empty state: 4 suggestion cards: \"Explain alarm SV0401 on Fanuc\", \"Feeds for a 10 mm 4-flute carbide end mill in 6061\", \"Why is my M10 thread oversize?\", \"Check this G-code for crash risk\".\n- POST /api/agent {chatId?, message, controller, language, imageBase64?, audioBase64?}:\n  System instruction: \"You are CNC Copilot, a shopfloor assistant for CNC operators and manufacturing engineers on {controller} controllers. 1) Never invent numbers for speeds, feeds, power, torque or thread data; always call calculate_cutting. 2) For alarms, parameters, programming and maintenance, answer only from retrieved manual passages and cite them as [Document, p.X]. If nothing relevant is retrieved, start with \'Not found in your uploaded manuals.\' and give general safe guidance labeled \'General guidance\'. 3) When an answer involves resetting alarms, changing parameters or overriding interlocks, start with a one-line safety warning. 4) Reply in {language}; keep G-codes, alarm numbers and parameter numbers in original form. 5) Be concise: the reader is standing at the machine.\"\n  If audioBase64: send it as inline audio with \"Transcribe the operator\'s question, then answer it.\" and save the transcript as the user message text.\n  If imageBase64: send inline with \"The image shows a CNC controller screen. First read out the alarm number, alarm text, mode and any axis values you can see, then answer.\"\n  Step 1: MODEL_FLASH with function declarations calculate_cutting(process, material, toolMaterial, D, z, Vc, feed, ap, ae, machineMaxKw), get_material(material), verify_gcode(program, controller). Execute calls with the engines, return results, get the draft.\n  Step 2: if the question or image concerns alarms, parameters, programming or maintenance, call MODEL_FLASH again with the File Search tool on config/app.fileSearchStoreName, metadata filter controller = selected controller OR \"generic\", and produce the final grounded answer with citations.\n  Save both messages to Firestore, write an activity row, return {answer, citations, toolCalls, transcript?}.\n\n## Route \"/calculator\": Cutting Calculator\n- Desktop: left inputs w-[400px] + right results. Mobile: stacked.\n- Inputs: process tabs Milling / Turning / Drilling / Tapping / Boring; material and tool material dropdowns; number inputs with +/- steppers; sliders for Vc (green band = recommended range for the material and tool material), fz or fn, ap, ae; machine max kW; units toggle mm / inch. Inline validation in red, e.g. \"Above recommended HSS speed for this material\".\n- Results update live: 3D viewport (cylinder tool spinning at a speed proportional to rpm above a box, grid, axis triad); metric cards in JetBrains Mono 32px bold: spindle speed, feed rate, MRR, torque, cycle time, plus Ra for turning and thrust for drilling; horizontal power gauge kW vs machine max with green / amber / red; warnings list.\n- \"Ask Copilot why\" (requires sign-in): POST /api/explain with inputs and results. MODEL_FLASH prompt: \"You are a senior CNC process engineer. Explain these cutting parameters to a machine operator in under 120 words. Do not change or recompute any number. Flag risks: power above 80% of machine limit, Vc outside the recommended band, deep holes, long overhang. Answer in {language}.\" Show in a side drawer. Write an activity row.\n\n## Route \"/gcode\": G-code Verifier\n- Desktop: editor 45% left, 3D backplot 55% right, findings below the editor. Mobile: 3D on top, editor, then findings.\n- Editor: dark, line numbers, syntax colors (G codes cyan, M codes orange, coordinates white, comments muted), active line with cyan left border. Toolbar: Upload .nc/.txt, Load sample, controller dropdown, Verify (orange).\n- Backplot: OrbitControls, rapids red dashed, feeds green, arcs blue, grid, axis triad, auto-fit camera; scrub slider moves a tool marker and highlights the matching editor line.\n- Deterministic findings appear instantly on Verify. Then POST /api/gcode-review sends program, controller and findings to MODEL_PRO: \"You are a senior CNC programmer for {controller}. The deterministic checker found: {findings}. Explain each issue plainly for an operator, give the corrected code lines, and list any additional risks. Do not contradict the checker; you may add issues. Reply in {language}.\" Each finding\'s \"Explain\" button expands its part of the answer. Write an activity row.\n- Load sample inserts exactly:\nO1001 (FACE AND POCKET DEMO)\nG21 G17 G90 G40 G80\nT01 M06 (D10 ENDMILL)\nG54 G00 X0 Y0\nS3000 M03\nG00 Z-2.0 X20 Y10\nG01 Z-3.0 F300\nG01 X60 Y10\nG02 X60 Y40 R15\nG01 X20 Y40\nG01 X20 Y10\nG00 Z50\nM05\nM30\nExpected result: CRITICAL NO_G43 and CRITICAL RAPID_PLUNGE, both on line 6.\n\n## Route \"/academy\": Crash Lab\n- Top bar: level badge (0-199 xp \"Trainee\", 200-399 \"Operator\", 400+ \"Setter\"), XP progress bar, streak counter (flame icon), badge shelf.\n- Mission map: vertical game-style path of 4 nodes; completed green, current pulsing orange, locked grey with padlock. Mission N+1 unlocks when mission N is passed.\n- Mission view: Desktop 3 columns (brief + editor | 3D machine scene | Instructor panel); mobile stacked (brief, 3D, editor, instructor).\n- 3D scene uses the fixed scene from 4.3: table, vise, stock, spindle and end mill that follows the toolpath during \"Run simulation\".\n- On a crash event: stop playback at the event position, flash the hit object red, shake the camera 0.4 s, play a short metallic sound (Web Audio API generated noise burst, no audio files), show the damage card (part, repair cost INR, downtime days) and a \"Rewind and fix\" button.\n- Pass condition: zero crash events AND zero CRITICAL findings from 4.2. Then green safe run, \"+{xp} XP\", badge unlock animation, \"Next mission\".\n- Missions (src/academy/missions.ts). Every program has exactly one fault; everything else is correct (G43 H01 present, spindle on, safe approach):\n  1 \"The Missing Offset\", 100 xp, badge \"Offset Master\": the O1001 sample with line 6 replaced by \"G00 X20 Y10\" and \"G00 Z2.0\", and without any G43. Fix: add \"G43 H01 Z50\" after \"S3000 M03\".\n  2 \"Rapid Into Stock\", 120 xp, badge \"Safe Approach\": correct program with G43 H01 Z50, but one block \"G00 X20 Y10 Z-2.0\". Fix: rapid to X20 Y10 and Z2.0, then G01 Z-2.0 F300.\n  3 \"Stripped Tap\", 150 xp, badge \"Tap Whisperer\": M10x1.5 rigid tapping, \"(M10x1.5)\" comment, S500, G84 with F600. Fix: F750.\n  4 \"Dead Spindle\", 100 xp, badge \"Safe Starter\": \"M05\" active before the first cut instead of \"M03\". Fix: M03.\n- Instructor panel: robot-machinist avatar, chat messages, \"Hint\" button showing \"Hint n of 3\", mic button (same audio flow as the agent).\n- POST /api/instructor {missionId, program, crashEvent, hintLevel, language, question?} to MODEL_FLASH: \"You are a patient CNC instructor training a new operator. The simulator detected: {crashEvent}. Give hint level {n} of 3 only. Level 1: a guiding question. Level 2: point to the line and the concept. Level 3: show the single corrected line. Never give the full program. If the learner has passed, explain in 3 sentences what would happen on a real machine and one habit that prevents it. Reply in {language}.\"\n- XP awarded = mission xp x (1 - 0.2 x hintsUsed), minimum 0. Streak +1 when a mission is completed on a new calendar day. Progress saved to users/{uid}/academy/progress through POST /api/academy/complete (server recomputes pass status with the engines; the client cannot set XP).\n- Admin card at the top (admins only): learners count, missions completed, average crashes before pass, most common crash type, computed from all academy progress docs by GET /api/academy/stats.\n\n## Route \"/kb\": Knowledge Base (admin only; non-admins are redirected to /)\n- Header \"Knowledge Base\", search, filters (controller, type), \"Upload document\" (orange).\n- Drop zone (dashed border, UploadCloud icon): \"Drop PDF, DOCX, XLSX, CSV, PNG or JPG. Upload only documents you own or are licensed to use.\" Controller and document type selectors are required before upload.\n- Table from kb_docs: name, controller, type, pages, status (Indexing with spinning Loader icon, Ready green, Failed red), date, actions (delete). Empty state when none.\n- POST /api/kb/upload (multipart, max 50 MB): save to Storage manuals/{docId}/{filename}, create kb_docs with status Indexing, import into the File Search store with custom metadata controller and docType, poll the operation, then set Ready (or Failed with the error).\n- On server start: if config/app.fileSearchStoreName is empty, create a File Search store named \"cnc-copilot-manuals\" and save its name there.\n- Right sidebar \"Test retrieval\": input box; POST /api/kb/test runs a File Search query and shows the real top 3 passages with document, page and snippet. Show a relevance score only if the API returns one.\n\n# 6. VOICE AND LANGUAGE\n- Voice input: MediaRecorder (audio/webm;codecs=opus) to base64, sent to /api/agent or /api/instructor.\n- POST /api/tts {messageId, text, language}: MODEL_TTS generates audio; cache it in Storage tts/{messageId}_{language} and return a short-lived signed URL; repeat plays reuse the cached file.\n- Languages en, hi, ml, ta. UI labels stay English. Every Gemini prompt receives the selected language and answers in it.\n\n# 7. BUILD ORDER\nBuild in milestones. After each milestone, stop, list the files created or changed, and give me a 3-step manual test for the preview.\nMilestone 1: project structure, design system, navigation, Firebase Auth sign-in, landing page, dashboard, server with token middleware, rate limiter, /api/health.\nMilestone 2: cutting engine + /calculator + /api/explain.\nMilestone 3: /agent with /api/agent (function calling, image, audio), chat history, feedback.\nMilestone 4: /kb, File Search store, upload, test retrieval, and step 2 grounding in /api/agent.\nMilestone 5: G-code engine + /gcode + backplot + /api/gcode-review.\nMilestone 6: crash engine + /academy + /api/instructor + progress + stats.\nMilestone 7: /api/tts, Firestore and Storage rules, error and empty states, mobile check at 375 px.\nStart with Milestone 1 now."
    user_requests: "Firebase terms accepted, continue setting up database.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: true\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "Fix the errors in the app\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nfix_it_trigger: manual\nerror 0: Google Sign In failed: FirebaseError: Firebase: Error (auth/popup-closed-by-user).\n    at createErrorInternal (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:435:35)\n    at _createError (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:411:9)\n    at https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:8063:18\nerror 1: FirebaseError: Firebase: Error (auth/popup-closed-by-user).\n    at createErrorInternal (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:435:35)\n    at _createError (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:411:9)\n    at https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:8063:18\nerror 2: [authMiddleware] Firestore get user warning: Error: 7 PERMISSION_DENIED: Missing or insufficient permissions.\nerror 3: Caused by: Error\nerror 4: [authMiddleware] Could not write user doc: Error: 7 PERMISSION_DENIED: Missing or insufficient permissions.\nerror 5: note: \'Exception occurred in retry method that was not classified as transient\'\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "The attached DESIGN.md and operator_dashboard/code.html are the single source of truth for all visual design. Redo the signed-in Operator Dashboard so it matches operator_dashboard/code.html as closely as possible: same layout grid, section order, card structure, colored top borders on the quick-action cards, Material Symbols Outlined icons, M3 color tokens from the Tailwind config in that file (surface-container-lowest, surface-container, primary-container #FF7A1A, secondary #5DE6FF etc.), 12px cards, 8px controls, 4px square badges, JetBrains Mono for all numbers and labels, glow on active attention elements. Replace lucide icons with Material Symbols Outlined across the app. Move these tokens into tailwind.config so every screen uses them.\n\nKeep the data rule: no invented machine data. Map every Stitch panel to real data exactly like this:\n1. Alert banner: show only when the user\'s latest activity of type \"chat\" in the last 24 h has an alarm code; text \"Last diagnosis: {alarm} on {controller}. {title}\", button \"Continue\" opens that chat. Otherwise hide it.\n2. Greeting block: \"Good morning/afternoon/evening, {firstName}\", live date, computed shift (Shift 1 06:00-14:00, Shift 2 14:00-22:00, Shift 3 22:00-06:00), and the user\'s preferredController instead of a machine name.\n3. The 4 stat chips: \"Questions today\", \"Calculations today\", \"Programs verified today\" (counts of users/{uid}/activity by type with createdAt today) and the Crash Lab chip with real XP and level linking to /academy.\n4. Quick action cards: Diagnose Alarm, Calculate Feeds, Verify G-code, Knowledge Base (admins only), Academy Crash Lab. Same styling as the HTML.\n5. Replace \"Kinematic Telemetry & Spindle Load Curve\" with \"Copilot Activity, last 7 days\": an SVG area chart in the same cyan style showing daily activity counts from users/{uid}/activity, and 4 readouts below: total chats, total calculations, programs verified, Crash Lab crashes avoided (missions passed). Show zeros, never invented numbers.\n6. Replace \"Chamber Enclosure CAM\" with \"Last screen snapshot\": the most recent imageUrl from the user\'s agent messages, shown through a short-lived signed URL from the server, with the alarm text Gemini extracted as the caption. Empty state: \"Snap a controller screen in the Agent to diagnose it.\" with a button to /agent.\n7. Recent Activity & Shop Logs: real activity rows in the same row design; the tabs All / Calculations / Alarms / Simulations filter by type.\n8. Pinned Manuals & Shop Standards: real kb_docs with status Ready in the same card design; \"+ Pin manual\" goes to /kb for admins and is hidden for users.\n9. Footer: \"CNC Copilot | Built for Google Cloud AI Builder Cup 2026\" left, app version right.\nAlso match the top navigation bar from the HTML (logo block, tab style, active tab, controller selector, avatar), but remove \"Shop Net: Haas VF-2 ONLINE\" and use the controller selector Fanuc / Mitsubishi / Generic plus the language selector.\nDo not change any server logic, auth, rate limiting or Firestore rules. List the files you changed."
    user_requests: "Attached is the Stitch HTML for this screen. Match its layout, components, classes and tokens exactly, using DESIGN.md. Replace every hard-coded value, name, machine, session or statistic in it with real data or a designed empty state, following the real-data rules already given. Never show a machine status, telemetry value or operator name the app does not actually have."
