    thinking: "**Examining Auth Middleware**\n\nI\'m currently looking closely at `server/authMiddleware.ts`, specifically the Firebase user document synchronization. I\'m focusing on the \"best-effort\" approach, and the fallback mechanism if the admin service account lacks write permissions. I want to understand how this handles potential write failures gracefully and efficiently. I will next look at `server/routes/user.ts`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Permission Handling**\n\nI\'ve examined the permission denial handling in `authMiddleware.ts` and noted the graceful fallback strategy. Instead of logging alarming errors or crashing on `PERMISSION_DENIED`, a `catch` block prevents that, because role-based access control and ID token verification already provide security. I\'ve also identified several image and HTML files to review, specifically `Image 2.html`, `Image 4.html`, `Image 6.html`, `Image 8.html`, `Image 11.html`, `Image 12.html`, `Image 14.html`, and `Image 15.markdown`, and am trying to locate them based on the compaction summary.\n\n\n"
