  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Server Status**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the full-stack server is operational. It returned a clean \"ok\" status, along with the application details including the tagline and Firebase project information. This establishes a baseline; the server is up and responding as expected.\n\n\n**Analyzing Design Consistency**\n\nI\'m now focused on achieving full consistency with the provided DESIGN.md and the operator_dashboard/code.html. I need to ensure every element, class, and token is perfectly aligned. It\'s a meticulous process, but I\'m replacing all hardcoded values with either real data or appropriate empty states and adhering to the data rules. I\'m paying very close attention to layout, section order, and those crucial Material Symbols Outlined icons and M3 color tokens to create a perfect match.\n\n\n**Refining UI Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing specific UI details. I\'m focusing on those 4px badges, using JetBrains Mono for all numbers and labels and applying a glow to active attention elements. All Lucide icons are being replaced with Material Symbols Outlined, and these new tokens are going into `tailwind.config` to maintain consistency. I\'m making sure to map all Stitch panels to real data. Specifically, I am updating the alert banner, greeting block, stat chips, and quick action cards.\n\n\n**Implementing Data-Driven Widgets**\n\nI\'m now integrating data into specific widgets. I\'m swapping out the hardcoded content with real data and dynamically displaying user activity, crash lab stats, and last screen snapshots, complete with captions extracted by Gemini. I\'m focusing on the SVG area chart for daily activity and ensuring that the data readouts accurately reflect actual values, never invented ones. I\'m paying close attention to filtering options within recent activity and shop logs, along with data-driven manual pinning. I am matching the Stitch HTML for the screen.\n\n\n**Matching HTML and Design**\n\nI\'m now carefully aligning the Stitch HTML with DESIGN.md to achieve a pixel-perfect match. I\'m focusing on ensuring all components, classes, and tokens are perfectly consistent. The challenge is replacing every hardcoded value with real data or appropriate empty states, always adhering to the data rules. I\'m committed to never displaying any data the app doesn\'t actually possess, which means there may be gaps until data is available.\n\n\n**Mapping App Screens**\n\nI\'m now mapping the incoming Stitch HTML files to the current application screens. I have a clearer picture now, and can see the new files relate to the Shopfloor Agent, G-code Verifier, Academy Crash Lab, and Knowledge Base screens, in addition to an operator Dashboard and cutting calculator. I\'ve updated my mental map of the application\'s structure.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
