    thinking: "**Analyzing Shopfloor Agent**\n\nI\'ve got the Shopfloor Agent screen\'s HTML from Stitch! I see this is the \"agent\" console. I\'m focusing on the layout. It\'s using the standard persistent header as the rest of the app, just Dashboard, Shopfloor Agent.\n\n\n**Examining Side Panel**\n\nI\'m now diving into the agent\'s left sidebar. It seems to be a full-width section on smaller screens that collapses to a width of 80px on larger displays, employing flexbox for layout and content arrangement. I see a persistent header with a \"New Session\" button and a search input. The chat history stream, dynamically populated from Firestore, presents diagnostic sessions.\n\n\n**Reviewing Main Display**\n\nI\'m now investigating the main display, the interactive diagnostic stream. The Telemetry Header Bar is clear - a live ping indicator, title, and diagnostic badge are present. I\'m noting the export and clear conversation options. The message history container with date/mode separators is also in focus. I see \"SESSION INITIALIZED \342\200\242 KINEMATIC STREAM SYNC\" as a start.\n\n\n**Detailing Message Structures**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the message structures within the chat stream. I\'ve confirmed that messages are sourced from `Firestore` under `users/{uid}/chats/{chatId}/messages`. If the chat is empty, an empty state is shown, which features some helpful quick prompts such as \"Snap controller alarm screen\" that triggers the camera, or \"Calculate feeds & speeds for 6061-T6\". Operator messages are right-aligned, including header details like name and shift, with image thumbnails if available. AI agent responses are left-aligned with identifying agent information and a diagnostic panel.\n\n\n**Dissecting Diagnostic Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the detailed components within the AI agent\'s responses. I\'m seeing the breakdown: diagnostic summaries (root cause/fault confidence), operational checklists with numbered steps, and relevant citations (manual pages, bulletins). There\'s also a physics reasoning chain section, and the composer area with a rich text input with camera upload.\n\n\n"
