ing\":\"**Analyzing Write Permissions**\\n\\nI\'m currently investigating whether a client can directly write to `users/{uid}/activity` even when the server\'s Firestore admin account lacks write access. I\'m focusing on the `firestore.rules` file to understand the access control logic related to the `/activity/{activityId}` path.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Database Permissions**\\n\\nI\'m now tracing the root cause of the `PERMISSION_DENIED` error encountered by the server when writing to the database. I\'ve cross-referenced database IDs in `firebase.ts` and `firebase-applet-config.json`. My focus has shifted to IAM roles of the Cloud Run service account, questioning its permissions. The client-side rules are also being re-examined in the `/activity/{activityId}` path for any potential vulnerabilities.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Allow user to create their own activity and academy progress in firestore.rules\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"45\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update firestore.rules to allow isOwner for activity and academy subcollections\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"      match /activity/{activityId} {\\\\n        allow read, create: if isOwner(uid);\\\\n        allow update, delete: if false;\\\\n      }\\\\n\\\\n      match /academy/{docId} {\\\\n        allow read, write: if isOwner(uid);\\\\n      }\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"36\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"      match /activity/{activityId} {\\\\n        allow read: if isOwner(uid);\\\\n        allow write: if false; // Written by server only\\\\n      }\\\\n\\\\n      match /academy/{docId} {\\\\n        allow read: if isOwner(uid);\\\\n        allow write: if false; // Progre\\n<truncated 48 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update firestore.rules permissions\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":285,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:28:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":3314,\"cache_read_tokens\":114384,\"output_tokens\":51,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"deploy_firebase\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Deploying firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Deploy updated firestore rules\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":287,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:28:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":2228,\"cache_read_tokens\":115598,\"output_tokens\":199,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Client-Side Writes**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed the Firestore rules are live! My next task is to meticulously examine `CuttingCalculator.tsx`. I need to verify that all calculation executions and explanations are correctly writing user activity data to `users/{uid}/activity` via client-side Firestore operations. This is crucial for user tracking.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"135\",\"StartLine\":\"90\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing handleAskCopilot in CuttingCalculator\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check handleAskCopilot\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":289,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:28:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":3117,\"cache_read_tokens\":115781,\"output_tokens\":475,\"thinking\":\"**Logging User Activity**\\n\\nI\'ve decided to log user activity to Firestore. Specifically, when the user clicks \\\"Calculate Physics Engine\\\" (line 645 in `CuttingCalculator.tsx`) or triggers `handleAskCopilot`, I\'ll use `addDoc` to add a record to the `users/{uid}/activity` collection. This should give us good insight into how the user interacts with the app, right?\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"20\",\"StartLine\":