artLine\":\"276\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"            <span className=\\\\\\\"block font-bold text-primary-container mb-0.5\\\\\\\">Gemini 2.5</span>\\\\n            <span className=\\\\\\\"text-[10px] text-tertiary\\\\\\\">Flash & Pro</span>\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/LandingPage.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating LandingPage model badge\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update model badge to Gemini 3.8\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":338,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:38:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2807,\"cache_read_tokens\":153404,\"output_tokens\":47,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting codebase\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check typescript compilation\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":340,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:39:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":2245,\"cache_read_tokens\":154114,\"output_tokens\":40,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Verify build\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":342,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:39:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":2218,\"cache_read_tokens\":154263,\"output_tokens\":67,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server with new Gemini config\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":344,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:39:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":2242,\"cache_read_tokens\":154385,\"output_tokens\":109,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/health\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking health status\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Health check test\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":346,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:39:19Z\",\"input_tokens\":2329,\"cache_read_tokens\":154530,\"output_tokens\":89,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598/task-345\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking task status\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check health task output\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":349,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:39:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":2552,\"cache_read_tokens\":154758,\"output_tokens\":539,\"content\":\"I have resolved the error by updating the Gemini AI model configuration:\\n\\n### Cause\\nThe endpoint was querying `gemini-2.5-flash`, which is no longer available to new users and returned a `404 NOT_FOUND` status from the Gemini API, triggering the fallback retry handler and displaying the high-load error message.\\n\\n### Fix\\n1. **Model Upgrade in `/server/config.ts`**:\\n   - `MODEL_FLASH` updated to `\'gemini-3.8-flash\'`.\\n   - `MODEL_PRO` updated to `\'gemini-3.8-flash\'`.\\n   - `MODEL_TTS` updated to `\'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'`.\\n2. **Client Header Configuration in `/server/geminiClient.ts`**:\\n   - Initialized `GoogleGenAI` with `httpOptions: { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\' } }` matching SDK recommendations.\\n3. **Verified Build & Server**:\\n   - TypeScript lint passed with zero errors (`tsc --noEmit`).\\n   - Applet compiled successfully and the dev server has been restarted. Cutting parameter explanations via Copilot now use `gemini-3.8-flash`.\",\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Availability**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed the server is operational. The crucial issue now is model availability; I\'m grappling with a 404 error indicating the specified Gemini model is deprecated and not accessible to new users. I\'m focusing on updating the code to work with the updated model, namely models/gemini-3.8.\\n\\n\\n\"}\n{\"step_index\":330,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:41:04Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nAttached is the Stitch HTML for this screen. Match its layout, components, classes and tokens exactly, using DESIGN.md. Replace every hard-coded value, name, machine, session or statistic in it with real data or a designed empty state, following the real-data rules already given. Never show a machine status, telemetry value or operator name the app does not actually have.\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-16T01:41:04-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nUser Email: biju0716@gmail.com\\nThe user\'s firestore db is ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598 and you must always load the firebase skill when processing queries that require interacting with the database or Firebase services.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"code.html\"}]}\n{\"step_index\":331,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T08:41:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":138494,\"cache_read_tokens\":18822,\"output_tokens\":1544,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Shopfloor Agent**\\n\\nI\'ve got the Shopfloor Agent screen\'s HTML from Stitch! I see this is the \\\"agent\\\" console. I\'m focusing on the layout. It\'s using the standard persistent header as the rest of the app, just Dashboard, Shopfloor Agent.\\n\\n\\n**Examining Side Panel**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the agent\'s left sidebar. It seems to be a full-width section on smaller screens that collapses to a width of 80px on larger displays, employing flexbox for layout and content arrangement. I see a persistent header \\n<truncated 1054 bytes>\\nf available. AI agent responses are left-aligned with identifying agent information and a diagnostic panel.\\n\\n\\n**Dissecting Diagnostic Elements**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the detailed components within the AI agent\'s responses. I\'m seeing the breakdown: diagnostic summaries (root cause/fault confidence), operational checklists with numbered steps, and relevant citations (manual pages, bulletins). There\'s also a physics reasoning chain section, and the composer area with a rich text input with camera upload.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/server/routes\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing server routes\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check existing server routes\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}"
    included_step_index_start: 187
    included_step_index_end: 333
    model_summarization_failed: true
    used_fallback_summary: true
    user_requests: "Fix the errors in the app\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nfix_it_trigger: manual\nerror 0: Google Sign In failed: FirebaseError: Firebase: Error (auth/popup-closed-by-user).\n    at createErrorInternal (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:435:35)\n    at _createError (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:411:9)\n    at https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:8063:18\nerror 1: FirebaseError: Firebase: Error (auth/popup-closed-by-user).\n    at createErrorInternal (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:435:35)\n    at _createError (https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:411:9)\n    at https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/firebase_auth.js?v=dae3b7d6:8063:18\nerror 2: [authMiddleware] Firestore get user warning: Error: 7 PERMISSION_DENIED: Missing or insufficient permissions.\nerror 3: Caused by: Error\nerror 4: [authMiddleware] Could not write user doc: Error: 7 PERMISSION_DENIED: Missing or insufficient permissions.\nerror 5: note: \'Exception occurred in retry method that was not classified as transient\'\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "The attached DESIGN.md and operator_dashboard/code.html are the single source of truth for all visual design. Redo the signed-in Operator Dashboard so it matches operator_dashboard/code.html as closely as possible: same layout grid, section order, card structure, colored top borders on the quick-action cards, Material Symbols Outlined icons, M3 color tokens from the Tailwind config in that file (surface-container-lowest, surface-container, primary-container #FF7A1A, secondary #5DE6FF etc.), 12px cards, 8px controls, 4px square badges, JetBrains Mono for all numbers and labels, glow on active attention elements. Replace lucide icons with Material Symbols Outlined across the app. Move these tokens into tailwind.config so every screen uses them.\n\nKeep the data rule: no invented machine data. Map every Stitch panel to real data exactly like this:\n1. Alert banner: show only when the user\'s latest activity of type \"chat\" in the last 24 h has an alarm code; text \"Last diagnosis: {alarm} on {controller}. {title}\", button \"Continue\" opens that chat. Otherwise hide it.\n2. Greeting block: \"Good morning/afternoon/evening, {firstName}\", live date, computed shift (Shift 1 06:00-14:00, Shift 2 14:00-22:00, Shift 3 22:00-06:00), and the user\'s preferredController instead of a machine name.\n3. The 4 stat chips: \"Questions today\", \"Calculations today\", \"Programs verified today\" (counts of users/{uid}/activity by type with createdAt today) and the Crash Lab chip with real XP and level linking to /academy.\n4. Quick action cards: Diagnose Alarm, Calculate Feeds, Verify G-code, Knowledge Base (admins only), Academy Crash Lab. Same styling as the HTML.\n5. Replace \"Kinematic Telemetry & Spindle Load Curve\" with \"Copilot Activity, last 7 days\": an SVG area chart in the same cyan style showing daily activity counts from users/{uid}/activity, and 4 readouts below: total chats, total calculations, programs verified, Crash Lab crashes avoided (missions passed). Show zeros, never invented numbers.\n6. Replace \"Chamber Enclosure CAM\" with \"Last screen snapshot\": the most recent imageUrl from the user\'s agent messages, shown through a short-lived signed URL from the server, with the alarm text Gemini extracted as the caption. Empty state: \"Snap a controller screen in the Agent to diagnose it.\" with a button to /agent.\n7. Recent Activity & Shop Logs: real activity rows in the same row design; the tabs All / Calculations / Alarms / Simulations filter by type.\n8. Pinned Manuals & Shop Standards: real kb_docs with status Ready in the same card design; \"+ Pin manual\" goes to /kb for admins and is hidden for users.\n9. Footer: \"CNC Copilot | Built for Google Cloud AI Builder Cup 2026\" left, app version right.\nAlso match the top navigation bar from the HTML (logo block, tab style, active tab, controller selector, avatar), but remove \"Shop Net: Haas VF-2 ONLINE\" and use the controller selector Fanuc / Mitsubishi / Generic plus the language selector.\nDo not change any server logic, auth, rate limiting or Firestore rules. List the files you changed."
