  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing CSS and HTML**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the token definitions are in `src/index.css`. I\'m now taking a close look at the provided HTML, specifically the title and the `Main` section. I\'ve noted the presence of the Top Stats & Metric Banner with its four columns, including the first card\'s \"INDEX\" header, to analyze the structure.\n\n\n**Reviewing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI components within the HTML, focusing specifically on the data cards within the \"Top Stats & Metric Banner.\" I\'ve identified the specific data points displayed in the banner, including the headers (\"ED DOCUMENTS\", \"VECTOR EMBEDDINGS\", \"AVG RETRIEVAL LATENCY\", and \"OCR & PARSING ACCURACY\"), their corresponding values, and subtext. I also noted the presence of progress bars with distinct background color classes like `bg-secondary`, `bg-primary-container`, and `bg-tertiary`.\n\n\n**Examining Page Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on the page\'s structure using the provided code. The left column, spanning a larger width on larger screens (`lg:col-span-8`), contains the core content, including badges, the title, and a descriptive paragraph. The action controls bar, which houses the search input, is also under analysis. Its responsive design with different layouts for different screen sizes is of particular interest.\n\n\n**Dissecting Search Controls**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the action controls bar. I\'ve dissected the search input element, noting its `doc-search-input` ID, placeholder text, and functionality. I\'ve analyzed the filter dropdowns for controllers and document types, understanding their selectable options. I\'m also examining the \"Upload Manual\" CTA button, specifically its styling, ID, and associated upload functionality, and the container for the upload drop zone.\n\n\n**Investigating Upload Functionality**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the upload component. I\'ve noted the styling of the upload icon circle, its dimensions, background, and hover effects. I\'ve also parsed the heading and subtext associated with the drag-and-drop area, and I am parsing the hidden file input element and its role in triggering the upload flow. I also noted the shield-shaped note.\n\n\n**Parsing Data Rows**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the real data rows within the HTML table. I\'ve noted the structure of each cell, focusing on document names with icons and subtitles. I\'m also examining how controller badges, document types, pages, status indicators (ready and indexing states with their distinct styles), date added, and action elements are displayed and styled.\n\n\n**Examining Control Icons**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the action icons within each data row. Specifically, I\'m noting the \"Inspect Chunks\" button which triggers a modal, the \"Download Source\" button, and the \"Archive / Purge\" button.\n\nI\'m now focusing on the table pagination at the bottom, including the text \"Showing X to Y of Z technical documents\" and the pagination controls. Furthermore, I\'ve noted the empty state design for when filters yield zero results, ensuring it aligns with the system\'s aesthetic.\n\nI\'ve also examined the right column\'s design, which spans four columns on larger screens and employs a sticky layout for its content. I\'m focusing on the \"Simulator Glass Card.\" I\'m parsing its styling details, including its background color, padding, rounded corners, shadow, and overall structure. I am also paying attention to its absolute-positioned corner glow effect, and the title\'s icon and text color.\n\n\n**Analyzing Simulator Input**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"Simulator Glass Card\" in detail. I see the query input block, which features a label, textarea for prompts with a default example, and a bottom bar with customization options. I\'m focusing on the \"SIMULATE\" button\'s styling and functionality to understand how it triggers retrieval. The results header and retrieved chunks are under analysis, including the display of chunk titles, sections, match badges, and snippets.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
