    thinking: "**Considering API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently evaluating the potential for adding or supporting `/api/gcode/explain` within `server/routes/explain.ts`. However, I need to stay within the existing constraints and ensure that no changes are made to server logic, authentication, rate limiting, or Firestore rules. The only allowed output are the files I changed.\n\n\n**Analyzing G-code Verifier**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to designing the G-code verifier\'s UI components. I\'m exploring the provided Stitch HTML for layout inspiration, paying close attention to the title and KPI cards. I am considering the use of `src/components/verifier/GCodeVerifier.tsx` (or `src/components/GCodeVerifier.tsx`) to implement the component. The exact HTML structure and tokens are under review, especially the layout for the KPI cards: Status/Safety Score, Block Count, and Work Envelope Bounds.\n\n\n**Defining G-code Validator**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the specifics of the G-code validator. I need to include: kinematic rates like spindle RPM and feed rate, and a preset program selector with example CNC programs. A file upload feature is essential, supporting formats like .NC and .GCODE. I\'m also planning a live, interactive editor with syntax highlighting, line numbers, and issue markers for errors, with status pills. Finally, I\'m considering a 3D toolpath backplot using Three.js.\n\n\n**Visualizing Toolpaths**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the 3D toolpath visualizer. I envision using `OrbitControls` to display a stock workpiece and a G54 work origin triad. I\'ll represent rapid paths with amber dashed lines and cutting feed paths with cyan glowing lines. I\'m prioritizing smooth arc segment interpolation and an active tool tip indicator. View presets and playback controls are also on my list, including step back/forward, play/pause, and a block slider. I will be sure to consider a speed multiplier as well.\n\n\n"
