    thinking: "**Analyzing Navigation Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the navigation logic, specifically focusing on how the application routes to the \'agent\' tab. The code snippet from `Dashboard.tsx` uses `onNavigate` with a \'chatId\' parameter, which I\'m cross-referencing with the `App.tsx` file and its state management of `currentTab`. I\'m trying to trace how state changes influence the active view.\n\n\n**Investigating URL Routing**\n\nI\'m now digging into how the application handles direct URL navigation, particularly `/agent`. The `App.tsx` file initializes the `currentTab` to \'home\', irrespective of the URL path, meaning direct access to `/agent` results in a blank page. The current implementation doesn\'t appear to react to the URL in determining the initial state. I\'m reviewing how the application is mounted to determine how to resolve this.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve implemented a red `GlassPanel` that displays the error message, component stack, and filename on-screen when an error occurs, replacing the blank page. I\'ve also added `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers to show this panel for both types of errors. Now I need to review imports, package.json, and data loading.\n\n\n"
