    thinking: "**Analyzing App.tsx**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on `/agent` within `App.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m watching `App.tsx` and focusing on how it handles user authentication and tab state, especially the \"agent\" tab. I\'m noting the `useAuth()` hook for user info and the `useState` hook for tab management.\n\n\n**Addressing Agent Page Issues**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag with the blank agent page. My current task is pinpointing the root cause by implementing comprehensive error handling. I\'m focusing on error boundaries, `window.onerror`, and `unhandledrejection` handlers to capture and display errors with stack traces. Crucially, I\'m now examining all agent page imports for server-side code leaks. I\'ll also confirm all dependencies are correctly listed in `package.json`.\n\n\n**Investigating Routing Logic**\n\nI\'m now investigating the URL path synchronization with the `currentTab` state in `App.tsx`. Specifically, I noticed a discrepancy. If someone navigates directly to `/agent`, the initial `currentTab` is \'home\'. This mismatch means the \"agent\" content might not load as expected, particularly if the user is not yet authenticated. I need to make a fix! I\'m also pondering how to incorporate error boundaries to address this type of issue. The prompt is reminding me to wrap every route in a React ErrorBoundary.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focused on robust error handling for the `/agent` page. I will implement a red GlassPanel to display error messages, component stacks, and filenames in case of a crash. I\'ll also add `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers that display the same panel. My next step will be checking for server-only code imports in the `/agent` page and ensuring that they are removed from the client side. I\'m also ensuring that any needed packages are listed in `package.json`. Additionally, I will address the handling of empty or undefined chat data on the chat list and messages. It seems like I also need to make sure there actually IS a `/agent` page component.\n\n\n**Examining Agent Component**\n\nI\'m now investigating *why* the `/agent` page component isn\'t rendering as expected. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the conditional rendering logic within `App.tsx` and trying to determine why the placeholder content is showing. Is the `currentTab` state correctly reflecting the URL, and does the component exist? I need to verify that the agent component is being correctly imported and that the render path is functioning.\n\n\n**Confirming Instructions Alignment**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on ensuring full alignment with the user\'s instructions regarding the blank `/agent` page. I need to make sure I *only* address the five specific points: React ErrorBoundary wrapping, `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers, eliminating server-side code from the client, verifying `package.json` dependencies, and handling chat data. The previous error handling implementation needs to be revised to match these requirements. I\'m prioritizing the ErrorBoundary implementation right now, and will test after!\n\n\n**Verifying Component Loading**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on why the `/agent` page might be blank despite the explicit instructions. I\'ve re-examined the code, focusing on how `App.tsx` handles initial state and URL paths. I need to confirm the agent component actually *loads*, especially when navigating directly to `/agent`. If the `currentTab` state doesn\'t update, the agent component will not render. I\'m also ensuring the server serves the correct `index.html` file, even for a route like `/agent`. I will check what happens with an initial, empty chat state.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Tab State**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to synchronize the `currentTab` state in `App.tsx` with `window.location.pathname`. I\'ve added a `getTabFromPath` function and using `history.pushState` on navigation to maintain proper routing. The `popstate` event listener is now in place to update the tab when the URL changes. This should address the initial tab mismatch, ensuring the `/agent` component renders correctly on direct navigation or clicks. I am now updating `/` as well.\n\n\n**Addressing Authentication Concerns**\n\nI\'m now considering the `/agent` route behavior with an unauthenticated user. I see the code renders agent content if `currentTab` is \'agent\'. If navigation happens, I will handle the case of unauthenticated access. I will make the error handling match instructions from the user, addressing error boundaries, unhandled rejections, server code, package dependencies, and chat data.\n\n\n"
