  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Codebase Structure**\n\nI\'ve discovered that `Dashboard.tsx` is the sole file interacting with user chat data and messages in the existing system. The user also reported a blank /agent page and requested a priority focus on wrapping every route within a React ErrorBoundary to improve error handling, without adding further features.\n\n\n**Investigating `/agent` Route**\n\nI\'m now focused on the `/agent` route and why it was blank. I\'ve pinpointed that the `currentTab` variable in `App.tsx` was initially set to `\'home\'`, which would cause the component not to load when navigating directly to `/agent`. Further, I\'m examining how to render comprehensive error information on the client side. I\'m investigating how to capture the error in a red `GlassPanel`, including stack traces, file names, and the actual error message.\n\n\n**Examining `/agent` Logic**\n\nI\'m digging deeper into the login flow related to the `/agent` route. I\'ve realized that a logged-out user attempting to access `/agent` might be the root cause of the blank page, as opposed to the original assumption. I am now looking at the conditional rendering in `App.tsx` and how it handles user authentication to ensure the expected component is always displayed.\n\n\n**Clarifying Authentication Flow**\n\nI\'ve determined that the `/agent` route blankness wasn\'t just a component-level issue. The navigation bar\'s conditional rendering based on user authentication is the culprit. A logged-out user won\'t see the \"Shopfloor Agent\" link, and if they manually enter `/agent`, `App.tsx` might not interpret it correctly, leading to the `LandingPage` instead. The server simply serves `index.html`. I\'m now exploring how to synchronize `App.tsx` with `window.location.pathname` to prevent inconsistencies, regardless of login state.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the error handling strategy. I\'m focusing on wrapping every route within a React ErrorBoundary to display error details in a red `GlassPanel`, including stack traces and file names. I\'m also adding `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers. I\'m checking the `/agent` route for server-only code imports, and ensuring all its packages are listed in `package.json`. Additionally, I\'m checking the `/agent` chat list and messages for proper handling of empty or undefined data.\n\n\n**Searching for Message Usage**\n\nI\'m now searching the codebase for further uses of `chats` and `messages`. I\'ve examined `src/components/Dashboard.tsx` and identified lines 97-118, where data fetching from chats and messages occurs. This data includes fetching the last screen snapshot from recent messages across chats, which is interesting.\n\n\n**Refining Data Fetching**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving the error handling in data fetching, specifically around Firestore queries. I\'m concerned about cases where `chatsSnap` or `msgsSnap` might be undefined or empty, or where document fields like `updatedAt` or `m.data().imageUrl` are missing. I am making sure to add optional chaining throughout to safeguard against errors within data fetching and rendering logic. I also noticed that the `catch` block in the data fetching method was catching errors silently, which could be a source of future problems.\n\n\n**Addressing Potential TypeError**\n\nI\'ve found a critical bug in `Dashboard.tsx` related to how chat activity titles are handled. Specifically, line 168 might throw a TypeError if `latest.title` is undefined when trying to use `.match()`. This can happen if an activity has `type === \'chat\'` but lacks a title, crashing React and causing a blank page. I\'m now implementing optional chaining throughout this part of the codebase to prevent the error. I\'m also checking other instances where `a.title` and activities with `type === \'chat\'` are accessed in the code to make sure it doesn\'t happen again, particularly on line 179.\n\n\n**Reviewing Chat Interactions**\n\nI\'m now examining several instances of chat interaction within the codebase. I\'m focusing on potential undefined or null values that could lead to errors. I\'ve noted problematic access patterns in the code on lines 198, 260, 806, and 840, looking for ways to safely handle the absence of properties or data, and ensuring that the `/agent` route always renders correctly.\n\n\n**Investigating UI Navigation**\n\nI\'m now investigating navigation issues and checking the codebase for the presence of a dedicated Agent component. I have identified a section of code in `App.tsx` that appears to conditionally render an \"Shopfloor Agent\" link. Further, I will check the `/agent` route to ensure chat lists and messages correctly handle undefined or empty data, particularly for new users, to prevent display errors.\n\n\n**Examining `/agent` Implementation**\n\nI\'m now examining the actual implementation of the `/agent` route, given the user prompt\'s focus. I am now checking the use of `currentTab` in `App.tsx` and how it relates to the blank `/agent` page. I need to make sure the tab is set to correctly allow the agent to render. Then, I am looking at the chat list and messages to ensure they handle empty or undefined data on initial load. I need to find all the code related to those two, to fix the agent.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the requested fixes. I\'m rigorously implementing React ErrorBoundaries across all routes, ensuring a red `GlassPanel` displays error messages, component stacks, and filenames in the event of an error. I\'ve integrated `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers to provide this same level of error display across the entire application. I\'m methodically scrutinizing the `/agent` route for server-side code imports and ensuring all relevant packages are listed in `package.json`. Also, I am carefully reviewing the chat list and message handling, making sure that it can handle undefined or empty data, such as for new users, to prevent crashes. I\'m meticulously documenting all changes.\n\n\n**Designing Error UI**\n\nI\'m now designing the `RedGlassPanel` and `ErrorBoundary` components. The panel will display the error message, component stack, and filename, as requested. I\'ve analyzed error objects and stack traces to determine how to extract the filename from within them. Specifically, I\'m working on extracting the filename from the stack trace which can be done through using regex. I\'ll include the necessary `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers to show this panel globally.\n\n\n**Crafting Error Presentation**\n\nI\'m now deep in the design phase for the `RedGlassPanel` and `ErrorBoundary` components. I\'ve successfully identified methods to extract crucial error information, specifically utilizing regex from component stack traces for filenames and component names. I\'m also preparing to use `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` to gain access to error details. The `RedGlassPanel` UI is also being defined for visual clarity and information presentation, including a clear header, severity badge, and detailed sections for error information. I am preparing how the UI should look.\n\n\n**Defining Error Handler Location**\n\nI\'m now determining the most effective location for global error handlers. I\'m evaluating attaching them in `src/main.tsx` or through a top-level provider component, such as `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx` or wrapping them inside of `App.tsx`. I need to ensure that the handlers capture errors as broadly as possible. I\'m carefully considering how to integrate `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` to correctly display the UI. I also am deciding how the `GlobalErrorHandler` will integrate.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1293664"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React from \'react\';\\n\\nexport interface RedGlassPanelProps {\\n  errorMessage: string;\\n  componentStack?: string | null;\\n  fileName?: string | null;\\n  stack?: string | null;\\n  route?: string | null;\\n  onReset?: () => void;\\n  onNavigateHome?: () => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport function RedGlassPanel({\\n  errorMessage,\\n  componentStack,\\n  fileName,\\n  stack,\\n  route,\\n  onReset,\\n  onNavigateHome,\\n}: RedGlassPanelProps) {\\n  const [showFullStack, setShowFullStack] = React.useState(false);\\n\\n  // Extract a clean file name if full URL or path is present\\n  const displayFileName = React.useMemo(() => {\\n    if (!fileName) return \'Unknown Source File\';\\n    try {\\n      const clean = fileName.replace(/^https?:\\\\/\\\\/[^/]+/, \'\');\\n      return clean.startsWith(\'/\') ? clean.slice(1) : clean;\\n    } catch {\\n      return fileName;\\n    }\\n  }, [fileName]);\\n\\n  const handleReload = () => {\\n    window.location.reload();\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleGoHome = () => {\\n    if (onNavigateHome) {\\n      onNavigateHome();\\n    } else {\\n      window.location.href = \'/\';\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-8\\\">\\n      <div className=\\\"relative rounded-2xl bg-red-950/70 backdrop-blur-xl border border-red-500/50 shadow-[0_12px_40px_rgba(239,68,68,0.35)] overflow-hidden text-red-100 font-sans\\\">\\n        {/* Top Decorative Hazard Accent Stripe */}\\n        <div className=\\\"h-1.5 w-full bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 via-amber-500 to-red-600 animate-pulse\\\" />\\n\\n        <div className=\\\"p-6 sm:p-8 flex flex-col gap-6\\\">\\n          {/* Header Row */}\\n          <div className=\\\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 pb-4 border-b border-red-500/20\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-3\\\">\\n              <div className=\\\"w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-red-900/60 border border-red-400/40 flex items-center justify-center text-red-400 shadow-inner\\\">\\n                <span className=\\\"material-symbols-outlined text-[28px]\\\">crisis_alert</span>\\n              </div>\\n              <div>\\n                <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n                  <h2 className=\\\"font-headline-md text-lg font-bold text-red-100 tracking-tight\\\">\\n                    Route Runtime Exception\\n                  </h2>\\n                  <span className=\\\"px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-red-900/80 border border-red-400/50 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-red-300\\\">\\n                    Fault Intercepted\\n                  </span>\\n                </div>\\n                <p className=\\\"text-xs text-red-300/80 mt-0.5\\\">\\n                  {route ? `Caught while rendering route /${route}` : \'Caught by global exception boundary\'}\\n                </p>\\n              </div>\\n            </div>\\n\\n            {/* Action Buttons */}\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2 self-start sm:self-auto\\\">\\n              {onReset && (\\n                <button\\n                  type=\\\"button\\\"\\n                  onClick={onReset}\\n                  className=\\\"h-9 px-4 rounded-lg bg-red-900/60 hover:bg-red-800/80 border border-red-500/40 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-red-100 transition-colors cursor-pointer flex items-center gap-1.5 shadow-sm\\\"\\n                >\\n                  <span className=\\\"material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]\\\">refresh</span>\\n                  Retry Route\\n                </button>\\n              )}\\n              <button\\n                type=\\\"button\\\"\\n                onClick={handleGoHome}\\n                className=\\\"h-9 px-4 rounded-lg bg-red-500/20 hover:bg-red-500/30 border border-red-400/40 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-white transition-colors cursor-pointer flex items-center gap-1.5 shadow-sm\\\"\\n              >\\n                <span className=\\\"material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]\\\">home</span>\\n                Dashboard\\n              </button>\\n              <button\\n                type=\\\"button\\\"\\n                onClick={handleReload}\\n                className=\\\"h-9 px-3 rounded-lg bg-surface-container hover:bg-surface-container-high border border-outline-variant/30 text-xs font-mono text-tertiary transition-colors cursor-pointer flex items-center gap-1\\\"\\n                title=\\\"Hard Reload\\\"\\n              >\\n                <span className=\\\"material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]\\\">restart_alt</span>\\n              </button>\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Source File Banner */}\\n          <div className=\\\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"md:col-span-2 p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-black/40 border border-red-500/30 flex items-start gap-3\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"material-symbols-outlined text-red-400 text-[20px] mt-0.5\\\">description</span>\\n              <div className=\\\"flex flex-col min-w-0\\\">\\n                <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-red-400/80 font-bold\\\">\\n                  Originating Source File\\n                </span>\\n                <span className=\\\"text-xs font-mono font-bold text-red-200 truncate mt-0.5\\\" title={displayFileName}>\\n                  {displayFileName}\\n                </span>\\n              </div>\\n            </div>\\n\\n            <div className=\\\"p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-black/40 border border-red-500/30 flex items-start gap-3\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"material-symbols-outlined text-red-400 text-[20px] mt-0.5\\\">shield</span>\\n              <div className=\\\"flex flex-col min-w-0\\\">\\n                <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-red-400/80 font-bold\\\">\\n                  Status\\n                </span>\\n                <span className=\\\"text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-red-200 mt-0.5\\\">\\n                  Execution Halted (Zero Blank)\\n                </span>\\n              </div>\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Error Message Box */}\\n          <div className=\\\"flex flex-col gap-2\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-red-300/80 font-semibold flex items-center gap-1.5\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-red-400\\\" />\\n              Error Message\\n            </span>\\n            <div className=\\\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-red-950/80 border border-red-500/40 font-mono text-xs text-red-100 break-words leading-relaxed select-text shadow-inner\\\">\\n              {errorMessage || \'Unknown application error\'}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Component Stack & Call Stack */}\\n          <div className=\\\"flex flex-col gap-2\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center justify-between\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-red-300/80 font-semibold flex items-center gap-1.5\\\">\\n                <span className=\\\"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-red-400\\\" />\\n                Component & Call Stack\\n              </span>\\n              {(stack || componentStack) && (\\n                <button\\n                  type=\\\"button\\\"\\n                  onClick={() => setShowFullStack((prev) => !prev)}\\n                  className=\\\"text-[11px] font-mono text-red-300 hover:text-white underline cursor-pointer\\\"\\n                >\\n                  {showFullStack ? \'Collapse Stack\' : \'Expand Full Stack\'}\\n                </button>\\n              )}\\n            </div>\\n\\n            <div\\n              className={`p-4 rounded-xl bg-black/60 border border-red-500/30 font-mono text-[11px] text-red-200/90 overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre leading-relaxed select-text shadow-inner ${\\n                showFullStack ? \'max-h-[400px]\' : \'max-h-[160px]\'\\n              }`}\\n            >\\n              {componentStack ? (\\n                <>\\n                  <div className=\\\"text-red-400 font-bold mb-1\\\">// React Component Hierarchy:</div>\\n                  <div>{componentStack.trim()}</div>\\n                </>\\n              ) : null}\\n\\n              {stack ? (\\n                <>\\n                  <div className=\\\"text-red-400 font-bold mt-2 mb-1\\\">// Native JavaScript Stack:</div>\\n                  <div>{stack.trim()}</div>\\n                </>\\n              ) : null}\\n\\n              {!componentStack && !stack && (\\n                <div className=\\\"text-red-400/60 italic\\\">No stack trace available.</div>\\n              )}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create RedGlassPanel component for displaying runtime errors with error message, component stack, and file name\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/RedGlassPanel.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating RedGlassPanel.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create RedGlassPanel component\"}"
