  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the itemized summary of what was found and changed across the 5 requirements:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Route ErrorBoundaries with Red GlassPanel\n* **Created `src/components/RedGlassPanel.tsx`**:\n  - Implemented an industrial red GlassPanel (`bg-red-950/70 backdrop-blur-xl border border-red-500/50 text-red-100 shadow-[0_12px_40px_rgba(239,68,68,0.35)]`) displaying:\n    1. **Error Message**: Prominent, formatted error message box.\n    2. **Component Stack & Call Stack**: Interactive, expandable mono view of the React component hierarchy and JavaScript execution stack.\n    3. **Source File Name**: Extracted originating source file (e.g., `src/components/...` with line and column numbers).\n    4. **Action Controls**: \"Retry Route\", \"Dashboard\", and \"Hard Reload\" actions so the UI never locks up into a blank screen.\n* **Created `src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx`**:\n  - React class component implementing `componentDidCatch` and `getDerivedStateFromError`. Automatically extracts the source file name and stack information and renders `RedGlassPanel`.\n* **Wrapped Every Route in `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Wrapped `home`, `agent`, `calculator`, `gcode`, `academy`, and `kb` in route-level `<ErrorBoundary>`.\n  - Wrapped root application in `<ErrorBoundary route=\"root\">`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Global `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` Handlers\n* **Created `src/components/GlobalErrorHandler.tsx`**:\n  - Intercepts `window.onerror` and `window.addEventListener(\'unhandledrejection\')` at runtime, capturing any unhandled promise or async exceptions and rendering the red GlassPanel instead of allowing blank page unmounts.\n* **Hardened Bootstrap in `src/main.tsx`**:\n  - Added pre-mount DOM emergency handlers for `error` and `unhandledrejection` so that even if a fatal error occurs before React completes mounting, a red GlassPanel is immediately injected rather than leaving `#root` blank.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Server-Only Code Audit\n* Audited all client-side files in `src/`:\n  - **No client imports** of `@google/genai`, `firebase-admin`, `fs`, `path`, or files from `/server`.\n  - All AI and administrative operations are proxied through server routes (`/api/explain`, `/api/user/*`, `/api/health`). Client files only consume `/api/*` endpoints via `apiFetch`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Package Verification in `package.json`\n* Verified all dependencies:\n  - `react-markdown`: Listed (`^10.1.0`).\n  - `react` & `react-dom`: Listed (`^19.0.1`).\n  - `firebase`: Listed (`^13.0.0`).\n  - `motion`: Listed (`^12.23.24`).\n  - `lucide-react`: Listed (`^0.546.0`).\n  - `three`, `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`: Listed.\n  - Zero missing dependencies.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Chat List & Messages Undefined/Empty Data Handling\n* **Fixed `src/components/Dashboard.tsx` (`fetchLatestMessageSnapshot`)**:\n  - Added safety checks for `!user?.uid`, `!chatsSnap || chatsSnap.empty || !chatsSnap.docs`, and `!msgsSnap || msgsSnap.empty || !msgsSnap.docs` so first-time users with no chats or empty message subcollections never trigger unhandled rejections.\n  - Added safe optional chaining for image inspection (`m?.data?.()?.imageUrl`).\n* **Fixed `latestChatWithAlarm` in `src/components/Dashboard.tsx`**:\n  - Added defensive fallback `const titleStr = typeof latest.title === \'string\' ? latest.title : \'\'` to eliminate potential `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \'match\')` crashes when activity titles are undefined.\n  - Added `(activities || [])` fallback across all chat metrics and stat computations.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`): Passed with zero type or syntax errors.\n- `compile_applet` (`vite build`): Built and compiled successfully.\n- Dev server tested and confirmed returning `200 OK` on `/agent` and `/api/health`."
    modified_response: "Here is the itemized summary of what was found and changed across the 5 requirements:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Route ErrorBoundaries with Red GlassPanel\n* **Created `src/components/RedGlassPanel.tsx`**:\n  - Implemented an industrial red GlassPanel (`bg-red-950/70 backdrop-blur-xl border border-red-500/50 text-red-100 shadow-[0_12px_40px_rgba(239,68,68,0.35)]`) displaying:\n    1. **Error Message**: Prominent, formatted error message box.\n    2. **Component Stack & Call Stack**: Interactive, expandable mono view of the React component hierarchy and JavaScript execution stack.\n    3. **Source File Name**: Extracted originating source file (e.g., `src/components/...` with line and column numbers).\n    4. **Action Controls**: \"Retry Route\", \"Dashboard\", and \"Hard Reload\" actions so the UI never locks up into a blank screen.\n* **Created `src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx`**:\n  - React class component implementing `componentDidCatch` and `getDerivedStateFromError`. Automatically extracts the source file name and stack information and renders `RedGlassPanel`.\n* **Wrapped Every Route in `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Wrapped `home`, `agent`, `calculator`, `gcode`, `academy`, and `kb` in route-level `<ErrorBoundary>`.\n  - Wrapped root application in `<ErrorBoundary route=\"root\">`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Global `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` Handlers\n* **Created `src/components/GlobalErrorHandler.tsx`**:\n  - Intercepts `window.onerror` and `window.addEventListener(\'unhandledrejection\')` at runtime, capturing any unhandled promise or async exceptions and rendering the red GlassPanel instead of allowing blank page unmounts.\n* **Hardened Bootstrap in `src/main.tsx`**:\n  - Added pre-mount DOM emergency handlers for `error` and `unhandledrejection` so that even if a fatal error occurs before React completes mounting, a red GlassPanel is immediately injected rather than leaving `#root` blank.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Server-Only Code Audit\n* Audited all client-side files in `src/`:\n  - **No client imports** of `@google/genai`, `firebase-admin`, `fs`, `path`, or files from `/server`.\n  - All AI and administrative operations are proxied through server routes (`/api/explain`, `/api/user/*`, `/api/health`). Client files only consume `/api/*` endpoints via `apiFetch`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Package Verification in `package.json`\n* Verified all dependencies:\n  - `react-markdown`: Listed (`^10.1.0`).\n  - `react` & `react-dom`: Listed (`^19.0.1`).\n  - `firebase`: Listed (`^13.0.0`).\n  - `motion`: Listed (`^12.23.24`).\n  - `lucide-react`: Listed (`^0.546.0`).\n  - `three`, `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`: Listed.\n  - Zero missing dependencies.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Chat List & Messages Undefined/Empty Data Handling\n* **Fixed `src/components/Dashboard.tsx` (`fetchLatestMessageSnapshot`)**:\n  - Added safety checks for `!user?.uid`, `!chatsSnap || chatsSnap.empty || !chatsSnap.docs`, and `!msgsSnap || msgsSnap.empty || !msgsSnap.docs` so first-time users with no chats or empty message subcollections never trigger unhandled rejections.\n  - Added safe optional chaining for image inspection (`m?.data?.()?.imageUrl`).\n* **Fixed `latestChatWithAlarm` in `src/components/Dashboard.tsx`**:\n  - Added defensive fallback `const titleStr = typeof latest.title === \'string\' ? latest.title : \'\'` to eliminate potential `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \'match\')` crashes when activity titles are undefined.\n  - Added `(activities || [])` fallback across all chat metrics and stat computations.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`): Passed with zero type or syntax errors.\n- `compile_applet` (`vite build`): Built and compiled successfully.\n- Dev server tested and confirmed returning `200 OK` on `/agent` and `/api/health`."
