s\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Safely handle empty/undefined activities and title matching in Dashboard.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"201\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add defensive checks for latestChatWithAlarm and today stats\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  // Rule 1: Alert banner: show only when the user\'s latest activity of type \\\\\\\"chat\\\\\\\" in the last 24 h has an alarm code\\\\n  const latestChatWithAlarm = useMemo(() => {\\\\n    const chatActivities = (activities || []).filter((a) => a && a.type === \'chat\');\\\\n\\n<truncated 1142 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"176\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  // Rule 1: Alert banner: show only when the user\'s latest activity of type \\\\\\\"chat\\\\\\\" in the last 24 h has an alarm code\\\\n  const latestChatWithAlarm = useMemo(() => {\\\\n    const chatActivities = activities.filter((a) => a.type === \'chat\');\\\\n    if (!chat\\n<truncated 1007 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Dashboard.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating latestChatWithAlarm in Dashboard.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Defensive null safety in Dashboard.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":464,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:29:32Z\",\"input_tokens\":4203,\"cache_read_tokens\":98856,\"output_tokens\":100,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"110\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx for ErrorBoundary integration\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":466,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:29:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":4293,\"cache_read_tokens\":100696,\"output_tokens\":2163,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Application Structure**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the structural elements within `App.tsx`. I\'ve outlined key imports, including `ErrorBoundary` and `GlobalErrorHandler`. I\'m also adding a function called `getTabFromPath`, essential for navigation. I\'m aiming to refine the architecture by identifying and defining discrete components, essential for achieving the intended outcome.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { AuthProvider, useAuth } from \'./context/AuthContext.js\';\\\\nimport { Navigation } from \'./components/Navigation.js\';\\\\nimport { LandingPage } from \'./components/LandingPage.js\';\\\\nimport { Dashboar\\n<truncated 6858 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Wrap every route in React ErrorBoundary, connect GlobalErrorHandler, and synchronize URL pathname\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx with ErrorBoundaries and routing\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Wrap every route in ErrorBoundary\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":468,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:30:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":2455,\"cache_read_tokens\":104888,\"output_tokens\":2247,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Main Entry Point**\\n\\nI\'m now examining `src/main.tsx`, the application\'s entry point. I\'ve noted the use of `createRoot` from `react-dom/client`, the import of `App` component and `index.css`, and how the root element is targeted. This seems like a standard React setup for mounting the application, but I\'ll make sure it follows the conventions.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Error Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve decided to add an emergency pre-mount error handler. This will prevent a blank screen in case of fatal bootstrap i\\n<truncated 354 bytes>\\ns a modal with a red-themed design to grab attention. The error message will now be clearly visible, along with the source file and even a stack trace, if available, so I can more readily pinpoint issues