    thinking: "**Analyzing HMR Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `vite.config.ts` file, specifically the HMR configuration, and how it behaves with environment constraints. I\'m investigating how the `process.env.DISABLE_HMR` variable impacts WebSocket behavior when HMR is disabled in AI Studio or within an iframe context by Vite\'s client.\n\n\n**Investigating Test Connection**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to the `testConnection()` function within `src/lib/firebase.ts`. It seems to execute immediately upon module import, which feels unusual. I\'m focusing on the call to `getDocFromServer` and how it interacts with the Firestore rules that effectively prevent read/write operations. I\'m trying to see if this could be the source of the HMR or WebSocket connection problems.\n\n\n**Examining Unused Function**\n\nI\'ve discovered `testConnection()` is entirely unused throughout the application, raising questions about its purpose and potential impact. My focus has shifted to scrutinizing its necessity and whether its presence introduces any unforeseen complications. Further, I\'m now looking at the `AuthContext.tsx` file and examining how `apiFetch(\'/api/user/me\')` is used, and how it handles potential errors. I\'m trying to determine if errors there could be relevant. Finally, I\'ve re-read User Prompt 4.\n\n\n**Fixing Client Errors**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust error handling throughout the application. I\'m focusing on the `ErrorBoundary` approach for all routes to display comprehensive error information, including the component stack and file name, in a red GlassPanel. I\'m also adding `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers to ensure no errors slip through the cracks. Next, I\'m examining the `/agent` page imports to identify and eliminate any server-side code leakage, specifically focusing on modules like `@google/genai` or `firebase-admin`, that are causing the unhandled rejection. Finally, I\'m verifying that all `/agent` dependencies are correctly listed in `package.json`, and then making a fix.\n\n\n**Debugging Error Sources**\n\nI\'m now investigating the \"Client Runtime (Vite)\" error, focusing on how `extractFileNameFromStack` is used in `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx` and `ErrorBoundary.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the logic that determines the \'file\' property, aiming to understand why it\'s not correctly identifying the source file in this instance. I\'m also scrutinizing the stack trace parsing within `extractFileNameFromStack` to pinpoint potential areas of improvement or misinterpretation, and re-reading the relevant code. I am carefully re-reading the relevant code, and making sure that the error source can be easily identified.\n\n\n"
