9:37:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":3619,\"cache_read_tokens\":34006,\"output_tokens\":68,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/GlobalErrorHandler.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing GlobalErrorHandler.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View GlobalErrorHandler.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":362,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:37:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":3403,\"cache_read_tokens\":35568,\"output_tokens\":356,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Error Origins**\\n\\nI\'ve pinpointed a key error. Line 59 in `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx` logs an unhandled rejection, and I\'ve tied that to the metadata error in the user input. The error logs the `reason` as an empty object, but identifies the `file` as the \\\"Client Runtime (Vite)\\\". I now need to determine the cause of the unhandled promise rejection within the Vite environment.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":364,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:37:30Z\",\"input_tokens\":2848,\"cache_read_tokens\":39051,\"output_tokens\":68,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/lib/firebase.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing firebase.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View firebase.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":366,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:37:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":3390,\"cache_read_tokens\":39836,\"output_tokens\":357,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Connection Tests**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `testConnection` function within `src/lib/firebase.ts`. It appears the connection test simply attempts to fetch a document from the \'test\' collection. I\'m curious about the implications of a failed retrieval. What are the potential error states, and how are they handled in the application\'s overall error strategy?\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/context/AuthContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing AuthContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View AuthContext.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":368,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:37:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":2675,\"cache_read_tokens\":43291,\"output_tokens\":123,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing ErrorBoundary.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View ErrorBoundary.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":370,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:38:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":3868,\"cache_read_tokens\":43898,\"output_tokens\":421,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Error Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the error handling strategies implemented in the codebase. I just reviewed `ErrorBoundary.tsx` specifically lines 58, and `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx`, which seems to be the central point for managing unhandled promise rejections. I\'m focusing on how these components interact and ensure comprehensive error capture and reporting.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -rnE \\\\\\\"Promise|async|fetch|useEffect|onSnapshot\\\\\\\" src/\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching async code in src\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search async code in src\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":372,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:38:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":2608,\"cache_read_tokens\":45771,\"output_tokens\":97,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598/task-371\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking task 371\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check task 371\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":375,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:38:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":3600,\"cache_read_tokens\":46308,\"output_tokens\":116,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/LandingPage.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing LandingPage.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View LandingPage.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":377,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:38:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":4088,\"cache_read_tokens\":47837,\"output_tokens\":103,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Hero3DScene.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"120\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing Hero3DScene.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View Hero3DScene.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":379,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:38:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":3993,\"cache_read_tokens\":49855,\"output_tokens\":148,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing package.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View package.json\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":381,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:39:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":3064,\"cache_read_tokens\":51781,\"output_tokens\":48,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":383,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:39:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":2195,\"cache_read_tokens\":52780,\"output_tokens\":1133,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Error**\\n\\nI\'ve successfully compiled the applet. Now, I\'m carefully examining the precise error message returned by the prompt: \\\"[unhandledrejection caught]: {\\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Client Runtime (Vite)\\\\\\\"}.\\\" This \\\"unhandledrejection caught\\\" seems like a critical clue to diagnose the root cause of the problem.\\n\\n\\n**Tracing the Source**\\n\\nI\'ve traced the origin of the \\\"[unhandledrejection caught]:\\\" string to `src/components/GlobalErrorHandler.tsx`. The code logs this to the console and uses it\\n<truncated 831 bytes>\\n\\nI\'ve been meticulously examining the `main.tsx` file and realized that unhandled rejections are being treated as uncaught promise rejections in the browser runtime, if `event.preventDefault()` is not called! I\'m now exploring potential causes for the `event.reason`. Could it be related to Vite WebSocket errors or HMR issues? Specifically, I\'m considering the scenarios where the Vite client tries to connect to the Vite dev server\'s WebSocket `ws://...` within the AI Studio preview or iframe environments.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View firestore.rules\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":385,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:39:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":4124,\"cache_read_tokens\":53301,\"output_tokens\":506,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Security Rules**\\n\\nI see a problem in the Firebase rules. Access to `/test/connection` is explicitly denied. I am examining line 6, which disallows all reads and writes if unauthenticated, essentially blocking all access to the path `/test/connection`. Therefore, the request fails with a \\\"Missing\\\" error.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Access Denial**\\n\\nI\'ve been digging deeper. It seems the `testConnection` function in `src/lib/firebase.ts` attempts a read from \'test/connection\' upon app startup. Critically, it *doesn\'t* rethrow errors. I\'m wondering if a permission-denied error from `getDocFromServer` is being silently swallowed, preventing proper error propagation. I also see that the error message is often \'the client is offline\', which is a concern.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/KnowledgeBase.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"220\",\"StartLine\":\"180\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing KnowledgeBase.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View KnowledgeBase.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":387,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:39:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":3365,\"cache_read_tokens\":55500,\"output_tokens\":111,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -rn \\\\\\\"useEffect\\\\\\\" src/components/calculator/\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking calculator useEffects\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check calculator useEffects\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":389,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:39:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":2310,\"cache_read_tokens\":56778,\"output_tokens\":96,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598/task-388\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking task 388\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check task 388\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":392,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:39:47Z\",\"input_tokens\":2485,\"cache_read_tokens\":57000,\"output_tokens\":112,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/GCodeVerifier.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"