mation. My focus is on how the `handleUnhandledRejection` function in `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx` extracts and formats error details. I\'m scrutinizing the handling of various error types\342\200\224Errors, strings, and other objects\342\200\224to ensure that the `mountEmergencyPanel` function receives the most relevant and helpful data, including file names and stack traces. I\'m also considering edge cases, like the serialization of complex objects.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"node -e \'console.error(JSON.stringify({ reason: new Error(\\\\\\\"Test\\\\\\\"), file: \\\\\\\"Client Runtime (Vite)\\\\\\\" }))\'\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing JSON serialization of error\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test error JSON\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":421,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:42:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":2958,\"cache_read_tokens\":74291,\"output_tokens\":96,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598/task-420\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking task 420\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check task 420\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":424,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:42:17Z\",\"input_tokens\":2560,\"cache_read_tokens\":75101,\"output_tokens\":3714,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Unexpected Behavior**\\n\\nI\'ve just noticed a curious behavior when stringifying an object containing an Error instance in a specific environment. The `reason` property, when stringified, yields an empty object instead of preserving its details like the message or name. Now, I\'m questioning how to access the error details within the object, considering the context of reason and file in JSON stringification.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Root Cause**\\n\\nI\'m now digging