:\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:43:25Z\",\"input_tokens\":5162,\"cache_read_tokens\":86567,\"output_tokens\":658,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Error Handling**\\n\\nI\'m now investigating `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx`, specifically lines 39-78. I\'m focusing on `handleUnhandledRejection`, and how it might handle promise rejections within the application. I need to determine how the current implementation can be optimized.\\n\\n\\n**Reviewing Rejection Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the `handleUnhandledRejection` function more closely. It logs the rejection reason and file, and sets a global error state. However, I notice a key oversight: there\'s no check for ignorable rejections, such as those from Vite\'s HMR WebSocket. The error handling mechanism\'s scope should be refined.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/vite.config.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing vite.config.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View vite.config.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":443,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T09:43:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":3301,\"cache_read_tokens\":89665,\"output_tokens\":1569,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing HMR Configuration**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `vite.config.ts` file, specifically the HMR configuration, and how it behaves with environment constraints. I\'m investigating how the `process.env.DISABLE_HMR` variable impacts WebSocket behavior when HMR is disabled in AI Studio or within an iframe context by Vite\'s client.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Test Connection**\\n\\nI\'ve shifted my attention to the `testConnection()` function within `src/lib/firebase.ts`. It seems to execute immediately upon module im\\n<truncated 1643 bytes>\\nsed in `GlobalErrorHandler.tsx` and `ErrorBoundary.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the logic that determines the \'file\' property, aiming to understand why it\'s not correctly identi