    thinking: "**Analyzing Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve discovered some interesting data structures! Specifically, `Dashboard.tsx` is making queries to `users/${user.uid}/chats` and its sub-collection, `users/${user.uid}/chats/${chatDoc.id}/messages`. Also, I found that `LandingPage.tsx` describes \"Card 1\" which relates to a \"Shopfloor Agent,\" and includes features like alarm diagnostics and multimodal capabilities!\n\n\n**Investigating Agent Functionality**\n\nI\'ve uncovered some key details. I\'m now looking into `Dashboard.tsx` around line 700. It seems the \"Agent\" has camera access to snap controller screens. The app navigates to an \'agent\' route with the `openCamera` flag set. The absence of an Agent component earlier was confusing, but I found an `ErrorBoundary` that renders the Shopfloor Agent, with a \"smart_toy\" icon.\n\n\n**Examining Blank Screens**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on why the Shopfloor Agent page might be appearing blank. I\'ve noted a user comment in a screenshot stating precisely that. I\'m focusing on the component\'s state and rendering logic, especially concerning camera diagnostics and manual grounding slated for Milestone 3, and whether any dependencies are failing to load. The `px-margin` class in `index.css` is also under scrutiny.\n\n\n**Discovering Component Interactions**\n\nI\'ve just focused on `App.tsx` and uncovered a critical flow. The app now conditionally renders either `Dashboard` or `LandingPage` based on the user\'s logged-in state when the current tab is \'home\'. When the tab is \'agent\', the app always renders an error boundary containing the Shopfloor Agent, which seems to resolve the blank screen issue I was looking into. The `smart_toy` icon is rendered within a container, which is promising.\n\n\n**Uncovering Conditional Rendering**\n\nI\'ve just made a crucial discovery! It looks like if `user` is null, the app conditionally renders a fallback: If the current tab is \'home\' then we see `<LandingPage />`. If we\'re on the \'agent\' tab, or the user is logged in, an `ErrorBoundary` that renders the `ShopfloorAgent` is rendered. This explains why I previously thought the Agent component was missing.\n\n\n**Investigating CSS Conflicts**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a `div` element with the class `bg-surface-container-low`. I\'m trying to determine its visual representation. I\'m checking if the `@theme` definition for `--color-surface-container-low` is correctly influencing this element\'s background color, and comparing that with the `text-on-surface` color. I\'m also attempting to reconcile this with the user\'s feedback that the Shopfloor Agent page is still blank, and I am reviewing the prompt for clues on possible related causes, such as server-side imports.\n\n\n**Addressing Agent Page Issues**\n\nI\'ve just focused on addressing the blank agent page issue based on new instructions. I\'m implementing a `React.ErrorBoundary` around every route to display error messages. I\'m also adding `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers for consistent error display. I\'m now auditing all the dependencies to make sure no server-side imports are being used in client-side code, and that client-side components call `/api` routes instead. I am also checking the `package.json` file for correct dependency listing.\n\n\n"
