    thinking: "**Observing Code Behavior**\n\nI\'m now investigating the `/agent` route and examining `App.tsx`, specifically the `getTabFromPath` function. I\'m focusing on how it determines the current tab based on the URL path. This function seems central to routing logic.\n\n\n**Analyzing Navigation Logic**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to `Navigation.tsx`, and I\'m looking at lines 82-94, which deal with the \"Shopfloor Agent\" button. I am trying to determine how the current tab state interacts with the navigation components when the `user` object is populated. I am also investigating the state of navigation when a non-signed-in user opens the preview URL.\n\n\n**Investigating Rendering Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focused on the rendering that occurs when the preview URL is loaded and the user is *not* signed in. Specifically, I\'m watching `currentTab === \'agent\'` and what it dictates about the `App.tsx` component. The lack of a signed-in user seems to lead directly to a specific section of UI being rendered, which I\'m working to understand.\n\n\n**Confirming Rendered Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the rendering of the `/agent` route. Based on the code, it looks like only the `ErrorBoundary` is displayed. I\'m confirming whether this is the sole output. This seems to align with the requirements for error handling, but I want to verify there are no other active UI elements.\n\n\n**Verifying Agent Imports**\n\nI\'m now focused on the `/agent` route and am checking for any server-side imports within its dependencies. I\'m scrutinizing direct and indirect imports for any occurrences of `@google/genai`, `firebase-admin`, `fs`, `path`, or items from `/server`. This is to ensure no server-only code is erroneously included on the client-side. I\'ll need to remove those imports and call the `/api` route instead.\n\n**Analyzing Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now making sure all packages used by the `/agent` route, including `react-markdown`, are listed within `package.json` to prevent dependency issues. I\'m also ensuring that the chat list and messages correctly handle undefined or empty data, particularly for new users with no existing chats, avoiding potential crashes. Finally, the user reported that the `/agent` page is blank, so I\'m investigating why, which may be related to the prior two points.\n\n\n**Clarifying Feature Status**\n\nI\'m now investigating the user\'s expectation around the \"Shopfloor Agent\" feature. It seems possible the user anticipated a working implementation, or perhaps believed it was previously attempted and incomplete, or they may have thought it was scheduled in Milestone 3. I\'m focusing on `App.tsx` lines 74-95 to confirm the UI is a placeholder, as it shows a centered container with a robot icon.\n\n\n**Examining Blank Page Cause**\n\nI\'m now investigating why the \"Shopfloor Agent\" page remains blank, even with the placeholder UI. The user\'s feedback directs me to scrutinize the `px-margin` class within the code, considering that the `px-margin` class may not be working as intended. In particular, is `px-margin` actually translating to the expected `padding-left` and `padding-right`? The user\'s prompt strongly suggests a possible rendering issue that I need to resolve.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Rendering Error**\n\nI am now carefully reviewing `App.tsx` again. I\'ve noted the absence of a `ShopfloorAgent` component. My focus is now on the `AppContent` rendering logic when `currentTab` is set to \'agent\', specifically the dependencies and imported modules. I\'m investigating how the `useAuth` hook and its associated user state interacts with the component rendering, and that ties into what the user had said. This seems the most likely source of the blank page, I think.\n\n\n**Reviewing Automated Evaluation**\n\nI\'m now going back to the user\'s prompt, making sure I understand the automated evaluation requirements. I\'ll meticulously follow each directive: implementing `ErrorBoundary` for error display, adding `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers, removing server-side imports from the client, checking `package.json` for all dependencies, and ensuring robust handling of undefined data in chat lists. This is a complete audit, not feature addition, based on the prior analysis.\n\n\n**Investigating Route Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the rendering of the `/agent` route when a user *directly* navigates there. I\'m confirming that `window.location.pathname` correctly triggers the `currentTab` state to `\'agent\'`. Next, I\'m verifying the intended rendering in `AppContent`, specifically the intended conditional rendering. This will help determine why only the error boundary renders for the route.\n\n\n**Confirming Placeholder Display**\n\nI\'m now confirming the placeholder UI displays correctly when the `/agent` route is directly accessed, specifically, lines 74-95 in `App.tsx`. I\'m verifying the `currentTab` state correctly triggers the expected UI elements and that these elements are rendering as anticipated. This is to ensure the user sees the expected placeholder, as I\'m moving toward the automated evaluation next.\n\n\n\n**Confirming User Navigation**\n\nI\'m now investigating what happens when a non-signed-in user directly navigates to the `/agent` route. I am verifying that the `currentTab` state is correctly set to \'agent\' in `App.tsx` and, critically, that the appropriate UI elements are then rendered, as indicated in `AppContent`. It is critical to confirm the expected render sequence, especially with respect to the user authentication state, as the prompt provided shows that the nav bar should **not** show the button when the user is not signed in.\n\n\n**Verifying Click Navigation**\n\nI\'m now investigating what happens when the \"Shopfloor Agent\" button is clicked after the user is signed in. I\'m scrutinizing the `onNavigate` function, and I am cross-referencing this function with the current route to ensure that it displays the correct placeholder text, as intended. This also involves tracing the `navigationState` value, which should be passed from Dashboard. I am also checking for unexpected JavaScript errors or blank pages in this scenario.\n\n\n**Discovering File Absence**\n\nI\'ve just made a significant discovery: `ShopfloorAgent.tsx` is completely missing, while other components have hundreds of lines. This explains the blank page and is key to addressing the user\'s prompt. I\'m now focused on implementing the ErrorBoundary, error handlers, and dependency checks as directed, with the top priority now being the addition of the missing file.\n\n\n\n**Addressing Missing Component**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the `ShopfloorAgent.tsx` component, as its absence is the root cause of the blank page, I believe. I\'m prioritizing its creation and proper integration within the application structure. After that, I will methodically review server-side imports and dependencies within `/agent` before moving on to error handling and data validation, per the user\'s prompt.\n\n\n**Confirming Root Cause**\n\nThe absence of `ShopfloorAgent.tsx` is the critical piece; it explains the blank page and missing placeholder content. Now, I\'m integrating that component, and then the automated evaluations will begin. This discovery necessitates a re-evaluation of prior assumptions.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now going to add an ErrorBoundary to wrap every route as specified in the prompt. I\'m focusing on displaying error details within a red GlassPanel. I will then add `window.onerror` and `unhandledrejection` handlers to capture and display errors similarly.\n\n\n**Adding Missing Component**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `ShopfloorAgent.tsx` file, integrating it into the routing logic to resolve the blank page. This directly addresses the core issue identified, and this component will serve as the foundation for the `/agent` route. After this, I\'ll move on to the user-specified automated evaluations.\n\n\n**Clarifying Page Expectations**\n\nI\'m now revising my focus. The user *is* seeing the placeholder, but they expect the full Agent functionality on the `/agent` route. I\'ll need to confirm what functionality is missing on the Shopfloor Agent page (chat, diagnostics, and more), and then ensure `ShopfloorAgent.tsx` renders this expected content, not just the placeholder. This is key.\n\n\n\n"
