    thinking: "**Analyzing Firestore Rules**\n\nI\'ve been examining the Firestore rules, specifically how they handle access control for chat data. The rules currently grant read and write permissions on `/users/{uid}/chats/{chatId}` to the user with the corresponding `uid`, and then further restrict access to the `/messages/{msgId}` documents within those chats to the chat owner as well. My focus is on the `isOwner(uid)` function.\n\n\n**Addressing Client-Side Errors**\n\nI\'m now implementing the error boundary and global error handlers as specified. The plan is to ensure that all client-side errors, particularly within the `/agent` page, are caught and displayed in a red GlassPanel with relevant debugging information. I\'m carefully reviewing the imports to identify and remove any server-only code from client-side modules, refactoring them to use the `/api` route. Furthermore, I\'ll be validating package dependencies and ensuring the chat list handles empty data gracefully.\n\n\n**Investigating Shopfloor Issue**\n\nI\'m now investigating why the shopfloor agent page renders blank. I\'ve re-examined the code, specifically the `ErrorBoundary` within `App.tsx`, and the component itself. I\'ve now checked for any uncaught rejections or other client-side errors that might be affecting the render, particularly within the agent route.\n\n\n**Evaluating Shopfloor Agent Features**\n\nI\'m now outlining the expected features of the Shopfloor Agent. It should have a chat list, message display, text input for alarms, and image capture capabilities. I\'m thinking about integrating voice input simulation and manual page references too, focusing on the user experience. I\'m also planning to incorporate functionality for taking/uploading images of the CNC controller screen.\n\n\n**Refining Agent Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the Shopfloor Agent UI should behave with or without a signed-in user. The goal is a seamless experience. Even for a guest, I want to present a functional UI for testing alarm queries. I\'m making sure that if the user isn\'t signed in, navigating to `/agent` doesn\'t result in a blank page. Also, I\'m carefully reviewing the imports, ensuring that the client-side code is clean, avoiding server-side modules by making calls to `/api/agent`. And of course I\'m working to handle the empty state gracefully, especially when a user first logs in and has no chat history. I\'m also planning to use `react-markdown` to format response.\n\n\n"
