    combined_output {
      full: "{\"reply\":\"### 1. Alarm Identification & Severity\\n- **Alarm**: Fanuc Alarm 1004 SPINDLE MOTOR OVERHEAT\\n- **Severity**: Feed Hold / Spindle Inhibit (Interlocked)\\n\\n### 2. Root Cause Analysis\\nThe thermistor embedded in the Fanuc Alpha i series spindle motor windings detected temperature exceeding 140\302\260C. Common causes:\\n- Spindle chiller coolant flow failure or clogged suction filter.\\n- Prolonged heavy roughing cut above the rated 30-minute spindle power envelope.\\n- Rear cowl cooling fan impeller locked by chips or swarf build-up.\\n\\n### 3. Step-by-Step Recovery Procedure\\n1. Allow spindle to idle in neutral or coast to a complete stop for 15 minutes with main air purge active.\\n2. Check spindle oil/glycol chiller pressure gauge (nominal: 2.0 to 3.5 bar).\\n3. Inspect rear motor housing fan grill for chips or airflow restriction.\\n4. Press **[RESET]** on Fanuc MDI keypad once winding temperature normalizes (< 110\302\260C).\\n\\n### 4. OEM Manual Citations & References\\n- Fanuc Series 0i-MODEL F Maintenance Manual (B-64605EN/01) \302\2474.3 \\\"Spindle Alarm List\\\", p.112.\\n- Fanuc AC Spindle Motor \316\261i Series Parameter Manual (B-65280EN) \302\2477.2, p.84.\",\"citations\":[{\"documentName\":\"Fanuc Series 0i-MODEL F Maintenance Manual B-64605EN/01\",\"pageNumber\":112,\"snippet\":\"Spindle Alarm 1004 Thermal Sensor Interlock Protocol\"}],\"latencyMs\":15}"
    }
