  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Layout**\n\nI\'ve got the Stitch HTML for the Shopfloor Agent console screen! I\'m now laser-focused on meticulously matching the exact layout, components, classes, and tokens. It\'s crucial to reproduce the UI precisely as it is. It seems the user\'s instructions are very specific, and they expect me to match the exact elements!\n\n\n**Deconstructing the Structure**\n\nNow I\'m diving deep into the Stitch HTML\'s structure. I\'ve broken down the layout: header is handled, and I\'m analyzing the main content, including the `<main>` element\'s dimensions, the left sidebar (`<aside>`), and the top action/search components within the sidebar, ensuring I capture all the details precisely. I\'m focusing on the dimensions, flex properties, and class names to get a handle on the visual layout.\n\n\n**Detailing the Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of the interactive components within the main content stream. The \"New Session\" button\'s styling is under scrutiny; the `md shadow-primary-container/20` and hover effect are noted, along with the `add_box` icon. The search input\'s styling, including dimensions, rounded corners, and focus states, is being meticulously documented. The chat history stream, with its flex properties and scrolling behavior, is next.\n\n\n**Examining the Details**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the session stream, analyzing its inactive item states, which use specific classes like `bg-surface-container/50` and the hover effect. The empty state design is also fully noted, especially the use of the `chat_bubble_outline` icon and specific text content when `safeChats.length === 0`. I\'m also capturing all the specifics of the bottom Machine Profile Selector, and the grid layout details for those controllers.\n\n\n**Dissecting the Section**\n\nI\'m now deep into the right/main section\'s structure. I\'m focusing on the flexbox layout (`flex-1 flex flex-col h-full bg-surface-container-lowest min-w-0`), especially the telemetry/status header bar. I\'m noting the pulsing green/cyan dot animation for the controller/session title and the styling for both the session title and subtitle. This helps me understand the visual arrangement. The Engine Badge is next on the list.\n\n\n**Defining the State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the message history container\'s design and its different states. The engine badge details are completed; now, I\'m analyzing the telemetry/status header, including the diagnostic engine\'s precision display and action buttons, like \"Export Diagnostics PDF.\" The \'Clear Conversation\' button is also under scrutiny. Next, I\'m examining the message history container\'s layout using `flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4 sm:p-6 space-y-6`, and the design of session separators. I also need to focus on designing the \"no messages\" empty state to use real CNC alarms.\n\n\n**Constructing the Chat**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the nuances of the AI diagnostic agent\'s chat bubble and its components. I\'m focusing on the formatting specifics, like the `ml-auto` margin on the right, which is essential. The layout of the user\'s header, with their name and timestamp, including the photo thumbnail layout and styling, are fully incorporated into the design. The message bubble\'s style, including `bg-primary/10`, text color, rounded corners, and shadow, is precisely captured. I\'m also including all the details and styles for the AI agent response.\n\n\n**Rendering the Details**\n\nI\'m now focused on incorporating the rich UI elements for the chat messages. I\'m prioritizing the presentation of markdown content. Key items include styling root cause probability metrics, the Operational Protocol checklist with its numbered steps and icons, and verified citations with menu book and functions. I\'m also including all the design for the Diagnostic Reasoning Chain component. Finally, I\'m working on the design and styling for the sticky composer area.\n\n\n\n**Designing the Composer**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the composer area at the bottom of the chat. I\'ve designed the text input field, including its transparent background, text color, and placeholder style. I\'m also capturing the styling for the toolbar buttons, specifically the camera, voice agent with its pulsing dot animation, and file attachment buttons. Finally, I\'m noting the design of the send button, including its size, rounded shape, and shadow effect.\n\n\n**Incorporating the Status**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the lower status bar design and the hotkey strip. I\'ve designed the \"Send\" action, and am including the `arrow_upward` icon and the styling nuances. The under-bar Industrial Hotkey Status Strip design is next. I\'m noting the left-aligned shift/spacebar hotkeys, and the right-aligned active controller / material details. I am carefully adhering to the rule: \"Never show a machine status, telemetry value or operator name the app does not actually have.\" I\'m replacing all hardcoded values with appropriate real-data or designed empty states.\n\n\n**Validating the Data**\n\nI\'m now carefully checking the actual data available to the application to replace all hardcoded values with real data or empty states, especially for the lower status bar. The machine status and telemetry values are being assessed against the data source to ensure accurate and relevant information. I\'m focusing on the operator name, machine status, and telemetry data to prevent any misleading or incorrect displays. I\'m also ensuring that any hardcoded values are replaced with placeholders or appropriate empty states if data isn\'t available. I need to make sure I am following the rule!\n\n\n"
