  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Camera Control**\n\nI\'m thinking about how camera view resets are handled when `controlsRef` is involved. I\'m wondering if I\'ll need to update `Viewport3D` to expose the ref or manage view presets differently. I\'ve also found in `GCodeVerifier` that it has `setCameraView` method which can take `iso` or `top` as an argument.\n\n\n**Refining Camera Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining how `controlsRef` is used to adjust the camera, particularly its position and target. It seems I can streamline things by either relocating the preset logic into `Viewport3D` or utilizing the `cameraPosition` prop, which will simplify external control. The camera target might be handled in a similar way. This approach could eliminate the need for direct `controlsRef` exposure.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_7878"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Update Viewport3D to handle camera position changes\",\"EndLine\":47,\"Instruction\":\"Add a hook to update camera position when the prop changes.\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"import React, { Suspense, useEffect } from \'react\';\\nimport { Canvas, useThree } from \'@react-three/fiber\';\\nimport { OrbitControls, Grid, PerspectiveCamera, GizmoHelper, GizmoViewport } from \'@react-three/drei\';\\n\\nfunction CameraUpdater({ position }: { position: [number, number, number] }) {\\n  const { camera, controls } = useThree();\\n  \\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    camera.position.set(...position);\\n    if (controls) {\\n      (controls as any).target.set(0, 0, 0);\\n      (controls as any).update();\\n    }\\n  }, [position, camera, controls]);\\n  \\n  return null;\\n}\\n\\ninterface Viewport3DProps {\\n  children: React.ReactNode;\\n  cameraPosition?: [number, number, number];\\n  gridSize?: number;\\n  showGrid?: boolean;\\n  overlay?: React.ReactNode;\\n}\\n\\nexport function Viewport3D({ children, cameraPosition = [150, 150, 150], gridSize = 200, showGrid = true, overlay }: Viewport3DProps) {\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"w-full h-full min-h-[400px] bg-black/20 rounded-xl border border-outline-variant/20 overflow-hidden relative\\\">\\n      <Canvas shadows gl={{ antialias: true, alpha: true }}>\\n        <PerspectiveCamera makeDefault position={cameraPosition} fov={45} />\\n        <CameraUpdater position={cameraPosition} />\\n        \\n        {/* Shared Industrial Lighting */}\\n\",\"ReplacementContent_explanation\":\"Added a CameraUpdater component that uses useThree to access the camera and controls, and updates the camera position whenever the cameraPosition prop changes.\",\"StartLine\":1,\"TargetContent\":\"import React, { Suspense } from \'react\';\\nimport { Canvas } from \'@react-three/fiber\';\\nimport { OrbitControls, Grid, PerspectiveCamera, GizmoHelper, GizmoViewport } from \'@react-three/drei\';\\n\\ninterface Viewport3DProps {\\n  children: React.ReactNode;\\n  cameraPosition?: [number, number, number];\\n  gridSize?: number;\\n  showGrid?: boolean;\\n  overlay?: React.ReactNode;\\n}\\n\\nexport function Viewport3D({ children, cameraPosition = [150, 150, 150], gridSize = 200, showGrid = true, overlay }: Viewport3DProps) {\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"w-full h-full min-h-[400px] bg-black/20 rounded-xl border border-outline-variant/20 overflow-hidden relative\\\">\\n      <Canvas shadows gl={{ antialias: true, alpha: true }}>\\n        <PerspectiveCamera makeDefault position={cameraPosition} fov={45} />\\n        \\n        {/* Shared Industrial Lighting */}\\n\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/ui/Viewport3D.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating Viewport3D with CameraUpdater\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update Viewport3D 4\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
