  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully consolidated the design system by creating and reusing shared building blocks in `src/components/ui/`. Every screen has been refactored to use these components, ensuring consistency across the application without changing their appearance or behavior.\n\n### Shared UI Components Created/Reused:\n*   **AppShell**: Provides the layout wrapper with top navigation and industrial footer.\n*   **PageHeader**: Standardized header with eyebrow labels, titles, and context-aware actions.\n*   **Card**: Multi-purpose container with optional semantic top-border accents.\n*   **GlassPanel**: Used for high-fidelity overlays and error boundary UI.\n*   **StatChip**: Compact data readout for telemetry and KPIs, now supporting clicks.\n*   **Badge**: Monospace labels with semantic color fills (12%) and borders (40%).\n*   **Button System**: Standardized `ButtonPrimary`, `ButtonSecondary`, `ButtonDanger`, and `IconButton` (48x48).\n*   **Tabs**: Segmented controls for switching process modes and filters.\n*   **SectionHeader**: Subtle dividers with icons and record counts.\n*   **Feedback**: Shared `EmptyState`, `Skeleton` loading states, and `ProgressBar` with multi-zone support.\n*   **Drawer**: Consistent slide-out panel for diagnostics and AI explanations.\n*   **CodeEditor**: Enhanced G-code editor with syntax highlighting, line numbers, and gutter click events.\n*   **Viewport3D**: Shared Three.js environment with industrial lighting, grid, and HTML overlay support.\n\n### Files Refactored:\n*   `src/components/Dashboard.tsx`\n*   `src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx`\n*   `src/components/ShopfloorAgent.tsx`\n*   `src/components/GCodeVerifier.tsx`\n*   `src/components/KnowledgeBase.tsx`\n\nAll hard-coded hex values in the UI have been replaced with Tailwind theme tokens. Syntax and nesting issues identified during the consolidation have been resolved, and the applet builds successfully."
    thinking: "**Consolidating UI Components**\n\nI\'ve just finished the refactoring and consolidation of the design system. The `Dashboard`, `CuttingCalculator`, `ShopfloorAgent`, `GCodeVerifier`, and `KnowledgeBase` now all use shared UI components from `src/components/ui`. This should make future updates and maintenance much easier.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully consolidated the design system by creating and reusing shared building blocks in `src/components/ui/`. Every screen has been refactored to use these components, ensuring consistency across the application without changing their appearance or behavior.\n\n### Shared UI Components Created/Reused:\n*   **AppShell**: Provides the layout wrapper with top navigation and industrial footer.\n*   **PageHeader**: Standardized header with eyebrow labels, titles, and context-aware actions.\n*   **Card**: Multi-purpose container with optional semantic top-border accents.\n*   **GlassPanel**: Used for high-fidelity overlays and error boundary UI.\n*   **StatChip**: Compact data readout for telemetry and KPIs, now supporting clicks.\n*   **Badge**: Monospace labels with semantic color fills (12%) and borders (40%).\n*   **Button System**: Standardized `ButtonPrimary`, `ButtonSecondary`, `ButtonDanger`, and `IconButton` (48x48).\n*   **Tabs**: Segmented controls for switching process modes and filters.\n*   **SectionHeader**: Subtle dividers with icons and record counts.\n*   **Feedback**: Shared `EmptyState`, `Skeleton` loading states, and `ProgressBar` with multi-zone support.\n*   **Drawer**: Consistent slide-out panel for diagnostics and AI explanations.\n*   **CodeEditor**: Enhanced G-code editor with syntax highlighting, line numbers, and gutter click events.\n*   **Viewport3D**: Shared Three.js environment with industrial lighting, grid, and HTML overlay support.\n\n### Files Refactored:\n*   `src/components/Dashboard.tsx`\n*   `src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx`\n*   `src/components/ShopfloorAgent.tsx`\n*   `src/components/GCodeVerifier.tsx`\n*   `src/components/KnowledgeBase.tsx`\n\nAll hard-coded hex values in the UI have been replaced with Tailwind theme tokens. Syntax and nesting issues identified during the consolidation have been resolved, and the applet builds successfully."
    thinking_duration {
