  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed Milestone 6: the Academy Crash Lab. This feature provides a safe environment for operators to simulate G-code programs on a Training VMC, analyze kinematic failures, and learn through guided instruction.\n\n### Files Created:\n*   `src/engine/crash.ts`: Contains the fixed geometry (Table, Vise, Stock), collision detection logic, and mission data for the Academy scenarios.\n*   `src/components/academy/MissionMap.tsx`: The mission selection screen showing XP progress, level status (Trainee/Operator/Setter), badge shelf, and a vertical certification path.\n*   `src/components/academy/MissionView.tsx`: The primary simulation workspace featuring the 3D viewport, code editor, and collision analysis system.\n*   `src/components/academy/MachineScene.tsx`: A specialized Three.js environment that renders the machine components and animate the toolpath with hit-detection highlighting.\n*   `src/components/academy/InstructorPanel.tsx`: A side panel providing AI-powered feedback, hint tiers (with XP penalties), and quick-query chips.\n\n### Files Updated:\n*   `src/App.tsx`: Integrated Academy routing logic to switch between the mission map and specific mission views.\n*   `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`: Added badge tracking to the user profile interface.\n*   `src/components/Navigation.tsx`: Verified and ensured \"Academy\" is present in both desktop and mobile navigation menus.\n\n### 4-Step Manual Test:\n1.  **Enter Academy**: Click **Academy** in the top nav. Verify you see the \"Crash Lab\" header, your initial Trainee status (0 XP), and the mission path where \"The Missing Offset\" is marked as **ACTIVE**.\n2.  **Run Simulation (Crash)**: Click **Begin Diagnostic Session** on Mission 1. Press **Run Simulation**. Observe the tool slamming into the vise. Verify the screen shakes, a metallic crash sound plays, and the **Damage Assessment** card appears showing a \342\202\2713,40,000 INR repair cost.\n3.  **Fix and Re-verify**: In the CodeEditor, insert `G43 H01 Z50.` on a new line before the first plunge (Line 6). Click **Rewind and fix**. Run the simulation again. Verify the tool now clears the fixture and completes the path, triggering the **Mission Accomplished!** card.\n4.  **Verify Progression**: Click **Back to Map**. Verify Mission 1 now has a green \"PASSED\" border, your XP bar has increased, and the **Offset Master** badge is now highlighted in the top shelf. Mission 2 should now be unlocked and **ACTIVE**."
    thinking: "**Confirming Project Milestone**\n\nI\'ve just finished the Academy Crash Lab \342\200\223 Milestone 6. I\'ve created all the necessary files: `crash.ts` for the engine, and `MissionMap.tsx`, `MissionView.tsx`, and `MachineScene.tsx` for the components. This phase feels complete!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed Milestone 6: the Academy Crash Lab. This feature provides a safe environment for operators to simulate G-code programs on a Training VMC, analyze kinematic failures, and learn through guided instruction.\n\n### Files Created:\n*   `src/engine/crash.ts`: Contains the fixed geometry (Table, Vise, Stock), collision detection logic, and mission data for the Academy scenarios.\n*   `src/components/academy/MissionMap.tsx`: The mission selection screen showing XP progress, level status (Trainee/Operator/Setter), badge shelf, and a vertical certification path.\n*   `src/components/academy/MissionView.tsx`: The primary simulation workspace featuring the 3D viewport, code editor, and collision analysis system.\n*   `src/components/academy/MachineScene.tsx`: A specialized Three.js environment that renders the machine components and animate the toolpath with hit-detection highlighting.\n*   `src/components/academy/InstructorPanel.tsx`: A side panel providing AI-powered feedback, hint tiers (with XP penalties), and quick-query chips.\n\n### Files Updated:\n*   `src/App.tsx`: Integrated Academy routing logic to switch between the mission map and specific mission views.\n*   `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`: Added badge tracking to the user profile interface.\n*   `src/components/Navigation.tsx`: Verified and ensured \"Academy\" is present in both desktop and mobile navigation menus.\n\n### 4-Step Manual Test:\n1.  **Enter Academy**: Click **Academy** in the top nav. Verify you see the \"Crash Lab\" header, your initial Trainee status (0 XP), and the mission path where \"The Missing Offset\" is marked as **ACTIVE**.\n2.  **Run Simulation (Crash)**: Click **Begin Diagnostic Session** on Mission 1. Press **Run Simulation**. Observe the tool slamming into the vise. Verify the screen shakes, a metallic crash sound plays, and the **Damage Assessment** card appears showing a \342\202\2713,40,000 INR repair cost.\n3.  **Fix and Re-verify**: In the CodeEditor, insert `G43 H01 Z50.` on a new line before the first plunge (Line 6). Click **Rewind and fix**. Run the simulation again. Verify the tool now clears the fixture and completes the path, triggering the **Mission Accomplished!** card.\n4.  **Verify Progression**: Click **Back to Map**. Verify Mission 1 now has a green \"PASSED\" border, your XP bar has increased, and the **Offset Master** badge is now highlighted in the top shelf. Mission 2 should now be unlocked and **ACTIVE**."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 563082619
    }
