  planner_response {
    response: "The errors and warnings in your log are related to three specific areas: **Firestore permissions**, **Three.js version updates**, and **Vite environment constraints**. Here is a breakdown of what they mean:\n\n### 1. Firestore Permission Warning\n*   **Message:** `[AuthProvider] Firestore client doc init notice: FirebaseError: Missing or insufficient permissions.`\n*   **Cause:** This occurs when the application attempts to read a user-specific document (like your profile or chat history) before the Firebase Authentication state has fully finished loading. \n*   **Impact:** This is generally harmless. The app is designed to re-sync automatically once the Auth SDK confirms your user ID. Your `firestore.rules` are configured to keep data private to the owner, so until you are verified, the database correctly blocks the request.\n\n### 2. Three.js Deprecation Warnings\n*   **Messages:** \n    *   `THREE.Clock: This module has been deprecated. Please use THREE.Timer instead.`\n    *   `THREE.WebGLShadowMap: PCFSoftShadowMap has been removed. Using PCFShadowMap instead.`\n*   **Cause:** You are using a very recent version of Three.js (`0.186.1`). These warnings appear because internal components or third-party libraries (like `@react-three/fiber`) are still using APIs that Three.js recently renamed or phased out.\n*   **Impact:** None. Three.js is automatically falling back to the correct modern replacements (`THREE.Timer` and `PCFShadowMap`) to ensure the 3D scenes still render correctly.\n\n### 3. Vite WebSocket Errors\n*   **Messages:** `[vite] failed to connect to websocket` and `WebSocket closed without opened.`\n*   **Cause:** These are environment-specific errors related to **Hot Module Replacement (HMR)**. The AI Studio preview environment uses internal networking that often restricts the WebSockets needed for \"instant\" code updates.\n*   **Impact:** These do not affect the functionality of your application for end-users. They only mean that as a developer, you might need to manually refresh the preview occasionally rather than relying on automatic updates.\n\n**Summary:** Your application is healthy. These logs are primarily technical \"noise\" related to library version transitions and the specific constraints of the cloud development environment."
    modified_response: "The errors and warnings in your log are related to three specific areas: **Firestore permissions**, **Three.js version updates**, and **Vite environment constraints**. Here is a breakdown of what they mean:\n\n### 1. Firestore Permission Warning\n*   **Message:** `[AuthProvider] Firestore client doc init notice: FirebaseError: Missing or insufficient permissions.`\n*   **Cause:** This occurs when the application attempts to read a user-specific document (like your profile or chat history) before the Firebase Authentication state has fully finished loading. \n*   **Impact:** This is generally harmless. The app is designed to re-sync automatically once the Auth SDK confirms your user ID. Your `firestore.rules` are configured to keep data private to the owner, so until you are verified, the database correctly blocks the request.\n\n### 2. Three.js Deprecation Warnings\n*   **Messages:** \n    *   `THREE.Clock: This module has been deprecated. Please use THREE.Timer instead.`\n    *   `THREE.WebGLShadowMap: PCFSoftShadowMap has been removed. Using PCFShadowMap instead.`\n*   **Cause:** You are using a very recent version of Three.js (`0.186.1`). These warnings appear because internal components or third-party libraries (like `@react-three/fiber`) are still using APIs that Three.js recently renamed or phased out.\n*   **Impact:** None. Three.js is automatically falling back to the correct modern replacements (`THREE.Timer` and `PCFShadowMap`) to ensure the 3D scenes still render correctly.\n\n### 3. Vite WebSocket Errors\n*   **Messages:** `[vite] failed to connect to websocket` and `WebSocket closed without opened.`\n*   **Cause:** These are environment-specific errors related to **Hot Module Replacement (HMR)**. The AI Studio preview environment uses internal networking that often restricts the WebSockets needed for \"instant\" code updates.\n*   **Impact:** These do not affect the functionality of your application for end-users. They only mean that as a developer, you might need to manually refresh the preview occasionally rather than relying on automatic updates.\n\n**Summary:** Your application is healthy. These logs are primarily technical \"noise\" related to library version transitions and the specific constraints of the cloud development environment."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\355\002\n\352\002\001i\024}\023\024\332iLvr\b\346\312\205\354\247\311\027\270\204.\022\202%J\036\177&\314b\t\023WUZ\313\255\335\247\313\213e\360J\327\221\275\267\323\024M\t0D \353\332\316\202\354u\232\267\203U\247\273\255\001\336\316\300\234\004M&\231\362\026\027\0319\235\t\366>E\004\200\217\353\336\212\354F<\220(\263\366Y\r:A\034|\275b\'9/\273Jk\372\227\v\331\261\235\240&\357\356\303OKl\250\303k\005@P\321\207}Y\201R\bf\331\v\001Q\330\374\2406\315\310\277\244\236\366TG\v\235L.\257\241h\2658\210\367W\2338\272\376Y\311,\221\026\306\021!\326\262\207\177\313\246\322\037\252\213\201Zb\2004~\261J\'\320\207}\304-\327\006\002\261(e\3335\362\002\226\301m.\221rO#6\3505U\335\357\022\346\023\306\370\255\225)\036\316\350,@/xU\206l6$\225\a\024\'\3041\242\303\177\222Z`\305\315/>3r\341\020\275_\276\351\036\347\237\313\265\367\330\376\211\247\257\003\364(\017\n\355-\212\272\v\350\211\342A\221;r\225N\306^\t\322\250\034\'>\'\033\305\215\302\364o\253\200\307\232t\321\re\335\227\025\233\317\354\316\b\fk\247fD\335\246]1\n\263/\034\367b\233d\030D\260\357\233O\320\301\306"
