  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Backgrounds and Colors**\n\nI\'ve noticed the `MachineScene` isn\'t setting a background, but the `Viewport3D` is using `bg-black/20`. I\'m considering what changes are required to the `Grid` if I alter the `Viewport3D` to utilize a lighter background. This should also affect the user\'s selector: `div#root:nth-of-type(`, among others. I\'m investigating how these elements interact.\n\n\n**Revisiting Element Interactions**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how the elements interact, particularly focusing on the `AppShell`. The selector `div#root` leads to the `AppShell` root div. Within the `AppShell`, the `main` tag and the `MissionView` root div within it are crucial. I need to understand how these relate to the background and color settings. The `MissionView` seems to be the critical wrapper element.\n\n\n**Examining MissionView Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `MissionView`\'s structure. It\'s the primary wrapper, and its root div has a specific layout: a header, then a grid. This grid has three columns: left for the brief and editor, center for the 3D scene and controls, and a right column, though I\'m not seeing it now. The `Viewport3D` is nested within the center column, and I need to ensure the background changes flow correctly through this hierarchy, particularly since the viewport is in a relative div.\n\n\n**Adjusting Viewport Background**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `Viewport3D`\'s root `div`. The selector I\'ve identified, nested within the grid hierarchy, is the target for background adjustments. I\'m leaning toward changing the background to a lighter color to enhance object visibility. Considering Tailwind\'s theming, I\'ll probably go with `bg-white` or `bg-slate-100`. This necessitates a corresponding update to the `Grid` and potentially the `Gizmo` color as well, if they have a hardcoded dark color scheme.\n\n\n\n**Refining Background and Grid Colors**\n\nI\'ve decided to update the `Viewport3D` background to `bg-zinc-200` for better visibility and a cleaner aesthetic. I\'m now modifying the `Grid` component within `Viewport3D.tsx` to use neutral colors. I\'m aiming for an industrial light background with this color choice, and I\'ll need to confirm that this doesn\'t conflict with any other color settings. The goal is to improve the overall 3D simulation experience\'s visual appeal, aligning it with the user\'s apparent preference for lighter tones.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1233825"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Allow custom styling and background for Viewport3D\",\"EndLine\":25,\"Instruction\":\"Add className prop to Viewport3DProps.\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"interface Viewport3DProps {\\n  children: React.ReactNode;\\n  cameraPosition?: [number, number, number];\\n  gridSize?: number;\\n  showGrid?: boolean;\\n  overlay?: React.ReactNode;\\n  className?: string;\\n}\\n\",\"ReplacementContent_explanation\":\"Added \'className?: string;\' to the Viewport3DProps interface to allow passing custom Tailwind classes to the root element.\",\"StartLine\":19,\"TargetContent\":\"interface Viewport3DProps {\\n  children: React.ReactNode;\\n  cameraPosition?: [number, number, number];\\n  gridSize?: number;\\n  showGrid?: boolean;\\n  overlay?: React.ReactNode;\\n}\\n\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/ui/Viewport3D.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Adding className prop to Viewport3DProps\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update Viewport3D props 2\"}"
