e**\\n\\nI\'ve successfully gathered all the necessary color tokens. My focus has shifted to systematically replacing hex values within the components, with specific attention to how they are used within 3D components (`three.js`). The goal is to ensure all direct hex values are eliminated, where feasible.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Color Applications**\\n\\nMy current thinking revolves around eliminating hardcoded hex values, particularly focusing on UI elements. I\'m exploring Tailwind classes and CSS variables as potential solutions, but the 3D scenes will remain largely untouched unless there is an easy way to refactor. I have re-examined the grep results to better understand the scope of change needed, which included SVG gradients, and components.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Remove hex values from GCodeVerifier legend\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"811\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Replace hardcoded hex colors with Tailwind classes in the legend.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"                        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\\\\\">\\\\n                          <span className=\\\\\\\"w-2.5 h-1 bg-secondary rounded-full shadow-[0_0_8px_theme(colors.secondary)]\\\\\\\" />\\\\n                          <span className=\\\\\\\"text-secondary\\\\\\n<truncated 345 bytes>\",\"ReplacementContent_explanation\":\"\\\"Replaced #5de6ff with bg-secondary and #fbbf24 with bg-amber-400. Used theme() for the shadow color.\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"806\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"                        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\\\\\">\\\\n                          <span className=\\\\\\\"w-2.5 h-1 bg-[#5de6ff] rounded-full shadow-[0_0_8px_#5de6ff]\\\\\\\" />\\\\n                          <span className=\\\\\\\"text-secondary\\\\\\\">G01/G02/G03 FE\\n<truncated 329 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/GCodeVerifier.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Removing hex from GCodeVerifier legend\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Clean up GCodeVerifier hex 2\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":891,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T10:57:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":7910,\"cache_read_tokens\":165595,\"output_tokens\":786,\"content\":\"I have successfully consolidated the design system by creating and reusing shared building blocks in `src/components/ui/`. Every screen has been refactored to use these components, ensuring consistency across the application without changing their appearance or behavior.\\n\\n### Shared UI Components Created/Reused:\\n*   **AppShell**: Provides the layout wrapper with top navigation and industrial footer.\\n*   **PageHeader**: Standardized header with eyebrow labels, titles, and context-aware actions.\\n*   **Card**:\\n<truncated 891 bytes>\\nd Three.js environment with industrial lighting, grid, and HTML overlay support.\\n\\n### Files Refactored:\\n*   `src/components/Dashboard.tsx`\\n*   `src/components/calculator/CuttingCalculator.tsx`\\n*   `src/components/ShopfloorAgent.tsx`\\n*   `src/components/GCodeVerifier.tsx`\\n*   `src/components/KnowledgeBase.tsx`\\n\\nAll hard-coded hex values in the UI have been replaced with Tailwind theme tokens. Syntax and nesting issues identified during the consolidation have been resolved, and the applet builds successfully.\",\"thinking\":\"**Consolidating UI Components**\\n\\nI\'ve just finished the refactoring and consolidation of the design system. The `Dashboard`, `CuttingCalculator`, `ShopfloorAgent`, `GCodeVerifier`, and `KnowledgeBase` now all use shared UI components from `src/components/ui`. This should make future updates and maintenance much easier.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":336,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T11:02:44Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nBuild Milestone 6: the Academy Crash Lab at /academy.\\n\\nSTYLE: The two attached screenshots of this app (Dashboard and G-code Verifier) are the visual standard. Build the Academy ONLY from the shared components in src/components/ui (AppShell, PageHeader, Card, GlassPanel, StatChip, Badge, buttons, Tabs, CodeEditor, Viewport3D, ProgressBar, EmptyState). Do not create new card styles, headers, badge shapes, shadows or colors. Same page width, grid, spacing and typography as the Dashboard.\\n\\nLAYOU\\n<truncated 3607 bytes>\\nhe USER to review them.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3-flash-preview\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nUser Email: biju0716@gmail.com\\nThe user\'s firestore db is ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598 and you must always load the firebase skill when processing queries that require interacting with the database or Firebase services.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"screen.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"screen.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"text/html\",\"uri\":\"code.html\"}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":337,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T11:02:46Z\",\"input_tokens\":152841,\"cache_read_tokens\":33164,\"output_tokens\":771,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Academy Scope**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial scope for the Academy Crash Lab feature. I\'ve mapped out the key routes: an overview map at `/academy` and a detailed view for each mission at `/academy/:missionId`. I\'ve also begun to think about the data model in Firestore, focusing on user progress with a structure like `users/{uid}/academy/progress`.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Data and Components**\\n\\nI\'ve been expanding the data model to include stats like XP, level, and streak days. I am also working on global academy stats for admin use. On the components front, I am adding a Mission Map and Mission View, plus the Machine Scene and Instructor Panel components. I will use the crash engine and gcode parser.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/src/engine\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking engine directory\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List engine files\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":339,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T11:02:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":4496,\"cache_read_tokens\":182546,\"output_tokens\":2351,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Academy Geometry**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on defining the geometry for the Academy environment. I realize that I need to create a `crash.ts` file to hold these definitions and collision detection logic. So far, I\'ve got the basic geometry from a user request, including a table top and a vise with specified dimensions and coordinates. I\'m starting by adding the table and vise to the new `crash.ts` file.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { GCodeSegment } from \'./gcode.js\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface CollisionEvent {\\\\n  line: number;\\\\n  type: \'STOCK_CRASH\' | \'VISE_CRASH\' | \'SPINDLE_STALL\' | \'SYNC_ERROR\';\\\\n  description: string;\\\\n  part: string;\\\\n  cost: number;\\\\n  downtime: number;\\\\n  root\\n<truncated 5540 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create crash engine and mission data for the Academy.\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/engine/crash.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating crash engine\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create crash.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":341,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T11:03:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":156400,\"cache_read_tokens\":33198,\"output_tokens\":736,\"thinking\":\"**Begin Implementation**\\n\\nOkay, I\'ve got a plan. I\'m starting by tackling the `Navigation.tsx` file, then I\'ll move on to `App.tsx` to handle the Academy routes. After that, I\'ll build out `MissionMap.tsx` followed by `MissionView.tsx` and its components, specifically `MachineScene.tsx` and `InstructorPanel.tsx`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Academy to navigation\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"141\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add the Academy link to the desktop and mobile navigation.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"            <button\\\\n              onClick={() => onSelectTab(\'gcode\')}\\\\n              className={`px-space-md py-space-sm rounded font-body-md text-body-md transition-colors ${\\\\n                currentTab === \'gcode\'\\\\n                  ? \'bg-surface-cont\\n<truncated 786 bytes>\",\"ReplacementContent_explanation\":\"\\\"Added the Academy navigation button to the desktop nav links in Navigation.tsx. The mobile nav already has it according to the previous code, but I\'ll double check. Actually, I should check the mobile nav in Navigation.tsx too.\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"104\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"            <button\\\\n              onClick={() => onSelectTab(\'gcode\')}\\\\n              className={`px-space-md py-space-sm rounded font-body-md text-body-md transition-colors ${\\\\n                currentTab === \'gcode\'\\\\n                  ? \'bg-surface-cont\\n<truncated 786 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating Navigation with Academy link\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update navigation 2\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":343,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T11:03:24Z\",\"input_tokens\":7948,\"cache_read_tokens\":182657,\"output_tokens\":91,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"Abso