file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Increase Academy simulation canvas size for maximum visibility\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"275\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add h-[500px] to the wrapper div in MissionView to allow the Viewport3D to expand.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"          <div className={`relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden h-[500px] transition-transform duration-75 ${cameraShake ? \'translate-x-1\' : \'\'}`}>\\\\n             <Viewport3D \\\\n              cameraPosition={[120, 100, 120]}\\\\n              showGrid={false}\\\\n\\n<truncated 67 bytes>\",\"ReplacementContent_explanation\":\"\\\"Added \'h-[500px]\' to the container div in MissionView.tsx. Since Viewport3D uses \'h-full\', this allows the canvas to expand to the maximum size of this defined container.\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"265\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"          <div className={`relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden transition-transform duration-75 ${cameraShake ? \'translate-x-1\' : \'\'}`}>\\\\n             <Viewport3D \\\\n              cameraPosition={[120, 100, 120]}\\\\n              showGrid={false}\\\\n          \\n<truncated 57 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/academy/MissionView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Increasing simulation canvas size\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update MissionView canvas size 2\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":338,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T15:40:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":11328,\"cache_read_tokens\":227432,\"output_tokens\":496,\"thinking\":\"**Expanding Canvas Thoughts**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on expanding the canvas to fit the dimensions of its parent `div`. The `div` already has `w-full h-full min-h-[400px]` applied, so I\'m looking at how the `Canvas` element itself interacts within those constraints in `Viewport3D.tsx`. I believe the solution lies within that file.\\n\\n\\n**Verifying Canvas Size**\\n\\nI\'ve increased the parent height in `MissionView.tsx` and now I\'m explicitly setting the R3F `Canvas` component\'s style to `width: 100%, height: 100%` within `Viewport3D.tsx` to ensure it\'s filling available space. I\'m double-checking the container `div` and verifying that the `Canvas` element should expand based on its size. I\'m ruling out other potential blockers like the overlay. I\'ll just keep double checking it one more time.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Verifying changes after canvas size update\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet 8\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":340,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T15:40:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":3532,\"cache_read_tokens\":236033,\"output_tokens\":95,\"content\":\"The Academy simulation viewport has been expanded to fill the maximum available layout area in the mission view. By increasing the container height to **500px**, the 3D environment now provides a significantly larger workspace for inspecting tool movements and kinematic details.\"}\n{\"step_index\":335,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T15:44:53Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nthe 3d objects colors needs to be more realistic. the 3d objects include the machine table, component, fixture and tools. need to change the colors accordingly so that it looks real in rendering.\\nApply style changes to the selected element(s).\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\\nCSS selector 1: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > main:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(2) > div:nth-of-type(2) > div:nth-of-type(2) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-ty\\n<truncated 296 bytes>\\nd App URL: https://ais-pre-2liicweyktuh4vuop7oowi-456692856985.asia-east1.run.app\\nUser Email: biju0716@gmail.com\\nThe user\'s firestore db is ai-studio-cnccopilot-3768fe9c-394b-4869-a3b5-72b028948598 and you must always load the firebase skill when processing queries that require interacting with the database or Firebase services.\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The user has focused on specific UI elements. You MUST adhere strictly to the targeting and styling rules defined in the \'focus-mode\' skill.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":336,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T15:44:53Z\",\"input_tokens\":8617,\"cache_read_tokens\":227694,\"output_tokens\":2044,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Scene Elements**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on improving the realism of the 3D objects within the Academy simulation. Specifically, I\'m examining `src/components/academy/MachineScene.tsx` to understand the machine table\'s current color and material properties as a starting point. The goal is to identify how these can be adjusted to enhance the visual fidelity of the simulation for all of the key components.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Simulation Textures**\\n\\nI\'ve been making good progress refining the Academy simulation\'s visual elements. My next move is to integrate more plausible hex codes and material characteristics within `MachineScene.tsx`. I\'m starting by updating the machine table to a cast iron look with `#2c2e33`. I\'m going to follow that by adjusting the vise and stock, and then finally applying similar alterations to the end mill and tool holder.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Apply realistic industrial colors and materials to Academy 3D objects\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"112\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update colors and material properties for table, vise, stock, and tools to match real-world industrial appearances.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"      {/* Machine Table (Cast Iron) */}\\\\n      <Box \\\\n        args={[200, 5, 200]} \\\\n        position={[40, ACADEMY_GEOMETRY.table.z - 2.5, -25]}\\\\n      >\\\\n        <meshStandardMaterial \\\\n          color={crashObject === \'TABLE\' && isCrashing ? \'#ff0000\' \\n<truncated 1537 bytes>\",\"ReplacementContent_explanation\":\"\\\"Updated the 3D object properties in MachineScene.tsx for realistic industrial rendering:\\\\n- Table: Changed to a deep matte grey (#1a1c1e) representing cast iron.\\\\n- Vise: Updated to \'Kurt Blue\' (#2b3e50) with standard tool-steel roughness.\\\\n- Stock: Switc\\n<truncated 328 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"64\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"      {/* Machine Table */}\\\\n      <Box \\\\n        args={[200, 5, 200]} \\\\n        position={[40, ACADEMY_GEOMETRY.table.z - 2.5, -25]}\\\\n      >\\\\n        <meshStandardMaterial color={crashObject === \'TABLE\' && isCrashing ? \'#ff0000\' : \'#181c21\'} />\\\\n      <\\n<truncated 1277 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/academy/MachineScene.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Applying realistic colors to 3D objects\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update 3D realism 2\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}"
    included_step_index_start: 83
