    used_fallback_summary: true
    user_requests: "Build Milestone 6: the Academy Crash Lab at /academy.\n\nSTYLE: The two attached screenshots of this app (Dashboard and G-code Verifier) are the visual standard. Build the Academy ONLY from the shared components in src/components/ui (AppShell, PageHeader, Card, GlassPanel, StatChip, Badge, buttons, Tabs, CodeEditor, Viewport3D, ProgressBar, EmptyState). Do not create new card styles, headers, badge shapes, shadows or colors. Same page width, grid, spacing and typography as the Dashboard.\n\nLAYOUT: Use the attached academy_crash_lab_2/code.html only as a layout and element reference: where the mission path, scenario brief, 3D scene, collision banner, damage card, code editor, instructor panel, hint tiers and quick question chips sit. Ignore its CSS classes, its header and footer, and ALL of its text and numbers.\n\nSCREENS\n1. /academy (Mission map): PageHeader with eyebrow \"ACADEMY\", title \"Crash Lab\", caption \"Crash the machine here. Never on the shop floor.\" Right side: level Badge (Trainee 0-199 XP, Operator 200-399, Setter 400+), XP ProgressBar to the next level, streak StatChip, and a badge shelf (Offset Master, Safe Approach, Tap Whisperer, Safe Starter; locked ones greyed). Below: a vertical mission path of 4 Cards with node states: completed (green top border, check icon, XP earned), current (orange top border, subtle pulse), locked (grey, lock icon). A mission unlocks when the previous one is passed. Admins also see a stats Card row on top: learners, missions completed, average crashes before pass, most common crash type (GET /api/academy/stats).\n2. /academy/:missionId (Mission view): desktop 3 columns (left: scenario brief Card + CodeEditor with the broken program; center: Viewport3D machine scene with Run simulation, Reset and speed 0.5x / 1x / 2x controls; right: Instructor GlassPanel). Mobile order: brief, 3D, editor, instructor.\n3. Machine scene: fixed geometry from src/engine/crash.ts (table top Z -60, vise X -10..90 Y -15..65 Z -60..-10, stock X 0..80 Y 0..50 Z -10..0), cylinder spindle and end mill following the toolpath. Label \"Training VMC (simulated)\". Live readouts in JetBrains Mono under the scene: current line, X Y Z, spindle state, feed, all from the simulation.\n4. On a crash: stop at the event position, flash the hit object red, 0.4 s camera shake, short metallic noise burst generated with the Web Audio API, red collision banner \"COLLISION DETECTED: {crash type in words}\", flag the faulty line in the CodeEditor, and show the damage Card: part, repair cost in INR, downtime days, root cause in one sentence, and the line \"Illustrative training cost. Real costs vary by machine.\" Button \"Rewind and fix\".\n5. Instructor panel: avatar, chat thread, hint tier list \"Hint 1 of 3\" with lock icons on unrevealed tiers and \"-20% XP\" on each paid tier (first hint is not free; every hint reduces XP by 20%), quick question chips (\"Why did it crash?\", \"What does this code do?\", \"How do I check this on a real machine?\"), text input and a hold-to-talk mic button. Calls POST /api/instructor as specified.\n6. Pass: when the edited program gives zero crash events and zero CRITICAL findings, play the safe run in green, show \"+{xp} XP\" and the badge unlock, and call POST /api/academy/complete (the server re-verifies with the engines and writes progress). Button \"Next mission\".\n\nMISSIONS: use exactly the 4 missions from the original spec (The Missing Offset, Rapid Into Stock, Stripped Tap, Dead Spindle), with T01 and H01, one fault per program. Do not use the mission text from the HTML.\n\nDATA: all XP, level, streak, badges, attempts and stats come from Firestore. New users see 0 XP, Trainee, no badges, mission 1 unlocked. Never show invented progress, machine names or operator IDs.\n\nAdd \"Academy\" to the top nav and mobile bottom tabs using the same nav component. List the files created and changed, then give me a 4-step manual test."
    user_requests: "what are these errors and warnings in this log?"
