  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the Academy Crash Lab and addressed the 3D simulation visibility and realism requests.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n- **Academy Mission Hub**: A vertical certification path at `/academy` tracking XP, levels (Trainee, Operator, Setter), and badges (Offset Master, etc.).\n- **High-Fidelity Simulation**: Improved 3D materials for the machine table (cast iron), vise (industrial blue), and stock (aluminum). The background is now light (Slate-100) with optimized lighting for clear visibility.\n- **Crash Mechanics**: Added Web Audio API metallic crash sounds, camera shake, and a detailed \"Damage Assessment\" card displaying illustrative repair costs in INR and downtime.\n- **AI Instructor**: Integrated Gemini-powered chat in the instructor panel with a tiered hint system (first hint costs 20% XP) and quick-question chips.\n- **Full-Stack Integration**: Real-time progress syncing via Firestore and server-side verification for mission completions.\n\n### Files Created/Modified:\n- `src/components/academy/MissionMap.tsx` & `MissionView.tsx` (Core Academy logic)\n- `src/components/academy/MachineScene.tsx` (Realistic 3D rendering)\n- `src/components/ui/Viewport3D.tsx` (Lighter scene background/lighting)\n- `server/routes/academy.ts` (Stats and AI Instructor API)\n- `server.ts` & `server/geminiClient.ts` (Backend mounting and AI helper)\n- `src/App.tsx` & `Navigation.tsx` (Routing and Nav updates)\n\n### 4-Step Manual Test:\n1. **Explore the Map**: Go to the **Academy** tab. Verify you see \"The Missing Offset\" as the unlocked mission and your progress starts at 0 XP (Trainee).\n2. **Trigger a Collision**: Start the first mission and click **Run Simulation**. Watch the toolpath crash; you should hear a metallic noise, see the camera shake, and a red \"Collision Detected\" banner and Damage Card appear.\n3. **Get AI Guidance**: In the **Instructor Panel**, click \"Why did it crash?\". The AI will analyze your specific failure and provide a hint about the missing `G43` height offset.\n4. **Pass the Mission**: Correct the code by adding `G43 H01` to the approach line and run the simulation again. Verify you receive the \"Mission Accomplished\" card, gain XP, and unlock the next mission."
    thinking: "**Confirming Project Deliverables**\n\nI\'ve got the project\'s state fully documented now, and everything appears to be in order. I\'m ready to move forward. I will now present the list of updated or created files, along with the detailed four-step manual test plan. I\'m ready for the next stage.\n\n\n**Detailing Technical Implementation**\n\nI\'ve completed the core implementation of the academy features, focusing on the mission path, simulation logic, and AI instructor interaction. I\'ve also implemented the 3D scene, defined collision logic, and integrated the Antigravity SDK for instructor chat. Backend routes for stats and mission completion are in place. Now I\'m preparing to test it.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the Academy Crash Lab and addressed the 3D simulation visibility and realism requests.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n- **Academy Mission Hub**: A vertical certification path at `/academy` tracking XP, levels (Trainee, Operator, Setter), and badges (Offset Master, etc.).\n- **High-Fidelity Simulation**: Improved 3D materials for the machine table (cast iron), vise (industrial blue), and stock (aluminum). The background is now light (Slate-100) with optimized lighting for clear visibility.\n- **Crash Mechanics**: Added Web Audio API metallic crash sounds, camera shake, and a detailed \"Damage Assessment\" card displaying illustrative repair costs in INR and downtime.\n- **AI Instructor**: Integrated Gemini-powered chat in the instructor panel with a tiered hint system (first hint costs 20% XP) and quick-question chips.\n- **Full-Stack Integration**: Real-time progress syncing via Firestore and server-side verification for mission completions.\n\n### Files Created/Modified:\n- `src/components/academy/MissionMap.tsx` & `MissionView.tsx` (Core Academy logic)\n- `src/components/academy/MachineScene.tsx` (Realistic 3D rendering)\n- `src/components/ui/Viewport3D.tsx` (Lighter scene background/lighting)\n- `server/routes/academy.ts` (Stats and AI Instructor API)\n- `server.ts` & `server/geminiClient.ts` (Backend mounting and AI helper)\n- `src/App.tsx` & `Navigation.tsx` (Routing and Nav updates)\n\n### 4-Step Manual Test:\n1. **Explore the Map**: Go to the **Academy** tab. Verify you see \"The Missing Offset\" as the unlocked mission and your progress starts at 0 XP (Trainee).\n2. **Trigger a Collision**: Start the first mission and click **Run Simulation**. Watch the toolpath crash; you should hear a metallic noise, see the camera shake, and a red \"Collision Detected\" banner and Damage Card appear.\n3. **Get AI Guidance**: In the **Instructor Panel**, click \"Why did it crash?\". The AI will analyze your specific failure and provide a hint about the missing `G43` height offset.\n4. **Pass the Mission**: Correct the code by adding `G43 H01` to the approach line and run the simulation again. Verify you receive the \"Mission Accomplished\" card, gain XP, and unlock the next mission."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 316035060
